&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deal Pricing is a dedicated global function that provides deal pricing expertise, financial insights and deal support for negotiated users to Stripe’s global Go-to-Market teams. We work to ensure deals create economic value for Stripe by establishing the deal commercial framework for a scaling sales organization, actively supporting large and strategic deals and providing pricing insights and feedback to sales, finance and product leaders. Deal Pricing frequently works with cross-functional business partners across Operations, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy and Product and there is constant collaboration with Deal Pricing colleagues across all regions. AMER Deal Pricing covers teams in the United States, Canada and Latin America and are located in Stripe offices and remote locations across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be instrumental in providing thought leadership to regional sales teams and senior executives and continuing to develop our framework, approach and associated processes in order to achieve mutually beneficial deals with our sold Users while mitigating risk to Stripe. In addition to providing key financial insights and recommendations to business partners and Stripe leadership, you will have a chance to stretch beyond the boundaries of finance through business case development and commercial negotiations with all types of customers across the full suite of Stripe’s financial and payment products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key financial and strategic thought partner to specific AMER Go-to-Market sales teams and their leadership in both pricing deals at scale and pricing strategic deals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for defining and implementing our pricing and margin guidance and identifying levers for financial uplift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and refine new frameworks to evaluate a deal’s attractiveness to Stripe, ensuring alignment between these frameworks, the company’s long range plan and mutually agreeable outcomes with cross-functional business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up to date pricing benchmarks and contribute to team analytical design and production efforts, using this data to enhance our pricing philosophy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3+ years of experience in finance or deal pricing at a company, or experience within investment banking or, management consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build collaborative working relationships with business partners through a combination of influencing and awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment by driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent financial modeling, verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience in the payments or technology sector&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting findings and recommendations to senior leadership, preferably to sales of go-to-market business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL and Tableau or a willingness to learn is a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8007358:
&lt;p&gt;Flow Traders is a leading global proprietary trading firm and a principal liquidity provider and market maker across ETFs, bonds, FX &amp;amp; Digital Assets. We are looking for a Global Head of Operations and Middle Office to join our Amsterdam office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Head of Operations is responsible for the strategic direction, global coordination, and continuous optimization of the operational infrastructure across all geographies. This includes full accountability for post-trade execution, trade support, process automation whilst maintaining Operational Risk Management and regulatory compliance. The role is pivotal in enabling scalability, efficiency, and control in support of Flow Traders&#39; trading ambitions. This is a unique opportunity to join a leading proprietary trading firm with an entrepreneurial and innovative culture at the heart of its business. We value quick-witted, creative minds and challenge them to make full use of their capacities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the firm’s global operations strategy in line with trading and business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise the board and senior leadership on operational decisions and business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare operations for market expansion and increased business activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multi-regional operations and middle-office teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent processes, systems, controls, and standards across locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish KPIs, quality controls, and accountability frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and monitor operational risk management and regulatory control frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee controls across the trade lifecycle, settlement, reconciliation, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead automation, digital transformation, data, and AI initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Technology and Product teams to improve post-trade infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce operational workload, improve efficiency, and strengthen service quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the main operations contact for Trading, Risk, Compliance, Finance, and Technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with clearing banks, custodians, prime brokers, and other vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide accurate management information and operational insights to the board&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, anticipate, and mitigate operational risks across multiple jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This is a full-time, on-site position based in Amsterdam.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will need to succeed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in financial services, with at least 5 years in leadership roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in trading operations and mid-office functions across multiple asset classes (e.g., equities, derivatives, FX, DA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in managing distributed teams across different time zones and cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with regulatory frameworks in Europe, North America, and Asia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of technology platforms, data flows, and automation solutions in a trading context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, decisive, and execution-oriented with a global mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and influencing skills; able to interact at all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Business, Finance, Engineering, or related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we offer&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flow Traders, we create the conditions for hard‑working, high‑performing people to do their best work. From a thorough onboarding and ongoing access to Flow Academy, to latest technology and a collaborative, non‑hierarchical culture, we give you the tools, ownership, and support to move fast and drive outcomes. We keep a close‑knit, small‑company feel while offering competitive salary, annual discretionary profit share, and comprehensive benefits,&amp;nbsp;so talent can grow here, and stay here.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;See our benefits below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flow Academy and opportunities to attend domain-related conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily catered lunch, great coffee, and a fully stocked kitchen and snack bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house Bar and Lounge with arcade, table tennis, billiards, and game consoles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company boat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house gym and sessions with our nutritionist or personal trainer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bi-weekly massages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company trip and a variety of events throughout the year, such as the New Years Event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global rotations across our offices worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

8007639:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation practice (within Professional Services) works with our most strategic users. The team serves as a transformation &amp;amp; growth partner to our most strategic and frontier users — helping them achieve complex business goals and enabling greater certainty in their outcomes when they invest with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will establish and lead a new sub-practice within Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation: &lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Monetization Advisory&lt;/strong&gt;. As Stripe&#39;s users grow in scale and ambition — launching new revenue channels, embedding payments &amp;amp; finance into platforms, pricing AI-powered products, and expanding into new geographies — they need a trusted, opinionated advisor in their corner to advice them with prescriptive point of view on revenue acceleration, GTM, pricing &amp;amp; monetization strategy. This role &amp;amp; practice will span both traditional fiat rails and the emerging crypto and stablecoin infrastructure across Stripe, Bridge, Privy, and Tempo — positioning it as one of the most forward-looking advisory capabilities in financial services today. You will run workshops for c-suite &amp;amp; senior management around this capabilities and support the team globally on including this workstream in their respective enterprise transformation workshop&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe works with the world&#39;s most ambitious platforms, marketplaces, and enterprises building the next generation of financial products — and the scale of what they&#39;re building creates an extraordinary opportunity to go deeper. As these users expand into new markets, launch AI-powered products, and layer embedded finance onto their core offering, the topics that unlock their next phase of growth become increasingly strategic: &lt;em&gt;design a monetization strategy that captures full value, price competitively across geographies without eroding margin, structure go-to-market motions and sales enablement for white-labelled financial products, and translate Stripe&#39;s capabilities into durable revenue streams for their business.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists to meet that moment — bringing a more prescriptive, hands-on advisory approach to the users where commercial model design is the primary lever for growth, and ensuring that Stripe&#39;s most strategic relationships are supported not just with best-in-class infrastructure, but with the monetization and revenue strategy expertise to make the most of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a strategy &amp;amp; transformation advisor for growth &amp;amp; monetization, you will own and build Growth &amp;amp; Monetization sub-practice end-to-end. You will be the globally recognised expert in this space working directly with and advising some of Stripe’s strategic users and in process enabling your teammates to do the same. Your work will sit at the intersection of commercial strategy, product economics, and payments infrastructure — and will span five core advisory domains:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. New Revenue Channel Growth &amp;amp; Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with platforms, marketplaces, and enterprise users at the earliest stages of their thinking to identify, validate, and prioritise new revenue channels. This includes embedded finance, monetization of distribution, bundled value-added services, and adjacency expansion. You will bring structure, data, and commercial rigour to decisions that are often made on instinct.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. AI Product Pricing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SaaS companies are racing to launch AI-powered features and products — and most are flying blind on pricing. You will develop a repeatable advisory model that helps users design pricing architectures for AI products: usage-based vs. seat-based vs. outcome-based models, packaging strategy, willingness-to-pay research, and competitive positioning. This is a fast-moving space and an area where Stripe can take a distinctive, opinionated stance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Platform &amp;amp; Marketplace monetization on Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe powers some of the world&#39;s most sophisticated platforms and marketplaces. You will help existing and prospective platform users unlock the full commercial potential of their Stripe integration — including but not limited to buy-rate modelling, revenue share to interchange-plus transitions, merchant segmentation and tiered pricing, and product-to-commercial-model fit across Connect, Terminal, Money management products (Capital, Treasury, Issuing), and Billing. You will draw on and extend the existing monetization Strategy capability &amp;amp; offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Geographic Expansion &amp;amp; Payments monetization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As users expand into new markets, their payments economics change significantly. You will advise on how monetization models need to evolve across card mix, scheme fee structures, local regulation, and competitive pricing dynamics in new geographies. The output will be clear market-entry pricing strategies, multi-year margin models, and phased expansion plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Embedded Finance &amp;amp; Digital Assets monetization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As platforms increasingly embed financial products into their core offerings, monetization strategy becomes one of the most complex and consequential decisions they face. This advisory domain covers the full spectrum of Money as a Service (MaaS) products: how platforms, marketplaces, and vertical SaaS companies can design and price the financial products they embed — including &lt;strong&gt;payments acceptance, card issuing programmes, treasury and money-movement capabilities, working capital and lending facilities, and stablecoin or crypto-native infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; You will help users build monetization models that capture the full economic value of their embedded financial stack, advising on revenue share structures, margin stacks, product bundling, and the commercial trade-offs between depth and scale across each financial product category. This domain spans both traditional fiat rails and emerging digital asset infrastructure, and is relevant wherever a platform is moving beyond pure SaaS economics into financial services revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sub-practice build and leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, launch, and own the Growth &amp;amp; Monetization advisory sub-practice within Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the methodology, offering structure, engagement models, and pricing for advisory workstreams across all five domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a library of reusable frameworks, financial models, benchmarks, and pitch materials that the global S&amp;amp;T team can deploy independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish Stripe as having a distinctive, opinionated position on growth and monetization in our target verticals and segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report sub-practice performance: pipeline contribution, closed Professional Services revenue, NPS, and user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client advisory and pre-sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the lead advisor and subject matter expert in strategic pre-sales engagements, bringing structured monetization thinking to the earliest commercial conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery workshops, pricing strategy sessions, and monetization blueprint engagements with C-suite and senior leadership at strategic users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of Professional Services workshops, engagements &amp;amp; deals in this domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives and Solutions Engineers to position the capability as a differentiator in competitive deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable the Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation team globally to incorporate Growth &amp;amp; Monetization thinking into their existing client engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training programmes, playbooks, and certification paths for the ProServ team to deliver foundational Growth &amp;amp; Monetization advisory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an internal escalation point and thought partner for complex monetization questions arising from any strategy &amp;amp; transformation engagement worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product and market intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep knowledge of pricing and monetization trends across SaaS, platforms, AI, and industries including but not limited to fintech — and bring those insights back into Stripe&#39;s GTM motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Stripe&#39;s Product and Engineering teams to inform product roadmap decisions based on user monetization needs and gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce thought leadership content — frameworks, benchmarks, reports — that reinforces Stripe&#39;s credibility in this space externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross Functional collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Stripe&#39;s internal product, finance, and go-to-market leadership to help explore our own monetization model around these services — advising on how we can package this engagement to improve margin and revenue outcomes for our business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an internal thought partner to senior Stripe leadership on how the monetization model should evolve as the company&#39;s product surface expands across fiat rails, stablecoins, and new financial infrastructure categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in management consulting, product/commercial leadership role, with a demonstrable track record in pricing strategy, monetization design, or growth advisory with payments experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in: SaaS pricing and packaging, platform/marketplace monetization, payments economics, AI product commercialisation, and geographic market expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building a practice, capability, or offering from scratch — including the methodology, commercial model, and go-to-market collateral — within a consulting, technology, or financial services firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modelling skills and the ability to build rigorous buy-rate, revenue share, and unit economics models that hold up in C-suite conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and executive presence — able to present complex monetization strategy clearly and persuasively to senior business leaders, and to build credibility quickly in pre-sales environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in pre-sales advisory or solution-selling in a technology or professional services context, with a track record of closing sizable engagements and developing Statements of Work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to enable and upskill colleagues — not just to do the work yourself, but to build the capability across a distributed global team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising high-growth SaaS or fintech companies on pricing strategy for new product lines, including AI-powered features or usage-based models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with payments infrastructure — including Stripe Connect, interchange economics, scheme fee structures, and embedded finance — and how these translate into platform commercial models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in working across multiple geographies, with an understanding of how payments pricing, regulation, and competitive dynamics vary by market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A network and reputation in the monetization or pricing strategy community, with published thought leadership a distinct advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a high-growth internet or software company, particularly one that navigated a significant monetization or business model transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with crypto, stablecoin, or digital assets economics — including an understanding of how platforms like Bridge, Privy, and Tempo are reshaping financial infrastructure monetization and what commercial models are emerging in this space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to build something genuinely new inside one of the most important technology companies of our generation. Stripe&#39;s users are at inflection points — launching new products, entering new markets, monetising new capabilities — and they are hungry for expert guidance they can trust. The person who builds this practice will have a direct impact on the trajectory of hundreds of companies, the revenues of Stripe&#39;s Professional Services business, and the confidence of our sales teams globally. If you have strong opinions about how businesses should monetise and grow — and the drive to turn those opinions into a global offering — this role was built for you.&lt;/p&gt;

8007692:
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Stripe · Professional Services · Global Transformation team · Dublin or London&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Professional Services (ProServ) team helps businesses around the world design, implement, and optimise their Stripe integrations. As we scale our global delivery capability, we are building a structured portfolio of service offerings that define the scope, methodology, resourcing, and commercial terms of how we engage with our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Product Manager (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Services)&lt;/strong&gt; to own the portfolio of offerings end-to-end. The role sits at the intersection of services strategy, commercial design, and delivery operations. You will be the person who determines whether our offerings are well-designed, effectively sold, and profitably delivered and you will take action to refine the portfolio as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional Product Manager role, but it demands the same rigour. Your &quot;product&quot; is the service itself: its scope, its pricing, its methodology, and its performance. You will work closely with Sales, Delivery, Finance, and Stripe&#39;s Product organisation to ensure that every offering in our portfolio is fit for purpose and continuously improving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the offering portfolio for Professional Services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and govern ProServ’s offering portfolio including scope, hours, pricing, and resource plans for each offering. Our portfolio includes offerings designed&amp;nbsp; for all user segments from start-ups to enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full offering lifecycle: design, build, launch, iterate, and deprecate offerings based on market need, delivery performance, and product roadmap changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the portfolio stays current as Stripe launches new products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement a governance framework for the portfolio of offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive offering performance analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track the offering KPIs: attach rate, average scope deviation, planned vs. actual burn rate, gross margin per offering, and customer satisfaction&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular performance reviews and present findings to ProServ leadership with clear recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refine and Improve Offering Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse delivery burn data to identify offerings that are systematically over- or under-scoped, and propose refinements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structured retrospectives with Delivery Leads after engagement close to capture insights and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the structured feedback loop between Delivery (what is hard to deliver), Sales (what is hard to sell), and Finance (what is margin-accretive), synthesising those inputs into offering design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of Professional Services or consulting delivery experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience shaping or owning a service offering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial literacy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Management training or experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to apply product thinking (hypothesis, prototype, measure, iterate) to service design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Certinia and/or Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to partner and SI ecosystem dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8009442:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ripple, we empower organizations on their path to strategic treasury through our leading SaaS treasury and risk management solutions. As a Professional Services Consultant, you will be the linchpin between our innovative technology and the financial aspirations of our esteemed clients. Your role transcends mere implementation; you will be a digital architect and a trusted advisor, carefully customizing solutions that enhance treasury operations to higher levels of efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discovery &amp;amp; Strategy: Lead deep-dive discovery sessions to uncover client pain points, workflows, and technical requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution Architecture: Design and document the &quot;To-Be&quot; state, determining the optimal configuration of Ripple Treasury’s suite to meet specific client goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted Advisory: Act as a subject matter expert, guiding clients through treasury best practices and helping them modernize legacy processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementation &amp;amp; Configuration: Take a hands-on approach to configuring the platform, ensuring the technical setup aligns perfectly with the strategic vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enablement &amp;amp; Training: Facilitate high-impact training sessions that empower users and ensure the client realizes the maximum ROI from our solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with Sales, Product, and Engineering teams to provide client feedback and influence the future of our product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in client-facing solution consulting or software implementations, particularly in ERP or SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultative approach, challenging the status quo and leading clients toward improved outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical competence, with an understanding of complex software ecosystems and data flow between treasury systems, banks, and ERPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication skills, translating technical jargon into accessible financial concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in treasury domains such as cash management, payments, risk, or hedge accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial proficiency, with experience in Corporate Treasury, Accounting, or Finance, and comfort discussing cash flow, debt, and financial risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both English and German is required, with other languages considered a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
