8066903:
&lt;p&gt;Flow Traders is looking for a driven event specialist to join our dynamic Communications team in our Amsterdam office. You will be instrumental in transforming events from decentralized, ad-hoc activities into a structured, consistent, and measurable communications and marketing channel, that strengthens brand visibility, deepens relationships, and directly supports our strategic business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to join a leading proprietary trading firm with an entrepreneurial and innovative culture at the heart of its business.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;We value quick-witted, creative minds and challenge them to make full use of their capacities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end planning and execution of corporate events, including conferences, client events, and internal engagement activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Centralize and standardize event planning processes across the firm, ensuring consistent quality and execution at every touchpoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for stakeholder management, aligning event objectives with business priorities and keeping all parties informed throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage budgets, suppliers, venues, and external agencies, ensuring cost-effectiveness without compromising on quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transform the firm&#39;s approach to events into a structured and measurable communications channel that supports brand visibility and relationship building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee multiple events simultaneously, balancing competing priorities and deadlines with confidence and precision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement best practices and frameworks that elevate the overall standard of event delivery across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply your creativity to deliver professional and engaging events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you need to succeed&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;University Degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years proven experience in event management, event marketing, or a related field. A strong portfolio of corporate events is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstratable track record of planning and executing high-quality events from concept through to delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with the ability to juggle multiple projects and stakeholders at the same time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, ensuring nothing falls through the cracks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing budgets, suppliers, venues, and external agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, solution-oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication skills, with the ability to craft clear briefs, proposals, and event-related content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we offer&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flow Traders, we create the conditions for hard‑working, high‑performing people to do their best work. From a thorough onboarding and ongoing access to Flow Academy, to latest technology and a collaborative, non‑hierarchical culture, we give you the tools, ownership, and support to move fast and drive outcomes. We keep a close‑knit, small‑company feel while offering competitive salary, annual discretionary profit share, and comprehensive benefits,&amp;nbsp;so talent can grow here, and stay here.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;See our benefits below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flow Academy and opportunities to attend domain-related conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily catered lunch, great coffee, and a fully stocked kitchen and snack bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house Bar and Lounge with arcade, table tennis, billiards, and game consoles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company boat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house gym and sessions with our nutritionist or personal trainer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bi-weekly massages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company trip and a variety of events throughout the year, such as the New Years Event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global rotations across our offices worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

8067604:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team + Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Proactive Capabilities team builds novel tooling and leverages state-of-the-art automation to eliminate business impact from threat actors! &lt;/strong&gt;Our mission is to close critical attack paths before they can be exploited and to mitigate active threats with speed and precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer on the Proactive Capabilities team , you will design, build, and scale engineering tools that empower Security Engineers, eliminate operational toil, and expand security coverage across Robinhood. This is a creative, high-impact role where you will identify high-priority security challenges, evaluate buy-vs-build opportunities, and turn one-off solutions into robust, company-wide security capabilities!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Bellevue, WA and Menlo Park, CA offices, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale flexible, reliable security tooling and services that improve visibility and expand scan coverage across Robinhood and its entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy AI agents and security automation workflows to drive and prevent proactive security risk discovery and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Security Engineering and Product Engineering teams to establish secure-by-default software design patterns and paved paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design and system reviews alongside Proactive Security initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation to maintain high availability and reliability for critical team security services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven software engineering fundamentals and practical system design skills, with experience building scalable, reliable microservices and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Go or Python (with a preference for Go).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and deploying services in cloud environments (AWS preferred, or GCP equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid foundational knowledge of containerization and Kubernetes concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong security domain context, including an understanding of the attacker lifecycle, application security concepts, and hands-on experience developing or integrating security tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic, curious, and collaborative mindset with the ability to navigate ambiguous problem spaces and independently identify high-value engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI, LLMs, or agentic frameworks to solve complex security problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in developer productivity, security automation, or toil-reduction initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Application Security (AppSec) experience, bug bounty participation, or CTF competition experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Kubernetes experience or a track record of building enterprise security platforms at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$166,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$147,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8068565:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startups, Existing Business team is a consultative sales team that is responsible for the growth and retention of the largest and fastest-growing Startup customers at Stripe. As an Account Executive, you&#39;ll identify new opportunities for our clients to get the most out of Stripe by understanding our clients&#39; needs, execute scaled sales strategies to close upsells and renewals with existing Stripe customers, and drive end-to-end campaigns to increase adoption of Stripe products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own contract renewals and lead commercial negotiations to increase and retain existing customer revenue and Stripe market share&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement full sales cycle strategies for driving product adoption, net new product sales, and client retention at scale among existing Stripe customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex client needs and work across product, sales, risk, and operations teams to improve our product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close for startups and small and medium businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate your own leads through cold calling, blitzing, research, networking, and driving your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make every potential Stripe user happy with every interaction, regardless of deal size&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and understand users&#39; pain points to propose Stripe solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure that internal teams are set up for users&#39; success by coordinating with other Stripe teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a client-facing sales role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical ecosystems and build great relationships with technical customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive and close upsell opportunities for additional Stripe products in long-term, consultative engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving ability to manage complex pricing and cost considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing projects with input from cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working well with a wide range of stakeholders, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and motivation to operate in an ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a sales and customer-facing role at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Excel and SQL, or a willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8068744:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Money Management team helps businesses move, store, and manage money at global scale. Our product suite&amp;nbsp; spanning Connect, Payouts, Issuing, Treasury, Capital, and FX gives companies the infrastructure to build programmable fund flows, embed financial services into their platforms, and offer financing to their customers and sellers. In ANZ, we work with some of the region&#39;s most sophisticated enterprises and fastest-growing technology companies, helping them solve complex fund flow problems and unlock new financial product opportunities. It&#39;s an exciting time to be part of the team: Money Management is one of Stripe&#39;s highest-growth product areas and ANZ is a key market in that expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As one of Stripe&#39;s first Money Management Account Executives in ANZ, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to build something from the ground up. This is an IC role for someone who is energised by being an early hire&amp;nbsp; defining how we sell the full Money Management suite in the region, establishing relationships with some of ASEAN&#39;s most ambitious companies, and creating the playbook as you go. You&#39;ll develop pipeline across multiple high-growth markets and serve as a trusted partner to companies tackling complex financial infrastructure challenges from global platforms routing payouts to local gig workers, to fintechs embedding card issuance and treasury into their products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full commercial cycle for Stripe&#39;s Money Management products&amp;nbsp; including Payouts, Issuing, Treasury, Capital, and FX&amp;nbsp; across a portfolio of enterprise and strategic accounts in ANZ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory plan for ANZ, generating pipeline through outbound prospecting, expansion within existing accounts, and collaboration with Stripe&#39;s partner ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive-level commercial conversations with CEOs, CFOs, CTOs, and product leaders&amp;nbsp; positioning Stripe&#39;s Money Management suite as strategic infrastructure for their business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate complex, multi-product deal structures in close collaboration with Solutions Architecture, Legal, Compliance, and Product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong, long-term relationships with key decision-makers across ANZ&#39;s enterprise and high-growth technology sectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop expertise in the ANZ competitive landscape across each Money Management product to win in competitive situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize customer feedback and market intelligence and bring insights to Stripe&#39;s product, marketing, and regional GTM teams to influence roadmap and go-to-market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of enterprise sales or business development experience at a technology or fintech company, with a consistent track record of top performance on strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience selling payments, financial infrastructure, or fintech products to large enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles and lead commercial negotiations, including bespoke deal structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to understand technical requirements and communicate complex solutions clearly to both technical and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who can build and manage a pipeline independently and operate effectively in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset with experience in fast moving startups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling across the ANZ market with strong knowledge of the local enterprise technology and fintech landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with money management products such as payouts infrastructure, card issuing, embedded banking, or business lending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with or selling to platforms, marketplaces, fintechs, or enterprise technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with Solutions Engineers, Legal, and Compliance on technically sophisticated or regulated deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the Australian and New Zealand regulatory environment for payments and financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8068746:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Product Sales, Money Management team helps businesses move, store, convert, spend and manage money at global scale. Our product suite&amp;nbsp; spanning Connect, Payouts, Issuing, Treasury, Capital, and FX gives companies the infrastructure to build programmable fund flows, embed financial services into their platforms, and offer financing to their customers and sellers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In ASEAN, the opportunity is enormous: a diverse, fast-growing region with complex cross-border payment challenges, rapidly expanding digital economies, and businesses hungry for the financial infrastructure to scale. We&#39;re building out the team in Singapore to capture that opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As one of Stripe&#39;s first Money Management Account Executives in ASEAN, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to build something from the ground up. This is an IC role for someone who is energised by being an early hire&amp;nbsp; defining how we sell the full Money management suite in the region, establishing relationships with some of ASEAN&#39;s most ambitious companies, and creating the playbook as you go. You&#39;ll develop pipeline across multiple high-growth markets and serve as a trusted partner to companies tackling complex financial infrastructure challenges from global platforms routing payouts to local gig workers, to fintechs embedding card issuance and treasury into their products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full commercial cycle for Stripe&#39;s Money Management products including Payouts, Issuing, Treasury, Capital, and FX across a book of enterprise and strategic accounts in ASEAN&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory plan across multiple ASEAN markets, developing pipeline through outbound prospecting, cross-sell motions, and Stripe&#39;s partner ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive-level commercial conversations with CEOs, CFOs, CTOs, and product leaders&amp;nbsp; acting as a strategic partner on their money management and embedded finance strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate complex, multi-product deals across diverse regulatory and market environments, collaborating with Solutions Architecture, Legal, Compliance, and product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with key decision-makers at target accounts, driving both new business acquisition and expansion within existing accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep knowledge of the ASEAN competitive landscape across each Money Management product to win in contested deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize customer and market feedback and bring insights back to Stripe&#39;s product, marketing, and GTM teams to shape regional strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of enterprise sales or business development experience at a technology or fintech company, with a consistent track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience selling payments, financial infrastructure, or fintech products to large enterprise or platform customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles and lead commercial negotiations, including bespoke deal structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a multi-country territory and navigating deals across varying regulatory and business environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to understand technical requirements and communicate complex solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or willing to relocate to Singapore; comfortable with regional travel across ASEAN markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset with experience in fast moving startups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in Mandarin and English, as the role involves working with users within the Greater China region and other ASEAN markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling across multiple ASEAN markets with knowledge of the regional payments and fintech landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with money management products such as payouts infrastructure, card issuing, embedded banking, or business lending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with or selling to platforms, marketplaces, fintechs, or digital economy companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with Solutions Engineers, Legal, and Compliance on technically sophisticated deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional Southeast Asian language skills are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8068918:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that we are unable to consider applications from candidates based in France, Italy, or Germany for this role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consensys is the leading blockchain and web3 software company. Founded by Joe Lubin, CEO of Consensys and Co-Founder of Ethereum in 2014, Consensys has been at the forefront of innovation, pioneering technological developments within the web3 ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The financial system is being rebuilt on open, programmable infrastructure, and Consensys is helping power that transition. From MetaMask, the platform trusted by tens of millions of users worldwide, to Linea, the only 100% proven zkEVM rollup and an emerging home for institutional ETH capital, Consensys builds products and infrastructure that enable users, developers, and institutions to participate in the next generation of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to unlock the collaborative power of communities by making the decentralized web universally easy to access, use, and build on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Consensys means working with a fully remote, globally distributed team of technologists, designers, cryptographers, product thinkers, and researchers who are building the next layer of the internet. You&#39;ll be exposed to new ideas, emerging technologies, and complex challenges that push you to stay at the top of your game while helping scale products and infrastructure used by tens of millions of users and thousands of developers across the web3 ecosystem. You&#39;ll join a network of builders that reaches the edge of our ecosystem. Consensys alumni have moved on to become tech entrepreneurs, CEOs, and team leads at tech companies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager to join our Growth Marketing team. In this role, you’ll be responsible for setting the strategy and executing on lifecycle campaigns across all Consensys products. You’ll look for opportunities to ensure we are bringing a level of personalization in our communication to our users such that every touch point is driving value for our customers and the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has a proven track record of taking projects from start to finish with deep experience leveraging customer data to inform their strategy. You’ve developed multiple lifecycle programs at scale, have conducted hundreds of A/B tests, and have even launched new lifecycle channels from the ground up.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the lifecycle strategy across Consensys’ product offering (e.g. in-app notifications, in-app banners, push notifications, full screen modals,, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine the channel and messaging throughout a user’s lifecycle (new user education, activation, engagement, retention)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working end-to-end on a lifecycle campaign (through setting the strategy, briefing the creative team, building the targeting, QAing the campaign, and measuring results)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an experimentation roadmap across lifecycle channels. Continuously test and learn, identifying the most effective content and messages for different audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-8 years of experience in lifecycle marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built lifecycle user journeys from the ground up with little to no oversight on large userbases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management skills to manage multiple experiments at different points in their development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience executing in CEP systems such as Braze&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with marketing and analytical tools like Segment, Mixpanel, and Preset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self starter who is data-driven, results-oriented and customer-obsessed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, able to clarify complex ideas in a way that a broad audience can understand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web3 experience will be a bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Don&#39;t meet all the requirements? Don&#39;t sweat it. We’re passionate about building a diverse team of humans and as such, if you think you&#39;ve got what it takes for our chaotic-but-fun, remote-friendly, start-up environment—apply anyway, detailing your relevant transferable skills in your cover letter. While we have a pretty good idea of what we need, we&#39;re ready for you to challenge our thinking on who needs to be in this role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #e03e2d;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;It is a requirement of employment in this position that applicants will be required to submit to background checks including but not limited to employment, education and criminal record checks. Further details will be provided to applicants that successfully meet the criteria for the position as determined by the company in its sole discretion. By submitting an application for employment, you are acknowledging and consenting to this requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The salary range listed for this role applies to US-based candidates only. Compensation for candidates based outside the US (including Canada, EMEA, and LATAM) will be determined based on location, experience, and skills during the interview process, and may differ from the listed US range.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US pay range (not including bonus, equity or other benefits)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$162,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the rapidly evolving Web3 space, we believe that everyone is a builder. This expansive paradigm requires a range of backgrounds, talents, skills, and experiences to influence and shape the future. At Consensys, this diversity fuels our ability to shift control and redefine the realm of possibility. We are committed to ensuring that our technology empowers people and communities with economic and political agency through decentralized technologies. We welcome the range of perspectives and differences and celebrate them. We&#39;re excited to see how your unique skills as a builder can contribute to our vision, drive innovation, and help us shape a more inclusive Web3.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consensys is an equal opportunity employer. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, religion, disability, medical condition, pregnancy, marital status, family status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Consensys is aware of fraudulent recruitment practices and we encourage all applicants to review our best practices to protect yourself which can be found (&lt;a href=&quot;https://consensys.io/careers/best-practices-to-avoid-recruitment-fraud/)&quot;&gt;https://consensys.io/careers/best-practices-to-avoid-recruitment-fraud/)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8069694:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mission of the People Analytics team is to improve Stripe’s performance by collecting data, measuring critical constructs, and generating insights that help Stripe attract, develop, and retain our most important asset: our Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a team with diverse backgrounds across consulting, HR, and data-focused disciplines who are curious, passionate, and committed to using science and data to deliver high-value, precise outputs to our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of analytics and business partnership in equal measure. You will serve as the People Analytics Analyst and Business Partner to the People Partners supporting Stripe&#39;s International organization who look after our global sites across Core, Tech, and GTM functions. As the sole People Analytics team member based in Europe, you will be the first point of contact for International stakeholders and will need to operate with confidence and autonomy in that capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary analytics partner and single point of contact for People Partners and senior business leaders supporting Stripe&#39;s International organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and present comprehensive analyses that shape how leaders understand and act on their organizations, including ad hoc requests requiring urgency and clear communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain analytics products and self-service tooling through Visier and AI-powered solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead backend Visier platform administration including metric and dimension configuration, data hygiene, security, and report design governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with data engineering to identify and execute improvements to our workforce data ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across People Research and Insights, People Partners, and the Business to identify and deliver the highest-impact work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an analytics analyst and business partner who will help us in our ongoing journey to build a world class People Analytics team and improve the overall employee experience and productivity of our Stripes. You are someone who is curious, has an eye towards craftsmanship and enjoys working in a very fast-paced environment.&amp;nbsp; Through your work, you will likely need to partner closely with our People Research &amp;amp; Insights team, People Partners, People Org teams, and the Business to identify opportunities for greatest impact - then deliver value through creative problem-solving, actionable insights, and effective people practices. Examples of projects this individual may lead include Org health analysis, team size and spans, talent density, recruiting productivity, and geo strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in management consulting, people analytics, or a related analytical role (inside or outside of HR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate in a business partner capacity, working directly with senior stakeholders as a single point of contact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data visualization and communication skills, with the ability to translate complex findings into clear narratives for a range of audiences including senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Visier or a comparable BI platform; Visier experience strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI platforms such as those from Anthropic, OpenAI, or Google to develop tooling and accelerate analytical workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with human capital benchmarking and target setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity, competing priorities, and delivering high-quality work at pace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting international or multi-site organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across the full analytics project lifecycle from requirements gathering through deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward automation, self-service enablement, and building for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a scripting language such as Python or R&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current on best practices, research, and case studies in people analytics and workforce measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can bring structure to ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8069943:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Marketing Services is a team of marketing execution experts and systems thinkers focused on efficiency. We partner closely with Regional and Demand marketing, Growth, Martech, and creative teams to deliver scalable, high-impact campaigns across channels. While we operate globally, this role is focused on supporting the EMEA region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled and results-driven Marketing Services Program Manager to serve as the process owner for marketing campaign execution across multiple channels. The ideal candidate will possess a strong background in campaign management, with deep expertise in email marketing platforms like Marketo. This individual will work closely with diverse teams to enhance our marketing efforts, driving operational efficiency and process improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the process owner for campaign execution across email, landing pages, and paid media, supporting Growth, Lifecycle, EMEA and Demand Marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope campaign requirements, assess complexity, and lead capacity planning to ensure smooth and timely execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult on best practices in Marketo, with a focus on automation, scalability, and operational design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute complex nurture and trigger campaigns, then standardize and scale them for broader use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with marketing stakeholders to streamline workflows, reduce friction, and optimize campaign delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programs to address recurring execution challenges—defining objectives, success metrics, and building repeatable processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational risks early, communicate clearly with stakeholders, and implement sustainable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive ongoing improvements in marketing execution through process innovation, automation, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Growth, Regional and Demand Marketing, Engineering, and Design to align on priorities and execution strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain scalable documentation and support coordination with offshore production teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a marketing automation or campaign management role, ideally within a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of proven expertise in Marketo, with a strong track record of developing scalable programs and driving successful campaign outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management skills with experience leading cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, able to convey complex ideas effectively and tailor messaging to diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with a detail-oriented mindset to track performance metrics, analyze data, and identify opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team-oriented environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Marketing, Business, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​​Proactive, with a growth mindset and a passion for continuous learning and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the technology or financial services sectors, ideally within a high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with digital marketing channels, including paid media, SEO, and landing page optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of marketing automation tools and processes to enhance efficiency and scalability in campaign execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong adaptive skills with a proven ability to thrive in a rapidly changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or collaborating with an offshore production team to streamline operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8070701:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Sales is a team of deep functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio. Stripe is investing in the growth of its Issuing and Treasury businesses, which help platforms and businesses embed financial products. As a Sales Manager of Issuing and Treasury Product Sales, you will lead a high-performing team of product sales executives and be a critical member of the leadership team responsible for growing adoption of Issuing and Treasury across the Americas. Few roles offer such a direct opportunity to shape the commercial success of a strategic product area while developing the next generation of product sales leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As the Manager, AMER Issuing and Treasury Product Sales, you will recruit, develop, and lead a team of product sales executives responsible for delivering ambitious growth goals across Issuing and Treasury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will bring strong sales leadership, operating rigor, and a customer-first mindset to a complex and evolving product area. You will help your team navigate consultative, technical, and cross-functional sales cycles, partnering closely with Core Sales, Product, Solutions Architecture, Risk, Compliance, Partnerships, Finance, Marketing, and Sales Development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ideal candidate has demonstrated success managing and developing enterprise sales teams, bringing complex products to market, operating effectively through ambiguity, and building durable sales motions in a high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and lead a high-performing team of Issuing and Treasury product sales executives across AMER.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a clear strategy and operating plan that delivers against pipeline, bookings, attach rate, adoption, and revenue goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day business operations, including pipeline creation, deal progression, forecasting, performance against targets, and inspection of key sales metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the team to lead consultative, solution-based sales cycles with prospective and existing users, from discovery through close and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Core AEs to identify, prioritize, and execute on the highest-potential Issuing and Treasury opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly in the largest and most strategic opportunities, building executive relationships, shaping commercial strategy, and helping the team win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and refine scalable sales motions for new business, expansion, and strategic account growth across Issuing and Treasury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong feedback loops with Product, Engineering, Risk, Compliance, and Operations to surface market needs, unblock critical deals, and improve the end-to-end customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product capabilities, implementation requirements, and regulatory considerations into clear value propositions for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure and focus for GTM initiatives, product launches, campaigns, and enablement programs. Drive execution, measure outcomes, and make timely recommendations for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and enable individual development, creating clear expectations and meaningful career growth opportunities for direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with clarity and context, communicating a compelling plan that is aligned with Stripe’s strategy and the broader Global Issuing and Treasury Sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve sales processes, operating mechanisms, and team effectiveness by sharing best practices and testing new approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technology sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people leadership experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in payments or financial services industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading enterprise new-business and expansion sales motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling complex, technical, or regulated products through multi-stakeholder buying processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train, and coach a high-performance sales team, and work in a matrixed environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build cross-functional relationships, motivate others, drive collaboration, teaming &amp;amp; resolve conflict between diverse stakeholder groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High energy, strong work ethic, disciplined execution skills, willingness to do whatever it takes to deliver results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;True team player - always&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humor is very welcomed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8070949:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Core Infrastructure organization operates the foundational systems that power Stripe globally — including databases (MongoDB, PostgreSQL), high availability and disaster recovery (HADR), AWS cloud infrastructure, Linux servers, container orchestration, mesh networking, service discovery, and network edge infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Core Infra, the &lt;strong&gt;Regional Enablement Platform (REP)&lt;/strong&gt; team helps Stripe launch and operate new regions without learning about broken dependencies from users. REP builds the regionalization, validation, deploy-safety, and operator tooling needed to answer practical launch-readiness questions: can critical payment paths run from the new region, which services still depend on a remote control plane, what breaks under packet loss or failover, and what must be fixed before deploys, launches, traffic shifts, or failovers proceed. The team uses traffic replay, synthetics, failover drills, dependency analysis, CI/CD gates, and incident data to turn those findings into platform fixes, service-owner asks, and reusable readiness checks across networking, HADR, and service teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in &lt;strong&gt;Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; and serves as a senior technical anchor for Core Infrastructure in India, with direct cross-region influence across AMER, EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer on REP, you will play a key leadership role in enabling Stripe&#39;s infrastructure to power all of our products, globally and at scale. You will decide how Stripe validates that a new region can safely take traffic and continue working through network loss, failover, and deploy changes. You will define the checks that must pass before launch or failover, build validation systems that replay real production paths against regional infrastructure, and turn those checks into CI/CD gates, operator workflows, and concrete fixes for service or platform owners. You will also help build Core Infrastructure&#39;s senior technical bench in Bangalore through design review, mentoring, and cross-region technical leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define evidence-based readiness criteria for regional launches, traffic migrations, and failovers — replacing manual checklists with repeatable, globally consistent patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and mitigate risks on critical payment paths; use system data to drive ownership and validate that platform mitigations measurably reduce impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end cross-functional delivery for new-region infrastructure, including safe service behaviors for remote control planes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable validation tooling that accelerates infrastructure integration for new acquisitions and reduces high-priority blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert recurring operational friction into scalable platform capabilities used across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical conversations and define decision mechanisms across Core Infrastructure and product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate a multi-year technical strategy for REP with clearly defined quarterly milestones and success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug production issues across services and levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow senior engineers, elevating technical planning, design standards, and cross-region execution from Bangalore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a global, distributed environment with asynchronous decision-making across AMER, EU, and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or MS in Computer Science or equivalent field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of professional experience in software or infrastructure engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading complex, cross-team or company-wide infrastructure projects with high reliability and scale requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering background in distributed systems, platform engineering, or backend infrastructure, with a focus on operational safety and correctness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience optimizing the reliability and security of distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling and migrating systems with little to no downtime&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and written communication skills, including design docs and trade-off analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers at various stages of their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with one or more major cloud providers — AWS, Azure, OCI, or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ops culture and a solid understanding of metrics, alarms, and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience validating large-scale migrations, failovers, regional launches, regionalization, or control-plane behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating infrastructure with strict reliability, correctness, latency, or availability requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong observability judgment across metrics, logs, tracing, alerting, and incident analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with networking, service discovery, traffic routing, databases, Kubernetes, Terraform, or cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reducing packet loss, network latency, cross-region dependency risk, or other infrastructure failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making infrastructure validation or readiness evidence usable by service owners, operators, or partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning repeated operational problems into reusable tools, standards, or platform mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8072886:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Executive Recruiter, you won&#39;t just fill positions—you’ll directly shape Robinhood’s trajectory by attracting, engaging, and landing the visionary leaders who build our business! You will lead high-impact executive searches across a range of functions, partnering closely with senior leaders to translate business priorities into thoughtful talent strategies. You will also build long-term relationships with executive talent, develop market intelligence, and create pipelines that support both immediate hiring needs and future leadership and succession priorities. This is an opportunity to help evolve Robinhood’s executive recruiting capabilities, introduce scalable and innovative practices, and directly influence the strength of our leadership team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Chicago, IL, Menlo Park, CA, and New York, NY offices, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with executives and hiring leaders to define leadership profiles, clarify organizational needs, and develop tailored search and assessment strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with high-caliber, passive executive talent through research, targeted outreach, networking, and long-term engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use search metrics, outreach data, and pipeline health checks to optimize search strategies in real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a high-touch, personalized candidate journey that reflects Robinhood’s mission, values, and commitment to excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to hiring leaders by providing clear perspectives on the market, candidate quality, pipeline health, search challenges, and closing considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiment with and integrate AI-powered tools and research platforms to elevate sourcing efficiency and talent discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of recruiting experience, with a proven track record of directly managing complex senior-level or executive searches (in-house executive recruiting experience is preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and the ability to establish credibility, influence decisions, and navigate differing stakeholder perspectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building executive talent communities or pipelines tied to long-term succession and organizational planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong research and sourcing capabilities, including experience with market mapping, competitive intelligence, and talent pipelining&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential searches, sensitive candidate information, and organizational planning discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to assess leadership talent beyond résumé qualifications, including scope, impact, operating style, motivations, and alignment with organizational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to develop compelling and highly personalized candidate outreach and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple complex searches and shifting priorities while maintaining a high level of organization and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$149,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$131,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$154,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$116,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$137,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8072892:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, our mission is to democratize finance for all. The Treasury Operations team plays a critical role in supporting this vision by ensuring the company has the financial resources and market access needed to grow, innovate, and manage cash. As the Senior Treasury Analyst, you will lead our efforts to implement a treasury management system, build and maintain a direct cash flow forecast, and to support daily operations. Reporting to our Director of Treasury Operations &amp;amp; Investments, you will work cross-functionally with teams such as Treasury Risk, Finance, Accounting, Engineering, Procurement,&amp;nbsp; Engineering, Legal, and Tax to drive critical initiatives that support the growth of centralized Treasury organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; or Chicago, IL office with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build &amp;amp; implement automation workflows that leverage AI and incorporate human approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and monitor the global daily cash position across all entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the implementation of a Treasury Management System to manage cash positioning, direct cash forecasting, bank account management, bank fee analysis, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based on an understanding of Flow of Funds and liquidity requirements, lead the opening and closing of bank accounts to support the corporate, brokerage, and futures businesses, and serve as the primary backup for crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the maintenance of bank KYC requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead U.S. cash management and wire settlements, including wire transfers, internal settlements, borrowings, repayments, capital markets transaction settlements, and investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement cash optimization strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take primary responsibility for banking portal management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backup responsibility for 13-week direct cash flow forecast , including variance tracking and scenario modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backup responsibility for the bank account database, which is the single source of truth of global bank account balances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strict adherence to all SOX controls while delivering on daily, quarterly, and annual audit requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the creation and maintenance of policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participant in the maintenance of treasury management banking relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide periodic on-call support to monitor internal funding alerts and SEVs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Corporate Treasury, preferably within a publicly traded global financial services company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in implementing automation using AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in managing a Direct Cash Flow Forecast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in Treasury Operations with a strong understanding of key management controls and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with proficiency in Excel, Google Sheets, and Superset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to collaborate cross-functionally and apply creative, curious problem-solving to complex financial operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Economics, Computer Science, Financial Engineering or a related field (MBA or CTP designation preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$102,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$99,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$106,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$80,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$94,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
