&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Toronto, ON&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$235,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8081423:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Global Product Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is a small, high impact team. We help run the Global product organization, which is responsible for helping Stripe and our users expand globally. Our team works cross functionally within the Global Product and across most of Stripe’s teams. We develop the long-term strategic plan for Global, drive an operating model that allows the Global organization to operate at scale, and design and incubate high impact 0→1 initiatives. Whatever it is, we work on what will move the needle most for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work cross-functionally within our group and across Stripe’s technical and user-facing teams to solve problems that benefit our users. Specifically:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on cross-cutting company strategy projects and collaborate with teams to implement changes;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with senior leaders and cross functional teams to accelerate progress, solve hard scaling initiatives, and incubate new programs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive analysis and research to help inform our overall strategy and make the right growth decisions for global products, including local payment methods;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the product roadmap for the Stripe’s APAC business through robust gathering of competitive intelligence, user insights, and data analysis;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Product, Engineering, GTM &amp;amp; cross-functional leadership teams on where resources should be deployed to maximize long-term strategic value;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance to drive planning processes, including investment decisions, strategy updates, operational plans, and OKRs; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a pulse on the financial health of the APAC business, highlighting key metrics and trends and developing action plans to drive improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a strategy, business operations, or highly analytical role at a technology company, or similar experience in management consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to add structure and clarity to ambiguous, open-ended problems, and distill complex findings into clear, concise, and actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex, technical products and articulate their value to non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, cross-functional projects with multiple functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional stakeholder management skills, demonstrated by a track record of driving alignment and complex decisions with senior cross-functional leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with Product and Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to thrive in influence-without-authority environments and contexts with a high degree of ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong oral and written communication skills, with a proven ability to work effectively with multiple, cross-functional stakeholders, including users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A “can do” attitude, comfort with ambiguity, and ability to juggle multiple priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Mandarin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8081673:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The administrative business partner team works with Stripe&#39;s executive leaders to strategically manage their day-to-day administrative and operational needs, while also contributing significantly to projects and initiatives that help drive the company&#39;s strategic priorities. In this role, you&#39;ll be a critical part of supporting our business function by offering administrative support to 2-3 leaders within the same organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll be a critical part of supporting our executive function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide complex calendar support for your leaders and, potentially, other members of their team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage travel arrangements and process expense reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make recommendations for your executives with regard to their time management, prioritization, delegation, and organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and plan team meetings and offsites by assisting with the production of materials and pre-reads, taking notes, and tracking action items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with your executive to track key project milestones as well as progress against personal, team, and company goals and targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish new—and improve existing—administrative systems and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the operations and culture of various Stripe teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of administrative experience at a quickly scaling or large company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are incredibly organized, with superb attention to detail and a strong ability to execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excellent with time management and able to quickly shift tasks and priorities as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a knack for working across various roles and teams in a fast-paced, changing environment while remaining flexible, proactive, resourceful, and efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate, perform, and react well under pressure or ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy optimizing processes to make them more efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are adept at handling sensitive information and situations with care and confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to anticipate and respond to the needs of others before they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience in a high-growth technology startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8081754:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Partner Engineering and Operations (PE&amp;amp;O) team is a vital part of Stripe’s Global Partnerships organization, playing a key role in our overall success. We manage the technical and operational dimensions of new and existing strategic product partnerships and programs. Positioned at the nexus of product development, engineering, and partnerships, we facilitate seamless collaboration essential for supporting Stripe’s rapid growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our team is a diverse mix of technical and business professionals dedicated to executing operations with financial ecosystem partners. We ensure efficient technical onboarding and implementation, while also overseeing ongoing KTLO (Keep-The-Lights-On) activities and achieving strict quality and performance benchmarks. Additionally, the PE&amp;amp;O team initiates partner-agnostic programs and solutions to tackle broad ecosystem challenges, developing tools that enhance operational efficiency and scalability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is establishing a new function to oversee Card Network Compliance. In this position, you will be responsible for developing programs and processes to address Stripe’s card network changes and their implications for both Stripe and its users. This role is crucial for ensuring we stay informed about ongoing card network announcements, enhancing our strategic position, and driving operational efficiency in response to changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity to contribute significantly to building a function from the ground up and to help formulate strategies that align with the best interests of Stripe and its users!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implement Release Management Process: &lt;/strong&gt;Establish a release management process for Stripe in accordance with Card Network mandates, advising all cross-functional partners on the impacts, changes, and timelines associated with network updates. Conduct comprehensive analyses of how these mandates affect existing processes and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review Card Network Releases: &lt;/strong&gt;Review, analyze, and assess biannual card network releases to identify key initiatives that will significantly impact Stripe’s business. Collaborate cross-functionally with various teams to ensure proper visibility and prioritization of these initiatives. Facilitate communication between engineering teams and the card networks&#39; Technical Partner Managers (TPaMs) to streamline clarifications and negotiations regarding complex mandates and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitor Compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Establish a framework and process for monitoring compliance with card network requirements and internal policies. Ensure regular audits and assessments are conducted to identify gaps and drive continuous improvement strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Metrics and Dashboards: &lt;/strong&gt;Create and implement comprehensive metrics and JIRA dashboards to effectively monitor, review, and analyze mandates for each release cycle. Regularly update and refine the dashboards to reflect current business priorities and challenges, enabling teams to make informed decisions and proactively address potential issues related to card network mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage Mandate Intake Process: &lt;/strong&gt;Oversee the network mandate intake process, ensuring timely review, assessment, and prioritization of mandates. Lead the proactive management of waiver requests, liaising between compliance and operational teams for resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with External Partners: &lt;/strong&gt;Actively engage with external network partners by participating in councils, forums, and regular strategic meetings. Establish and nurture relationships that facilitate mutual understanding of goals and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advocate for Stripe: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as a dedicated advocate for Stripe within the card network ecosystem, ensuring that the unique perspectives, challenges, and opportunities faced by Stripe are considered by network stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the payments industry, with significant expertise in working with card networks and understanding card network rules and compliance activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of acquiring platforms and systems, and their interactions with card network products and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in navigating and using JIRA for project management and tracking. Familiarity with card network portals for managing and monitoring compliance activities. Comfortable utilizing Google Workspace tools (such as Sheets, Docs, and Slides) for collaboration and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of effectively collaborating with product and engineering teams to develop new processes and strategies in partnership with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program and project management abilities, with the capacity to engage and influence stakeholders outside of direct control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills to effectively engage with both internal and external partners and drive change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive with minimal guidance, navigating uncertainty and ambiguity while shaping a new program and function at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker adept at identifying cross-functional issues, providing innovative solutions, and communicating the implications of these solutions across existing processes, systems, and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a payment service provider (PSP), card network, or high-growth technology company&amp;nbsp; is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., Finance, Technology) is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8082579:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM + ROLE&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI R&amp;amp;D team is at the core of Robinhood&#39;s product intelligence. Our mission is to build and scale high-impact models that power personalization, search, social feeds, fraud detection, and risk management for millions of Robinhood users. We operate as a cross-functional partner to growth, product, and data engineering—translating complex financial data into intelligent systems that make Robinhood smarter for every customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast, raise the bar, and care deeply about building things that matter. If you&#39;ve ever wanted to solve personalization problems no one else has cracked—in one of the most data-rich, regulated industries on the planet—this is the team for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Machine Learning Engineer on the AI R&amp;amp;D team, you will own the design and delivery of sophisticated personalization and recommendation systems that directly shape what millions of users see and do on the Robinhood platform. You&#39;ll be a technical anchor on a growing, high-caliber team — collaborating with product, data engineering, and fellow ML engineers to take ambitious ideas from zero to one and into production at scale. You&#39;ll help define the team&#39;s technical direction, mentor engineers, and push the frontier of what&#39;s possible when you apply modern ML — including agentic workflows and LLM fine-tuning — to real financial data. This role offers a rare combination of technical depth, product impact, and the satisfaction of building systems that genuinely don&#39;t exist anywhere else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA and Bellevue, WA offices, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and ship end-to-end personalization, ranking, and recommendation systems that power core Robinhood products including growth, social feeds, and search — handling the full ML lifecycle from feature engineering through model deployment and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, data engineering, and platform teams to define technical strategy, scope complex projects, and drive execution across multiple workstreams simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead zero-to-one development of new ML capabilities — prototyping, iterating, and scaling models in a high-stakes fintech environment where data quality and regulatory constraints are first-class concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, experiment with, and integrate modern AI paradigms including agentic workflows and LLM fine-tuning into existing ML systems, pushing the team&#39;s technical capabilities forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical bar through architecture reviews, code reviews, and mentorship — helping to elevate the craft and velocity of the broader AI R&amp;amp;D team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience as a Machine Learning Engineer, with a strong foundation in ML fundamentals (ranking, recommendation systems, deep learning, optimization) and a track record of shipping models to production at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in personalization and recommendation systems — specifically, experience owning these systems end-to-end in a high-traffic, data-rich environment (fintech, e-commerce, social, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to deliver projects from zero to one: you&#39;ve taken ambiguous, high-impact problems and built production-grade solutions with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to or hands-on experience with agentic systems, LLM fine-tuning, or other modern AI paradigms — and the technical judgment to know when (and when not) to apply them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Statistics, or a related technical field, or equivalent professional experience; strong coding skills in Python and familiarity with ML infrastructure tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Tier benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet - a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$255,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$225,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$264,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$199,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$234,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8082718:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Robinhood set out to open the financial system to the many, not the few. We&#39;ve done it for tens of millions of people in the US—now we&#39;re taking it global. This is one of the most ambitious initiatives for the company, and you&#39;d be sitting at the center of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;We&#39;re building an elite team that applies frontier technology to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We want bold thinkers, sharp problem-solvers, and builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency—it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. Expectations are high. So are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;As a Senior Product Manager for the Crypto Onchain team, you&#39;ll be responsible for Robinhood&#39;s crypto wallet. You&#39;ll work to understand what customers need on their first day, first week and first month and deliver it in a simple, easy-to-understand experience. Whether it&#39;s improving our sign-up process or the self-custody experience, you&#39;ll be responsible for rolling out the red carpet for every new customer, setting them up for success in their financial lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA and New York, NY offices, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p8i6j0a&quot;&gt;Drive the product roadmap for Robinhood Wallet, evolving the existing experience while defining what’s next—including new products and localized experiences for priority markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p8i6j0a&quot;&gt;Partner with research, data science, engineering, and design to understand new customers, identify their most pressing needs, and translate insights into product strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p8i6j0a&quot;&gt;Build strong, collaborative relationships across design, engineering, operations, and other cross-functional partners to align teams and drive execution at both the team and organizational levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p8i6j0a&quot;&gt;Lead the launch of intuitive, high-impact products in partnership with communications, content, and marketing teams, ensuring experiences are easy to understand and use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;5+ years of experience building and shipping high-quality consumer products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Demonstrated history of using research, experimentation and analytics to guide decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Past experience working closely with design and UXR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Extremely curious&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Motivated self-starter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Ability to set high-level strategy + execute with cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Well-versed in the current crypto wallet market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Deep knowledge of onchain culture and products — ideally an active onchain trader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Past experience in fintech or trading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Deep experience with the latest AI tooling such as Claude Code, Gemini, Cursor, or ChatGPT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Market competitive and pay equity-focused compensation structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Annual lifestyle wallet for personal wellness, learning and development, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Lifetime maximum benefit for family forming and fertility benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Dedicated mental health support for employees and eligible dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Generous time away including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Lively office environment with catered meals, fully stocked kitchens, and geo-specific commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Our team is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming interview experience for all candidates. If you require a specific accommodation during the application or interview process due to a physical or mental condition, please complete this &lt;a class=&quot;underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current&quot; href=&quot;https://robinhood.hracuity.net/webform/index/752875e4-42ba-4dff-9951-fd51e315997e&quot;&gt;Applicant Accommodation Form&lt;/a&gt; to notify our team. The form should only be completed if you need a specific accommodation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;AI Usage Disclosure: Robinhood uses artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of our recruiting process. These tools enhance the efficiency and consistency of our hiring process; however, all hiring decisions are made by our hiring teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$166,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$146,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$129,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8082847:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/payments/link&quot;&gt;Link&lt;/a&gt; helps Stripe&#39;s merchants deliver frictionless and secure checkout experiences by auto-filling customers&#39; payment information, letting customers check out in seconds and pay in one click across the Link merchant network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Balance team is building on top of that network to transform Link from a one-click checkout into a global consumer financial platform. Link Balance lets consumers hold, spend, earn rewards on, and off-ramp digital dollars—stored as stablecoins, powered by Bridge and Privy, and distributed through Stripe&#39;s network of hundreds of millions of consumers. We&#39;re bringing the borderless, programmable, and instant utility of digital dollars into everyday use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Staff Software Engineer to lead the design and delivery of new money-movement capabilities in Link. You will take ambiguous product opportunities and turn them into reliable, scalable, and intuitive experiences for consumers and merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual-contributor role with broad technical and organizational scope. You will own large, cross-functional projects from early product and technical definition through launch and iteration; lead teams of engineers through complex execution; and partner closely with the many Stripe systems and teams that make money movement possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the stack, building services and APIs as well as the user experiences that expose those capabilities. The work may involve modern financial infrastructure—including stablecoin-enabled capabilities—while requiring sound judgment around safety, reliability, compliance, and user trust. You will make the architectural decisions that let the balance model scale globally, and raise the engineering bar for the team as we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical strategy, architecture, and execution for large, ambiguous Link initiatives that create new money-movement primitives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects end to end: clarify the problem, define an incremental technical plan, align stakeholders, drive delivery, launch safely, and use results to guide further investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build robust, scalable backend services and high-quality consumer-facing experiences across Java, Ruby, and TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a project team of engineers through execution, creating clarity on priorities, decisions, risks, and delivery milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Data Science, Risk, Infrastructure, and other Stripe teams to build capabilities that are safe, reliable, and useful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate dependencies across Stripe’s payments and money-movement platforms, making thoughtful tradeoffs between speed, user experience, operational reliability, and durable technical foundations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the engineering bar through technical leadership, design reviews, mentoring, and constructive feedback across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the team’s longer-term roadmap by identifying opportunities, technical risks, and investments needed to scale Link’s financial capabilities globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of backend and/or full-stack software development experience, with a track record of owning large, ambiguous systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical experience leading the design and delivery of large, complex software projects from early definition through production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering skills, including experience building reliable backend services and polished user-facing product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and unblocking a group of engineers on a substantial project as a senior individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in high-ambiguity environments: framing problems, making durable technical decisions, and creating an actionable path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional and cross-organizational collaboration skills, with the ability to align teams with different systems, priorities, and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering judgment around system reliability, operational excellence, security, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-minded approach to engineering, with a focus on delivering meaningful outcomes for users and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Java, Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building payments, money-movement, fintech, or other regulated financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer products at scale, particularly products that require a high degree of user trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on 0→1 products or taking new capabilities from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with stablecoins, digital assets, or the infrastructure that enables global financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appreciation for the importance of good documentation—internal and external—and taking pride in seeing projects through to successful completion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8082905:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) primary goal is to ensure operational excellence across deal cycles, increase revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs, and drive closure of Stripe’s deal portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region; GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users and cross-functional teams. GBS’s priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as user feedback and market insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Global Business Services (GBS) team is looking for a Deal Strategist to play a pivotal role in shaping our strategy and commercial operation. In this strategic position, you will be a key partner to our go-to-market teams, providing expert guidance, recommendations, and influence on deal structuring, pricing, and commercial strategy to support strategic decision-making across the region. You will be responsible for deal lifecycle management and supporting cross-organizational alignment. This role requires a background in driving custom commercial and pricing deals to closure, a strong understanding of private pricing frameworks, and experience supporting sales through complex negotiations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate will have experience with subscription, usage-based revenue and hybrid pricing models, pricing strategies, and a background in supporting selling motions. The candidate will have strong communication skills and a passion for applying emerging technology to drive efficiency. You will love this job if you are a natural relationship and mechanism builder who thrives in fast-paced, dynamic environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support sellers with their deals end-to-end, this includes structuring, coaching, pricing, drafting, editing, managing xfn collaboration and approvals. Reviewing agreements while supporting the sales cycle to ensure deal terms align with business goals, reflect strategic priorities, and close as forecasted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach sellers on constructing strategically defensible opening commercial positions that preserve room to negotiate without conceding value, planning for typical deal iteration cycles and the commercial flexibility needed to maintain competitive terms through to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead contact between Sales, Commercial Legal, Risk, Monetization Ops, and other cross-functional stakeholders for deal-related queries, approvals, and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with sales teams, sales leaders, services/support teams and customers to advise on deal structures, establish compelling commercials, and drive closure of customer issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the business and technical requirements of our customers and partners, advising sales teams on the best approach (balancing risk between custom terms and internal system limitations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove internal blockers and drive solutions between cross-functional teams such as Product, Legal, Finance, Accounting, Service Teams, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial and legal agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the pricing and structuring of multithreaded product use cases in all segments and industries especially in highly competitive sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead program ownership for New Product Initiatives (NPI), including the creation of new commercial constructs, pricing bundles, and packages to support product go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally on the design, build, and launch of seller systems and tooling, including CPQ design and configuration, contract management platforms, and commercial workflow automation to support scalable deal operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strong support, communication, and persuasion skills including XFN and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong relationships with APAC regional go-to-market stakeholders to drive commercial alignment and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and enable Sales teams on pricing, quoting, and contract best practices, internal approvals to accelerate deal cycles and maximize business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clear, concise, and insightful commercial analyses, deal recommendations, and executive-level reports to stakeholders and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI fluency and actively apply emerging technology tools to drive day-to-day efficiency in deal workflows and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in deal operations/ pricing and strategy/procurement/program management/financial consulting/legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, comfortable with high-agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, negotiation, and program management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Payments and/or SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Salesforce and Ironclad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing redline agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with subscription and usage-based revenue models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of regional market regulations and business practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in AI, or related technology sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of building commercial or deal processes from the ground up in high-growth environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of scaling deals or commercial operations in rapidly growing organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English, as the role involves working with clients within the Greater China market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8083601:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Operations Specialist provides outstanding customer service and supports the daily management of the office, employee experience, vendor relations, and overall office and building maintenance. Ripple&#39;s Chicago office is currently under construction, and this role will be instrumental in standing it up from day one — helping develop the procedures, programming, and partnerships that set the foundation for a great workplace and employee experience. In this role, you have the strong ability to think on your feet, assigning an appropriate level of urgency to specific situations and working on projects independently. You are a diligent and resourceful problem-solver, able to iterate until the right solution is found. You can easily collaborate and communicate with internal teams and external partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Office Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee day-to-day workplace operations including food programs, deliveries, mailroom, decor, and supply ordering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure smooth functionality, high service standards, and a consistently positive employee experience as the site scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, execute, and maintain office procedures and workplace programming for a brand new space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a welcoming, safe, and professional office environment and serve as the primary point of contact for employees and guests for workplace-related questions, requests, and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Employee Experience &amp;amp; Events&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a culture of inclusion, hospitality, collaboration, and productivity across assigned office locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute surprise and delight moments for employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the People team on onboarding logistics to ensure new hires have a welcoming first-day experience, including desk setup, office tours, and introductions to workplace resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate logistics for onsite meetings and events, including meeting room/furniture setup and food orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
