8089302:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Crypto Operations team at Robinhood is dedicated to delivering an excellent end-customer experience and mitigating firm risk while supporting cutting-edge crypto products. As a Product Operations Associate, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation of our crypto products and future launches. You will lead cross-functional projects designed to improve Robinhood’s operational efficiency and readiness. The role will work on scaling operations for our existing Crypto products as well as scoping operational impact for new Crypto initiatives. This role will work with cross-functional partners including Product Management, Crypto Operations, Compliance, Legal, Engineering, Security, and Customer Experience to guarantee operational readiness. Product Operations Managers are passionate about delivering an excellent customer experience, achieving product objectives, and working with multiple partners. This is a unique opportunity to shape the future of crypto operations for one of the most dynamic teams in the industry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our New York City, NY office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and refine operational processes supporting Robinhood’s crypto products, ensuring they are efficient, scalable, and compliant with applicable laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, prioritize, and communicate product-related challenges to be considered by product and engineering in future development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Managers to own and execute tasks cross functionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools to optimize processes across workflows&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support product operations workflows, including routine and ad-hoc responsibilities, such as customer communications, language translations, pricing comparisons and product remediations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a liaison between operations and customer-facing teams, ensuring that support teams are equipped with the tools, training, and context needed to provide high-quality service to crypto customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process gaps, pain points, and inefficiencies across the crypto product lifecycle—and implement improvements through automation, enhanced tooling, or revised procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze operational metrics to ensure processes are performing as expected, and lead cross-functional efforts to address any issues or optimize performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in crypto product operations, crypto operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of cryptocurrency markets, blockchain technology, and the evolving regulatory landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to drive complex initiatives independently across teams and global time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI tools to optimize workflows across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail paired with a proactive, risk-aware mindset and a bias toward problem-solving and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourcefulness and agility in fast-paced, entrepreneurial environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$102,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$90,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$106,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$80,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$94,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8089353:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you would join Stripe&#39;s Vulnerability Management team, whose mission is to &quot;Surface vulnerabilities at scale across Stripe.&quot; Our vision is to create a culture of continuous excellence in managing vulnerabilities. We want to enhance customer trust by giving users context about threats and vulnerabilities affecting Stripe&#39;s systems. We aim to be a key partner in Stripe&#39;s risk management by providing visibility into vulnerabilities across Stripe&#39;s products and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer focused on Vulnerability Management at Stripe, you will use your software engineering expertise to find and prioritize vulnerabilities in our systems. Working closely with engineers across the company, you will drive the timely remediation of discovered vulnerabilities, playing a key role in Stripe&#39;s overall security and risk strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition, you will continuously improve Stripe&#39;s security defenses by enhancing our vulnerability management processes and selecting effective scanning tools to uncover weaknesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your core responsibilities as a Vulnerability Management Software Engineer will involve building data- and agent-backed systems to surface vulnerabilities across Stripe. In addition, you will coordinate fixes to prevent exploits that could impact Stripe or our users and serve as an advisor on security risks. All of this requires collaborating cross-functionally to advocate for practices that strengthen the safety of Stripe&#39;s systems and data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify vulnerabilities using automated tools and triage them appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other teams to drive remediation of vulnerabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our overall security and risk management strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve our security posture, processes, and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering experience within the security domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, strong communication skills and a deep respect for the power of collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards for code quality and a constructive attitude to help others raise the bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to think creatively and holistically about reducing risk in a complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with automated vulnerability identification tools and triage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery of successful projects using agents to automate human review processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our team, you will have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach, securely.&lt;/p&gt;

8089358:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Communications team builds and protects Stripe’s brand and influence across the world. Product Comms is a team of creative thinkers and entrepreneurial strategists tasked with deepening the understanding of Stripe’s products. We work closely with the Product, Marketing, Policy and wider Comms teams to produce imaginative and effective messaging and provide strategic counsel to our executive team that goes far beyond the bounds of traditional comms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is to lead global product communications for Stripe’s crypto offerings. You’ll work shoulder-to-shoulder with senior leaders and the teams building Stripe’s crypto products to shape the storytelling strategy around this new frontier of financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three important dimensions of this role include: (i) entrepreneurialism — you’ll work in uncharted territory, building a new comms muscle for Stripe. It’ll be up to you to identify and go after the best opportunities. (ii) superb writing and storytelling — you’ll bring your writing skills to bear on Stripe’s highest profile public moments, such as company letters, executive keynotes, and other long-form content. The vision for Stripe’s crypto products needs to come to life with your words. (iii) attention to detail — building in a new space requires a foundation of trust and legitimacy. You’ll work at an uncompromising quality bar where no detail is too small to matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead global product communications for Stripe’s crypto products,including Bridge and Privy (crypto infrastructure companies acquired by Stripe in 2025).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development, articulation and testing of Stripe’s long-term public vision for its crypto products, specifically as a substrate for economic growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and roll out strategic campaigns that build awareness for Stripe’s crypto products and deepen key audiences’ understanding of exactly what makes stablecoins so useful to global businesses of all sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and edit extremely high quality written materials for Stripe’s biggest moments, including newsroom posts, social content, industry keynotes, top tier media interviews and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with local and regional comms leads to raise awareness for Stripe globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain relationships with thought leaders and influencers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic counsel to our executive team, including Stripe’s founders and most senior product leaders, and collaborate closely with your counterparts on the partnerships, policy, and product marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve done exceptional work in your career to date and have the proof points to show for it (built a great product, ran a high-impact campaign, started your own business, or similar accomplishments).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a superlative writer; someone who has been recognized by their peers as a truly exceptional writer, with a particular knack for making technically sophisticated topics interesting and memorable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience collaborating effectively with large, cross-functional teams as well as working with senior executives 1:1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked in a technology, B2B and/or financial services or banking environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re passionate about the potential for (and real-world impact of) crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re deeply immersed in the world of independent media—Substackers, podcasters, video makers, influencers on X. You might personally know some of the people shaping these conversations (or even be one yourself), but more importantly, you understand the culture, the discourse, and where the zeitgeist is heading next. You combine the best of what you’ve found online with your original ideas to create compelling stories and new insights. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8089812:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini is a global crypto and Web3 platform founded by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss in 2014, offering a wide range of simple, reliable, and secure crypto products and services to individuals and institutions in over 70 countries. Our mission is to unlock the next era of financial, creative, and personal freedom by providing trusted access to the decentralized future. We envision a world where crypto reshapes the global financial system, internet, and money to create greater choice, independence, and opportunity for all — bridging traditional finance with the emerging cryptoeconomy in a way that is more open, fair, and secure. As a publicly traded company, Gemini is poised to accelerate this vision with greater scale, reach, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Department: Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini’s Customer Support Team is a highly skilled and dynamic group dedicated to providing exceptional customer service. Each team member plays a crucial role in ensuring that customers receive the best possible experience when seeking assistance, asking questions, or sharing feedback. The Gemini Credit Card and Exchange teams are expanding their presence with a regional office to better align customer support divisions.&amp;nbsp; Collectively, these teams efficiently handle all inbound phone-based service requests and communications for the Gemini Credit Card and email-based requests for Gemini Exchange.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Associate Director, Customer Support (Operations Center)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Director of the regional team, your role will be a combination of “getting your hands dirty” and management responsibilities within an inbound contact center. You will be expected to lead the workforce management function, collaborate with the Operations team with forecasting and building team rapport.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is required to be in person 5 days per week at our Tempe, AZ office.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead workforce management activities, including scheduling, forecasting, headcount planning, and timecard management to ensure optimal staffing and service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead local shift managers while partnering with global operations leaders to drive alignment and operational excellence across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and sustain a high-performance, customer-centric culture rooted in accountability, continuous improvement, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, develop, and empower leaders and team members through performance management, targeted training, feedback, and recognition to achieve individual and team goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate organizational strategy into actionable operational plans, measurable outcomes, and scalable solutions that support business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational inefficiencies and leverage data, analytics, and process improvements to optimize performance and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure operational readiness and business continuity for new products, business initiatives, organizational growth, and incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Global Operations, Legal, Facilities, Office Management, and Security to ensure compliance with company policies and maintain a safe, secure, and productive workplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage site budgets and operating expenses while identifying opportunities to improve efficiency and optimize costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minumum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 12 years of experience in a contact center, contact centers or financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5 years of contact center workforce management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google applications (Sheets, Docs, Slides).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success scaling operations during periods of rapid organizational growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Workforce Management principles, forecasting, scheduling, and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using operational metrics and data analytics to drive business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading change management and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a dynamic, high-growth environment with evolving priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and a dependable team-player attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt quickly to new information and changing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for delivering excellent client service with integrity and a proactive approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in the banking or financial industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of client service experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate Degree or higher.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within fintech, financial services, payments, or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;It Pays to Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;The compensation &amp;amp; benefits package for this role includes:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
