8089815:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Developer Productivity group is responsible for making Stripe’s developers happy and productive. We work on tools, processes, and code refactoring to accelerate Stripe engineering as Stripe scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people with an interest in building the tools to improve the day to day experience of Engineers in Stripe. The ideal candidate will have a passion for solving developer experience problems, and a pragmatic ability to ship results iteratively—powered by a mix of technical expertise across some or all of: language processing tools; version control systems; build systems; and distributed systems engineering. You’ll be working on a mix of engineer-facing systems, CI infrastructure platforms, and big-data engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a ton of important work to do, which is why we’re hiring! Our active projects change all the time, but here are a few examples of recent projects so you can get an idea of the types of work we do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage systems to handle CI at massive scale—including batching, speculative stacking, merge-race inhibition, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage systems to handle our enormous CI test suite–identifying and managing flaky tests, assessing and reproducing flakiness, and optimizing for test effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance our CI systems for reliability, including adaptive response to available capacity, resilience and self-recovery from outages, and highly-leveraged observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detect and isolate code breakages to minimize their blast radius.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with product engineers to understand and deliver their productivity needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and lead large technical projects with enormous impact for engineers within Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain the core CI systems used by all of Stripe’s engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrutinize and reason clearly about the technology and architecture choices we make in building these products. In many cases, you will be the owner of these decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly contribute to core interface design and write code. Serve as a role model for how great software should be written for Stripe as a whole.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arbitrate critical decisions correctly that fully consider software best practices, Stripe system realities, and numerous stakeholders’ preferences and concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach and mentor the next generation of technical leaders at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the effective and highly-leveraged use of AI-assisted implementation, ops, and delivery within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional hands-on software development experience&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience designing and building large scale distributed systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of technically mentoring junior and senior engineers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession, ability to articulate and represent customer experience in various forums to drive the right outcome&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability of defining &amp;amp; driving complex initiatives/projects across multiple teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success with cross-discipline and cross-team collaborations, possess strong conviction and courage skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy, responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related experience in the area of Developer Tooling, CI/CD or DevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8089882:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global GTM Operations team is responsible for overall productivity and effectiveness of the sales organization, partnering closely with the sales team and teams across Stripe to drive initiatives.&amp;nbsp; Within the Sales Strategy and Operations team, the &lt;strong&gt;Global Product Sales Strategy and Operations team&lt;/strong&gt; is aligned to each of Stripe’s Product Pillars (Revenue Suite, Money Management and Payments) and are heavily focused on partnering with both GTM and Product to drive the rhythm of business, strategic initiatives, bi-annual planning and execution. We advance the sales policies, processes and tools to drive revenue and growth. Within Stripe, the goal of the Product sellers is to help users understand Stripe’s specialised offerings and recommend the right Stripe solutions and implementation path.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an incredible opportunity that plays an integral role in shaping and executing GTM strategies with Sales leaders.&amp;nbsp; You will partner with senior Sales leadership and the broader Sales team to drive the overall productivity and effectiveness of the mid market segment. Responsibilities include go-to-market design, resource planning, quota setting and management, sales process optimization and business analytics. You will also partner with key cross-functional stakeholders, including Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, Functional Sales Operations, Global Systems &amp;amp; Processes, and the Strategy Planning and Insights team to streamline and optimize our internal processes and deliverables (monthly business reviews, weekly forecasting calls, target setting and planning). We are looking for a self-starter who&amp;nbsp; is passionate about their work, detail oriented, analytical and has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity in a high-growth environment, and solving problems with limited oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is growing rapidly and the majority of our near term focus is on building business foundations, which entails a focus on operational projects (process design, business cadences, systems work). This &lt;strong&gt;Sales Strategy and Operations business partner&lt;/strong&gt; is the right-hand person to their Product Sales Leader on everything related to planning and running their business, including: org design and planning, partner/sales coverage models, setting SOKRs, measuring and providing insights on performance, forecasting, and process improvement.&amp;nbsp; In addition to engaging with the Sales team, you will also be collaborating with numerous cross-functional stakeholders from across the globe, including: finance operations, sales operations, professional services consulting operations, product and system operations and customer success and renewals operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales leadership and cross-functional stakeholders in developing go-to market strategy, resource plan and key performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage operational processes such as&amp;nbsp; territory planning and target setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to investigate and conduct analysis on system and operational issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute initiatives designed to optimize sales team efficiency and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive rhythm of business (forecasting, pipeline council, monthly / quarterly business reviews) with strong operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights on key performance metrics and priorities (e.g. weekly, monthly, quarterly business reviews), identify key roadblocks to progress, and work efficiently to remove them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide business analytic strength to help drive initiatives critical to ongoing growth and provide key insights for business leadership to support strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive critical projects and initiatives and drive alignment with cross-functional teams across the organization by developing detailed project plans with activity based milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee implementation of enabling systems and tools, working closely with internal systems teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the minimum requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of sales strategy and operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, or operational experience in investment banking, management consulting, private equity, venture capital, or business insights / analytics roles. Knowledge of sales data such as customer accounts, opportunities and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in a related field (e.g. Finance, Business, Engineering, Mathematics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and ​​Distinctive problem solving and analysis skills. Ability to solve complex and diverse business problems (commercial, operational, organizational).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills and a structured approach to solving unique business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL and Excel skills to include experience financial modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large data sets, especially in analyzing large imperfect data sets to solve problems and creating scalable reports and dashboards or ad-hoc analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management experience - with strong communication and influencing skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter and comfortable dealing with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly, proactively, and concisely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast-paced and frequently changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality. Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast paced, ambiguous and rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or higher degree in an analytical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/software company or FinTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in BI visualization tools (e.g. Tableau)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Salesforce.com as a user and report developer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8090126:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Partnerships team sources, develops, and manages relationships with the payments ecosystem partners that power Link, Stripe&#39;s consumer wallet. Our team drives the growth and utility of Link by building partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, crypto providers, and emerging commerce platforms. We execute on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives that expand Link&#39;s acceptance, improve performance, and enable new payment experiences—including agentic commerce. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Development Manager who builds and manages Link&#39;s payments partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment method providers, and crypto and stablecoin providers. You&#39;ll own the strategy and execution of partnerships that expand Link&#39;s payment capabilities, improve transaction performance, and position Link as the default payments layer for agentic commerce. You&#39;ll negotiate commercial agreements, drive technical integrations, and shape Link&#39;s payments roadmap in collaboration with these partners. As part of these efforts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with cross-functional stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, and others. You&#39;ll also lead relationship management and partner closely with external partners&#39; executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute Link&#39;s payments partnership strategy across card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, and crypto and stablecoins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage commercial agreements with payment partners that expand Link&#39;s acceptance footprint, improve authorization rates, and unlock new payment capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the card network and issuer landscape—including scheme rules, tokenization frameworks, authentication protocols, and competitive dynamics—to inform partnership strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive partnerships that enable Link to serve as the payments layer for agentic commerce, working with networks and issuers to establish rules, liability frameworks, and technical standards for agent-initiated transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather inputs from and coordinate with internal cross-functional stakeholders (including product, risk, compliance, engineering, and security) to drive creation and execution of partner strategy including our global LPM roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product and Engineering to define requirements and shape Link&#39;s payments product roadmap based on partner capabilities and market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, educate them about Link&#39;s value proposition, and build alignment between Stripe and our partners&#39; executive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and effectively analyze new partnership opportunities, ultimately making recommendations to relevant decision makers and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit an operationally focused mindset, with an ability to lead teams through complex relationship management activities by setting a clear vision and running tight processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re a skilled dealmaker and a strategist by nature. You understand how to work closely with Product and Engineering teams and can formulate partner strategies that drive tangible and measurable results. You&#39;re energized by the intersection of payments infrastructure and emerging commerce models, and you see the opportunity to define how payments work in an agentic world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in or working closely with card networks, card issuers, digital wallets, or payments infrastructure providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience negotiating commercial deals with partners, including scaling such deals across multiple partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, in both verbal and written form, and ability to influence stakeholders across a wide variety of functions, including at executive levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen, especially an ability to understand product strategy and use this understanding to define requirements for scaling products through partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategies and identifying, sourcing, and analyzing new partnership opportunities in greenfield segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with card scheme rules, tokenization (network tokens, device tokens), authentication frameworks (3DS, SCA), and issuer-side authorization optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with emerging payment models such as agentic commerce, embedded payments, or programmable payment flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new partnership category or vertical from zero—defining the strategy, establishing first partnerships, and scaling the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8090141:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Service Infrastructure team is responsible for empowering teams to build highly reliable and performant services, backing our payment systems, fraud detection, and a multitude of other products. As an infrastructure team, you will build and expand the service frameworks to make complex systems easy to use, resilient, and scalable. We build powerful interfaces for engineers that depend on these systems—deployment, load balancers, web framework, databases, Kafka, and Kubernetes—while keeping them highly available and performant. We&#39;re looking for engineering leaders who drive the technical vision of Stripe&#39;s service infrastructure platform for thousands of engineers to use and build on top of, and thrive in a highly autonomous environment with many moving pieces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join as a Technical Lead for one of the most impactful teams at Stripe. You will lead a team of engineers, collaborate with infrastructure and product engineering orgs, and advance service-oriented architecture (SOA) adoption at Stripe. By collaborating with the team&#39;s technical leaders, you will ensure the software your team builds meets the needs of Stripe and its customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a highly effective team that consistently delivers high-impact results while genuinely caring for one another. We expect you to bring your curiosity and critical thinking skills to this challenging domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for individuals with a strong background in designing and delivering high-performance infrastructure products for both internal and external customers. We would love to hear from you whether you have spent your entire career in infrastructure or are looking to apply your skill set to the database engineering domain for the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers to create roadmaps that deliver milestones toward a cohesive engineering vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize engineering work and deliver high-quality solutions that meet user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with high-visibility teams and their stakeholders to support the Infrastructure&#39;s key engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture and design, vision, direction, and requirements setting, and incident response processes) for team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across the company to create and drive toward the longer term vision of Stripe&#39;s services roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of technical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a strategic technical leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading engineering team(s) working on API design, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g., building internal or external developer products)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building infrastructure and products for internal or external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering pragmatic solutions that accelerate business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adjust conversations from high-level discussions to detailed coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, critical thinking, determination, and a growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of people, genuinely caring for each other and contributing to a high level of psychological safety for all team members and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in at least one of the programming languages (Java, Ruby, Python, Go)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of common infrastructure platforms (databases, logging, event streams, metrics, caching, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote and distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sustainable, in-house framework and abstraction ecosystems in large engineering orgs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building serverless platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on-call rotations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t expect deep expertise in every dimension above, but genuine curiosity about any of the areas that are less familiar is important to us&lt;/p&gt;

8090190:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Operations team’s mission is to provide accurate, complete, and timely financial and operational information to our leaders, regulators, customers, and key stakeholders. We ensure efficient asset utilization, proactively mitigate risks, and ensure full compliance with regulatory bodies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Financial Operations Manager to join our growing team on the ground in Singapore. In this role, you will lead our local financial regulatory reporting and finops work, ensuring adherence to Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) regulations while collaborating across international entities. As one of the early operational hires in Singapore, you will play a key role in building processes from the ground up with high autonomy and visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Singapore office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage risk for back-office activities by maintaining controls over customer and firm cash, suspense accounts, and exception handling. Execute daily trust and custody computations by the strict deadline of 12:00 PM SGT in compliance with Securities and Futures (Licensing and Conduct of Business) Regulations (SF(LCB)R).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage automated MT940 (Swift) messages and API pulls, extract customer ledger balances, and download statements from trust banks and sub-custodians. Reconcile security quantities against sub-custodian statements and verify no liens or encumbrances are placed on customer assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor Financial Resources to ensure continuous compliance above Total Risk Requirement (TRR) limits. Prepare and submit quarterly filings via the MAS-Tx portal, including Form 1 (Statement of Assets &amp;amp; Liabilities), Form 2 (Statement of Financial Resources &amp;amp; TRR), and Form 7 (Aggregate Margin Exposure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Corporate Accounting, Treasury, RHS Clearing, and Engineering teams to support system transitions (e.g., system migrations, report automation) and cross-train across broader global entity reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of MAS Risk-Based Capital (RBC) frameworks, SF(LCB)R requirements, and capital requirements for broker-dealers in Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in financial operations or regulatory reporting within a broker-dealer or financial institution in Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing back-office ledger systems, Swift/API data feeds, and reporting automation using tools like Excel/Google Sheets (SQL or data visualization tools like Superset are a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong self-starter attitude with proven success operating independently in a fast-paced environment and managing time-sensitive regulatory deadlines (e.g., 12:00 PM SGT daily deliverables).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills to partner with global teams across varying time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, and equity ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top tier benefits to fuel your work, including supplemental health insurance, ancillary insurance, and mental health support programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet - a highly flexible employer-paid benefits spending account expenses beyond traditional benefits such as wellness, childcare, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, paid volunteer time off, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly commuter stipend to help offset in-office commuting costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8090203:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product Marketing team&#39;s mission is to generate customer insights that inform Stripe&#39;s product strategy, and lead go-to-market for our suite of products. Product Marketing is a highly cross-functional role at Stripe, partnering closely with Product and Engineering, Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation and Campaigns to name a few. Different from many other Product Marketing teams, our team works across the entire product lifecycle, from helping shape the product, to driving launch and commercialization, to growing product adoption post-launch. We also drive both self-serve and sales-sold marketing efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced product marketing leader to own our go-to-market strategy and grow adoption for Stripe Billing—which includes Subscriptions, Invoicing, and Metronome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead the go-to-market strategy for all Billing products, including segmentation, target audiences, positioning, launches, and post-launch adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and develop a high-performing team of product marketers, setting clear priorities and raising the bar for strategic thinking, customer insight, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize customer, market, and competitive insights to inform product strategy, roadmap prioritization, and differentiated commercialization plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear, compelling positioning and messaging that translates complex revenue-management capabilities into value for executive and technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation, and Campaigns to equip go-to-market teams with the narratives, enablement, and programs needed to engage enterprise customers effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams through high-stakes launches and growth initiatives, aligning senior stakeholders around decisions, sequencing, and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish success metrics and use customer, sales, and product data to assess performance, identify growth opportunities, and improve go-to-market strategy over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the product area in executive narratives, customer conversations, and key industry moments, building credibility with enterprise audiences and internal leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of product marketing experience, preferably in B2B technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing teams, with a proven record of building and leading high-performing, highly cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience marketing to enterprise audiences, with a demonstrated ability to understand complex buying committees, long sales cycles, and sophisticated business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort toggling between big-picture strategy and detailed execution, with a strong bias to action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation abilities, with a proven track record of explaining complex technical concepts in ways that executive, technical, and non-technical audiences can understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in billing, payments, subscription management, financial operations, or an adjacent industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to AI companies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8090244:
&lt;h2&gt;Who We Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSA) are domain experts aligned to specific Stripe solutions and customer buying centers. We have in-depth knowledge of specific solution offerings and a deep understanding of customer challenges. We align with specialist product sellers on deals, advise the broader pre-sales team on complex opportunities, support pipeline development and revenue attainment, serve as an advisor on go-to-market sales plays, and provide critical insights to our product and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with sales and pre-sales teams to drive pipeline and revenue targets, while also educating the product and engineering teams on market trends and strongly influencing the product roadmap. You will develop deep relationships with senior customer business leaders and grow Stripe&#39;s solution offerings with new and existing customers. As a subject matter expert, you will scale the broader organization by creating reusable assets and coaching others on complex, high-value opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert on Stripe Tax to accelerate opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a deep understanding of global indirect taxes—VAT, GST, sales and use tax, mandatory e-invoicing requirements—and how automated compliance solutions help online businesses meet their obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide solutions and recommendations to B2C, B2B, and platform business models on how to integrate Stripe Tax for end-to-end indirect tax compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep discovery of customers&#39; current processes and needs to architect solutions that drive key implementation decisions and accelerate deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and share best practices and reusable assets such as reference architectures to enhance the quality and efficiency of the broader sales and pre-sales organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Tax product sales team and actively drive opportunities for Stripe&#39;s largest customers, leading Tax solution strategy and owning key customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a &quot;Voice of the Customer&quot; to drive product and feature request prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify product, industry, implementation, and competitive trends, and provide actionable insights to product stakeholders and sales to influence Stripe&#39;s Tax product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation point to drive complex technical issues to resolution with Stripe&#39;s engineering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the technical health of the business on quarterly sales forecast calls and highlight deal blockers with proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing events including executive briefings, conferences, user groups, and trade shows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role such as solutions architect, solutions consultant, or sales engineer for a global software enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of accounting, indirect tax, or tax compliance experience within a technical sales organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or implementing a tax automation software solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of software engineering and architecture patterns, with the ability to understand how a wide variety of technologies and systems interact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for learning and staying up to date with indirect tax laws and emerging compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with compliance subjects including VAT, GST, B2B invoices, mandatory e-invoicing (Peppol, national mandates), sales and use tax, exemption certificates, and tax IDs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Stripe or other RESTful APIs into web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with competing tax automation solutions such as Avalara or Vertex&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-sales experience with enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8090473:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Engineer, Revenue and Financial Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Revenue &amp;amp; Financial Management group is building new products that expand the scope of problems we tackle beyond payments into Revenue Management, Financial Operations and analytics. Right now this includes products like Billing, Invoicing, Revenue Recognition, Reconciliation and the underlying platform for batch and real time processing of large scale financial data to power these solutions. These solutions are going to be key pillars for Stripe’s growing SaaS business and a major revenue stream.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Staff Engineer that will help architect and design this system from ground up. You will need to set the technical direction across a variety of projects and initiatives while also mentoring and growing others on the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and lead large technical projects that are the foundational pillars for Financial Data Management Infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrutinize and reason clearly about the technology and architecture choices we make in building these products. In many cases, you will be the decider of these decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly contribute to core interface design and write code. Serve as a role model for how great software should be written for Stripe as a whole&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arbitrate critical decisions correctly that fully consider software best practices, Stripe system realities, and numerous stakeholders’ preferences and concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Stripe’s leadership team on key technical considerations related to the future of financial data management (e.g., on the utility of blockchain technologies). If you’re successful, you will change how finance teams operate fundamentally across the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach and mentor the next generation of technical leaders at Stripe&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong technical background, including 12+ years of experience with system architecture and designing distributed systems handling large amounts of data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have been a Staff, Principal, or Distinguished Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience building custom solutions using big data and streaming technologies like Hadoop, Spark, Presto, Iceberg, and Airflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands on experience in building modern microservices architecture-based products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have served as the technical lead for a team of engineers and can demonstrate broad technical leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have owned the technical roadmap for a business area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You listen well and internalize the best ideas from all over the organization while also setting a vision that others are excited to get behind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well cross-functionally and your co-workers at all levels and across all teams trust you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are often cited as the inspiration for engineers that join your teams. Even senior engineers feel that they’re able to learn from you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain expertise in accounting or financial management&amp;nbsp; is a plus but not a requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8091954:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini is a global crypto and Web3 platform founded by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss in 2014, offering a wide range of simple, reliable, and secure crypto products and services to individuals and institutions in over 70 countries. Our mission is to unlock the next era of financial, creative, and personal freedom by providing trusted access to the decentralized future. We envision a world where crypto reshapes the global financial system, internet, and money to create greater choice, independence, and opportunity for all — bridging traditional finance with the emerging cryptoeconomy in a way that is more open, fair, and secure. As a publicly traded company, Gemini is poised to accelerate this vision with greater scale, reach, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Department: Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Predictions Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Marketing Lead&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building out our Predictions product and are creating a new team to lead our partnerships program. We&#39;re looking for a Predictions Partnerships Lead to own our relationships with the traders and distribution partners that make our predictions markets tradable. This is a highly visible role at the center of our Predictions roadmap.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone who&#39;s genuinely fluent in how prediction markets work under the hood — trending contracts, liquidity, marketplace dynamics — and who also knows how to hold a real relationship with ecosystem partners. You&#39;ll spend your time identifying prospective partners, leading outreach and relationship-building, and helping turn conversations into active partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high impact role with real ownership. At its core, it&#39;s what you make of it — built for a high agency, mission driven operator who wants to set the strategy, level the team up, and win with a team that actually keeps score.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re chronically online, a builder, or someone who just hates losing, you&#39;ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is required to be in person twice a week at our New York City, NY office.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and evaluate partnership opportunities across predictions ecosystem of market makers, data providers, traders, and distribution partners that expand brand awareness of Gemini’s Predictions product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure partnership terms in collaboration with legal, finance, and compliance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage onboarding, integration and activity of partners in close cross-functional partnership with Engineering, Product, Compliance, and Operations. Act as the escalation point for any issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep, current view of the competitive landscape and translate that into actionable strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in Partnerships, preferably in crypto or an emerging technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building partner programs or ambassador ecosystems from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real fluency with Prediction markets including trading behavior, order books, market-making mechanics, and how liquidity actually gets built on an exchange&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading commercial terms and working with legal/compliance to finalize agreements and onboard new partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills — able to size opportunities, track liquidity/volume performance, and make data-informed prioritization calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently in a fast-paced, evolving regulatory and competitive environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;It Pays to Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;The compensation &amp;amp; benefits package for this role includes:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive starting pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;A discretionary annual bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Long-term incentive in the form of a new hire equity grant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Comprehensive health plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;401K with company matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;: The base salary range for this role is between $129,500 - $185,000 in the State of New York. This range is not inclusive of our discretionary bonus or equity package. When determining a candidate’s compensation, we consider a number of factors including skillset, experience, job scope, and current market data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the United States, we offer a hybrid work approach at our hub offices, balancing the benefits of in-person collaboration with the flexibility of remote work. Expectations may vary by location and role, so candidates are encouraged to connect with their recruiter to learn more about the specific policy for the role. Employees who do not live near one of our hubs are part of our remote workforce. All employees, however, are required to onboard in-person at one of our office locations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Gemini, we strive to build diverse teams that reflect the people we want to empower through our products, and we are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status. Equal Opportunity is the Law, and Gemini is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. If you have a specific need that requires accommodation, please let a member of the People Team know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-GR1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

8091972:
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a hands-on, detail-oriented HR Generalist to join our Global HR team in Munich. You’ll support employees and managers across Germany and Luxembourg, while contributing to HR operations across the UK and wider EMEA region as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Global HR Business Partner&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll own the day-to-day delivery of core HR processes—from onboarding and employment changes to benefits, leave and offboarding. You’ll help create a consistent, responsive employee experience while ensuring our processes, systems and records remain accurate, compliant and scalable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be a trusted first point of contact for employees and managers, providing practical guidance on policies and routine HR matters. You’ll use sound judgement to resolve day-to-day queries independently and involve the appropriate HR Business Partner, specialist team or Legal partner when matters carry greater complexity or risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a varied, operational role for someone who enjoys taking ownership, improving how things work and collaborating across countries and functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;HR Operations and the Employee Lifecycle&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own employee lifecycle processes across Germany and Luxembourg, including onboarding, probation reviews, internal transfers, promotions, contractual changes and offboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare accurate, locally compliant employment documentation, including contracts, amendments, confirmation letters and employee correspondence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track lifecycle events and required actions, ensuring they are completed accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain complete and accurate personnel files in line with local requirements and Spire standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a first point of contact for employees and managers, providing clear, timely guidance on policies, processes and routine HR matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support HR Business Partners with the implementation and administration of employee and organisational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify complex employee relations, performance, organisational change or employment-law matters and escalate them appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits, Equity and Leave&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the day-to-day administration of employee benefits across Germany and Luxembourg.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with external benefits providers and Spire’s Total Rewards team to resolve queries and maintain an effective employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support benefit renewals, enrolment activity and employee communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help administer employee equity and share plans, coordinating documentation, communications and HR processes with the Global Total Rewards team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate statutory and company leave, including maternity, parental leave, sickness absence and other country-specific entitlements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide employees and managers through benefit and leave processes, escalating complex or exceptional cases when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;HR Systems and Data&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate employee data in Rippling and related HR systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular audits to identify and resolve gaps or inconsistencies in employee records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce routine reports and support audit, compliance and information requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain HR templates, employee documentation and shared repositories with appropriate version control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to routine HR system queries and coordinate the resolution of technical or configuration issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support HR system implementations, enhancements and opportunities to improve employee and manager self-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Payroll Coordination&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Payroll with accurate, timely information relating to new hires, leavers, compensation changes, leave and other employee updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review payroll inputs and supporting data within agreed deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll to investigate and resolve routine employee data or payroll queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate discrepancies or more complex payroll matters to the appropriate team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compliance and Regional HR Administration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer HR processes in accordance with employment requirements, Spire policies and established procedures across Germany and Luxembourg.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support local compliance activities, including mandatory employment documentation, statutory reporting, personnel records and works council information requirements where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate immigration and work-authorisation documentation when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audits and compliance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain employee information and HR documentation in accordance with GDPR and internal governance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Spire’s global HR processes consistently while ensuring documented local requirements and country-specific practices are followed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognise potential employment-law, employee relations or compliance risks and involve the appropriate HR Business Partner or Legal partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Process Improvement and Global Programmes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify, automate and standardise HR processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain process documentation, standard operating procedures and employee or manager guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the rollout of HR policies, templates, systems and global initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to annual programmes such as compensation reviews, performance cycles and employee engagement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in cross-functional projects supporting Spire’s continued growth across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use recurring employee and manager queries to identify opportunities for clearer guidance, stronger processes and improved self-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Essential Experience and Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3–5 years of experience in an HR Generalist, People Operations or HR Operations role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have practical experience supporting employees and managers in Germany, with a sound working knowledge of German employment practices and HR compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are professionally proficient in both German and English, with strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand HR administration across the full employee lifecycle and can manage processes accurately from start to finish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience administering employee benefits and statutory or company leave.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have coordinated HR inputs with Payroll and are comfortable working to fixed payroll deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are confident using an HRIS such as Rippling, Workday, HiBob, BambooHR or a similar platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly organised, attentive to detail and comfortable managing competing priorities in a fast-paced, international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership, follow through on commitments and look for practical ways to improve how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You handle sensitive employee information with discretion and sound judgement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can distinguish between matters you can resolve independently and those requiring support from an HR Business Partner, specialist team or Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Desirable Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting employees or HR processes in Luxembourg.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across the UK or multiple EMEA jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to employee equity or share-plan administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with payroll providers and external benefits vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global technology, aerospace or similarly fast-moving organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting HR audits, systems implementations or process-improvement projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spire operates a hybrid work model, and this position will require you to work a minimum of three days per week in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun CommentHighlightClicked SCXW152905918 BCX0&quot;&gt;Access to US export-controlled software and/or technology may be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun CommentHighlightClicked SCXW152905918 BCX0&quot;&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun CommentHighlightClicked SCXW152905918 BCX0&quot;&gt; for this role. If needed, Spire will arrange the necessary licenses—this is not something candidates need to have before applying. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-MK1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Global Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛰️ Name Your Satellite Program (NYSP)&lt;br&gt;🚀 Launch Attendance&lt;br&gt;🌴 Generous Time Off Policy&lt;br&gt;🎓 Education Assistance Program&lt;br&gt;🥰 Employee Assistance Program (EAP)&lt;br&gt;📈 Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;br&gt;👣 Family Leave&lt;br&gt;💪 Fitness Reimbursement&lt;br&gt;🧡 Employee Referral Program&lt;br&gt;🍉 Healthy snacks &amp;amp; beverages in every office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Spire&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;improve life on Earth with data from space.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spire Global is a space-to-cloud analytics company that owns and operates the largest multi-purpose constellation of satellites. Its proprietary data and algorithms provide the most advanced maritime, aviation, and weather tracking in the world. In addition to its constellation, Spire’s data infrastructure includes a global ground station network and 24/7 operations that provide real-time global coverage of every point on Earth.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spire is Global and our success draws upon the diverse viewpoints, skills and experiences of our employees. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, gender identity or veteran status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;To help &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;maintain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt; a safe and secure workplace for Spire employees, all candidates who receive a conditional offer will &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;be required&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;to complete a background check&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;. This &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;may include criminal history and employment verification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please take a moment to review &lt;a href=&quot;https://spire.com/global-data-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;Spire&#39;s Global Data Privacy Notice for Employees, Contractors, Candidates and Visitors&lt;/a&gt;, as well as&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spire.com/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;Spire&#39;s Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kindly be advised that communication regarding your application may come from @spire.com, @recruiting.spire.com, or from Candidate.fyi (our scheduling tool).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8092304:
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for an outstanding transactional lawyer to join our commercial legal team supporting our fast-growing business in EMEA. We are committed to building an inclusive work environment where all Stripes feel welcomed as their authentic selves—inclusive of all genders, sexual orientations, ethnicities, races, education, ages, and other personal characteristics. We work on broadening our internal diversity because we want to be culturally equipped to build products and solutions for our diverse user base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a core member of our Commercial Legal team, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to build strategic relationships with regional sales leaders. You&#39;ll act as a force multiplier, directly influencing the growth of Stripe&#39;s business in EMEA. We trust you to exercise independent judgement and encourage you to bring forward ideas for scaling and streamlining our contracting process. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to develop your legal knowledge and technical skills working at the frontier of payments and fintech innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the EMEA sales team, leading negotiations and advising on a wide range of commercial and legal issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an integral part of the build out of Stripe&#39;s commercial legal infrastructure so that we can scale and operate efficiently at pace with Stripe&#39;s exponential growth—this work includes drafting and maintaining Stripe&#39;s agreements and playbooks, leading and contributing to projects to improve internal processes and operational efficiencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with teams across Stripe, including sales, privacy, operations, product, tax, and risk groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver training and other resources to help the Sales team sell our products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a point of escalation for outside counsel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant experience as a lawyer in-house or in a technology practice group in a top law firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectually curious and a creative problem solver—Stripe&#39;s products and our industry are complex and ever evolving—you relish learning new things and finding creative solutions to challenging problems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter with a bias for action—you&#39;re proactive and have a strong sense of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear and concise communicator (in written and verbal forms), who distills the key risks and explains complex, nuanced issues in plain and simple terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural collaborator, able to guide cross-functional teams and drive to a win-win solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with the range of legal issues and commercial risks that arise in connection with hosted data and technology services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player who is willing to do what it takes to contribute to the collective success &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in French and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in payment or fintech industries and knowledge of associated regulatory issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience advising high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working knowledge of relevant data protection and AI regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8092408:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To thrive as a company and meet our impact goals, we must cultivate a culture of high-performance. You can read about our culture principles &lt;a href=&quot;https://guild.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know managers are often the single-largest driver of employee satisfaction and growth, and our talent is our biggest asset. Because of that, we’ve identified consistent expectations for all of &lt;a href=&quot;https://guild.com/careers/people-manager-expectations&quot;&gt;Guild’s people managers&lt;/a&gt; —&amp;nbsp;helping you know what to expect from your experience here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are an Internal Candidate, please apply via our &lt;a href=&quot;../../internal_job_board&quot;&gt;Internal Job Board&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;----&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Guild is hiring a Senior Compensation Manager. This role plays an integral part on the Total Rewards team, helping build and scale Guild’s compensation function to align with our employee value proposition, keep Guild in compliance, and partner with internal stakeholders on strategic compensation matters. Our compensation programs are core to the Total Rewards team’s mission of ensuring employees feel valued and rewarded for their contributions, and this role offers the chance to do that work in a fast-paced, ever-changing environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As Senior Compensation Manager, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the annual compensation cycles, including planning tool setup, data analysis, reporting, troubleshooting, and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform complex analysis of salary ranges to ensure they remain competitive, recommending consolidation and updates as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design of equity-related compensation and stock option administration, including monthly equity grant analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage job evaluation, job family creation, and salary survey benchmarking, including participating in surveys and analyzing results and trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key collaborator on sales incentive plan design and administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Business Partners and the Talent team on compensation-related processes, approvals, questions, and company-wide education.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain compensation technology, and partner with the People Operations team to keep systems and HRIS data accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for process improvement and represent the Compensation team on cross-functional People and company project teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a strong fit for this role if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of compensation principles, including salary structures, equity compensation, and incentive program design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret complex compensation data and translate it into actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of compensation-related compliance, regulations, and reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and implementing compensation and equity programs and policies, including incentive plan design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively across HR teams and management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CCP, CEP, or SHRM certification (SPHR or SHRM-SCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in HR, Finance, or Analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Excel and Google Sheets, with the ability to build complex data models for compensation analysis and market trend forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to equal pay for equal work and believe in compensation transparency. All salary ranges are standardized nationwide and will not vary by region. This role offers a competitive total compensation package, including a base salary of &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;$150,000 - $180,500&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; and stock options. Compensation offered will be based on a combination of factors such as experience, competencies, and internal equity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Date&lt;/strong&gt;: July 30th, 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*This role will stay open for a minimum of 3 days.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Guild partners with the country’s most innovative employers, including Chipotle, Target, Walgreens, JPMorgan Chase, Hilton, Spectrum, PepsiCo, Tyson, and more, to build the talent needed for today and a resilient workforce for tomorrow. Guild helps employers identify, develop, and mobilize internal talent, enabling workers to gain skills for in-demand roles and companies to stay agile.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By connecting employees to real-world learning, coaching, and career support, and providing companies with actionable talent insights, Guild transforms all talent into high-impact contributors and positions companies for long-term, sustainable growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.guild.com&quot;&gt;https://www.guild.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guild is a female-founded, certified B Corp. The company has been recognized by Fortune’s Change the World list (2021, 2025), the Forbes Cloud 100 (2020–2025), Great Place to Work (2022–2025), CNBC’s Disruptor 50 (2021–2024), TIME’s 100 Most Influential Companies (2022), Inc.’s Best-Led Companies (2021), Fast Company’s World Changing Ideas (2020), and B Lab’s Best for the World (2019), among many others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guild is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let your recruiter know. We currently offer the following benefits:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to low-cost, high-quality health care options through Collective Health and Kaiser (due to coverage limitations, Kaiser is currently only available in CA &amp;amp; CO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a 401k to help save for the future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vacation policy to rest and recharge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 days of fully-paid sick leave, to take the time to heal and or recover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-friendly benefits, including 12 weeks of parental leave for non-birthing parents and 18-20 weeks for birthing parents; 2-week ramp-up period for when employees return from a leave of 6 weeks or more; as well as employer-paid short-term and long-term disability, employer-sponsored life insurance, fertility and caregiving benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-rounded wellness benefits including free and low cost mental health resources and financial wellbeing support services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education benefits and tuition assistance to help your future development and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our home and headquarters in Denver, but some of our roles allow for remote work, allowing us to reach the best talent across the US. &lt;strong&gt;Please refer to the job location referenced below the job posting title to determine location.&lt;/strong&gt; Roles based outside of our Denver office can sit in any of the following 32 states: AZ, CA, CO, CT, FL, GA, ID, IL, IN, KS, MA, MD, ME, MI, MN, MO, NC, NH, NJ, NV, NY, OH, OK, OR, PA, SC, TN, TX, UT, VA, WA, WI and Washington D.C. State locations and specifics are subject to change as our hiring requirements shift.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIVACY NOTICE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I understand that I am applying for employment with Guild and am being asked to provide information in connection with my application. I further understand that Guild gathers this information through a third-party service provider and that Guild may use other service providers to assist in the application process. Guild may share my information with such third-party service providers in connection with my application and for the start of employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;I understand and agree to Guild&#39;s use of my information in accordance with Guild&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://guild.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; and, for applicants that are residents of the State of California, &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.guild.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.guild.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Guild&#39;s Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.guild.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/#ca-privacy-rights&quot;&gt;California Notice at Collection&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8092411:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace team’s mission is to create and support work environments that are welcoming, comfortable, and intuitive. These spaces are designed to promote collaboration, well-being, and productivity while adhering to the rigorous safety, security, and confidentiality standards required of a financial services company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Experience team comprises hospitality-focused professionals who partner with the business to shape the daily experiences of Stripes, visitors, and candidates across 20+ global office locations. This geographically dispersed team oversees facilities management, daily operations, and local workplace programs, including events and onsites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic leader and experienced manager with a high EQ who&#39;s enthusiastic about, and has a driving need to deliver, the best possible workplace experience for Stripes. You&#39;ll be a key member of our Experience team and responsible for ensuring that workplace operations, experiences, facilities, and programs run smoothly at our New York office. As a business partner, you have a deep understanding of the needs, experiences, and day-to-day realities of Stripes at your location and build strong relationships not only with site leads but also with cross-functional partners across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a high level of expertise and operational oversight—from understanding how the building functions top to bottom to governance of contractor team performance and ensuring financial accountability. A key part of the role is anticipating the needs of the business by understanding both the site and the broader context of company growth. You&#39;ll gather and synthesize feedback from multiple sources to ensure the workplace strategy is informed by real insights from the ground. While enterprise workplace strategy is developed centrally, you&#39;re expected to bring informed recommendations based on local business needs and operational insight, and to own successful implementation and adoption at your site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note this role requires an in office presence of 4 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace operations at your site(s), providing direction on all workplace services, including building operations, front of house, shipping and receiving, events support, and employee health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound, independent operational decisions by balancing business impact, risk, cost, and employee experience, seeking alignment when decisions create broader organizational impact or precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and motivate a team of workplace services professionals, providing direction, coaching, and performance management to drive team excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, including senior leadership, department heads, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong rapport with locally assigned Stripes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance for your site by monitoring service levels and utilization, identifying trends, resolving root causes, and driving continuous improvement across workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate business needs by understanding both local context and company priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful, data-informed recommendations that help shape workplace programs and experiences while maintaining alignment with global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workplace partners and service providers accountable for performance, ensuring contractual obligations, service levels, and operational standards are consistently achieved while driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our Finance &amp;amp; Strategy partner and IFM partner to develop and oversee the opex budget for all facilities, opex, fixed assets, and events of the NYC office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the local site leadership team to activate the office by creating engagement, connection, and an inclusive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft relevant communications and documentation regarding Workplace policies and programs for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of global workplace programs, standards, and policies at your site,&amp;nbsp; as developed by our Food, Space Planning, and Programs teams, adapting implementation to local operational requirements while maintaining alignment with enterprise objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Workplace team&#39;s goals by taking on ad hoc tasks and projects as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in workplace/hospitality management in a fast-paced environment with a strong customer service orientation and an understanding of operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong demonstrated ability in facilities management, vendor, and budget management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strength in building relationships with key internal partners to ensure efficiency and understanding on cross-functional projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team focused on customer service, hospitality, and operations, with the ability and desire to develop and coach your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize operational data, stakeholder feedback, and business context into clear recommendations that support sound decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite, Slack and Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and translate enterprise strategy into effective local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, digging into problems to understand the root cause and delivering scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a fast-paced workplace with rapidly changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8092416:
&lt;p&gt;Flow Traders is looking for a Compliance Officer to join our Compliance team in New York. The ideal candidate is self-motivated with a strong analytical and problem-solving mentality. This is a unique opportunity to join a leading proprietary trading firm with an entrepreneurial and innovative culture at the heart of its business. We value quick-witted, creative minds and challenge them to make full use of their capacities. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This Compliance Officer will play a central role in the Know Your Customer (“KYC”) / Anti-Money Laundering (“AML”) program as well as the firm&#39;s employee compliance program. Responsibilities span reviewing and onboarding institutional counterparties, investigating alerts across a wide range of risk areas including personal trading, sanctions and negative news, electronic communications, and exchange registrations, and supporting the full lifecycle of employee compliance obligations. This position offers broad exposure across the compliance function, close collaboration with the Chief Compliance Officer (“CCO”), and the opportunity to help shape and strengthen policies and procedures as the firm grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, review, and document new institutional counterparty onboardings and periodic updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and investigate compliance alerts across a broad range of areas including personal trading, sanctions/negative news, electronic communications, and exchange registrations, among others — documenting findings in clear, well-supported case notes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage employee access to third-party trading, clearing, and compliance platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the broader employee compliance program, including in the areas of employee onboardings/terminations, personal trading, outside business activities, gifts and entertainment, political contributions, exchange registrations, social media, electronic communications, and continuing education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the implementation and dissemination of Written Supervisory Procedures, identifying opportunities to strengthen the compliance program and promoting a culture of compliance across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the CCO with day-to-day functions and compliance projects, including shared ownership of global Compliance initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you need to succeed&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three years of relevant experience in AML/KYC and/or broker-dealer compliance strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate degree in Finance, Economics, or Business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mature, professional, and of unquestionable integrity, exercising excellent judgment when handling sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing skills, with the ability to translate facts and analysis into clear, well-organized case notes and alert documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills with high attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-based approach to problem-solving, with the ability to develop informed and concrete proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated self-starter who can manage competing priorities and thrive in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with third-party vendors such as World-Check One, ACA ComplianceAlpha, Salesforce, Smarsh, Bloomberg Vault, and Microsoft Purview, a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and/or SQL, a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flow Traders, we acknowledge the importance of open and transparent communication whether it be with our employees, our stakeholders, or our local and global communities. When it comes to salary, Flow Traders uses reliable market research to create base ranges. Where candidates will fall within the range depends on a few different factors including but not limited to level of experience, location, and specific skill set. We also consider ourselves one global team, and to demonstrate that, all employees are eligible to share in the company’s success through an annual discretionary variable remuneration allocated based on company, group and individual performance and contribution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Per NYC salary transparency law, the total compensation for this role includes a base range of $95,000 to $130,000 plus annual discretionary variable remuneration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MM1&lt;/p&gt;

8092485:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;The Stablecoin team builds and operates Coinbase Custom Stablecoins (CCS), the platform that lets partners launch their own branded, USDC-backed stablecoins on Coinbase&#39;s infrastructure. As a Software Engineer on this team within the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Developer&lt;/a&gt; group, you&#39;ll build and extend the backend services and onchain contracts that power issuance, reserves, minting and burning, and rewards distribution for a fast-growing roster of partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and extend smart contract functionality for minting, burning, and safeguarding custom stablecoin supply, working closely with senior engineers on design and security review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement backend services that power onboarding, issuance, reserve accounting, and rewards distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineers, designers, and product managers to turn the stablecoin roadmap into shipped features every quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reporting, monitoring, and internal tooling that improve reliability and operational excellence for the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write high-quality, well-tested code across both backend and smart contract surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience building and maintaining production backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to writing, testing, or deploying smart contracts (Solidity or similar EVM languages), or demonstrated ability to ramp quickly in new technical domains with mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working within a service-oriented architecture and contributing to established systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Golang and blockchain fundamentals (Ethereum or similar EVM chains).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates the ability to responsibly use generative AI tools and copilots (e.g., LibreChat, Gemini, Glean) in daily workflows, continuously learn as tools evolve, and apply human‑in‑the‑loop practices to deliver business‑ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
