8100129:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Enterprise Sales team partners with over 50% of the Fortune 500 companies in North America, helping them build new business models and drive meaningful modernization. The East Coast region is one of our highest-concentration markets for strategic accounts and new logo opportunities across all industries with a concentration in fintech, media, financial services, retail, and travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Enterprise Sales for the East Coast, you&#39;ll own regional revenue delivery and team performance, working closely with our Americas Enterprise leadership on strategy while driving execution on the ground. You&#39;ll lead a team of Regional Sales Directors and their Account Executives, shaping this team to focus on industry-led motions, and you&#39;ll serve as the region’s GTM executive with our most important customers in Stripe’s New York office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own East Coast Enterprise revenue: new logo growth, expansion of existing accounts, and accurate forecasting across your region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of Regional Sales Directors and their AEs, setting high standards for performance, pipeline discipline, and customer engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry executive relationships with strategic accounts and step into key deals to accelerate outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Americas-level strategy into regional plans, priorities, and hiring decisions that reflect local market dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Solutions Architecture to bring the right resources to your largest opportunities and surface customer signal that shapes Stripe&#39;s roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and reinforce the industry-first motion, sales process, the Stripe Way methodology, and forecasting practices your team runs on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbook for consumption-based, API-driven enterprise sales in your region, and share what works across the broader team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As the Regional Sales Leader, you will lead a team of Regional Sales Directors and their Enterprise Account Executive teams, with direct management of RSDs and shared accountability for the broader supporting functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision and operating rhythm for the East Coast region, balancing long-term team development with near-term execution and forecasting discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and reinforce Stripe&#39;s sales methodology across your team, setting the standard for pipeline quality, deal progression, and forecast accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the repeatable practices your team needs to hit revenue targets and grow, then share what works with the broader Americas Enterprise organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step personally into the largest strategic deals, leading executive relationships and helping your team close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customer and market signal back into Stripe, working with Product, Engineering, and Marketing to influence roadmap priorities based on what you&#39;re seeing in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you do, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in enterprise technology sales, including 7+ years managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering revenue results at scale in a high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and hiring senior sales talent across multiple markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills: you&#39;re comfortable in the numbers and use data to drive decisions and hold the team accountable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage credibly at the C-suite level with complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling developer platforms, APIs, or financial infrastructure to enterprise buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in payments, fintech, or adjacent financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up new sales coverage in a region or market from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8100160:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;374&quot; data-end=&quot;399&quot;&gt;About the team + role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;401&quot; data-end=&quot;843&quot;&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;845&quot; data-end=&quot;1229&quot;&gt;The Android team’s mission is to redefine how millions of users engage with their finances. We&#39;re focused on delivering intuitive, scalable, and inclusive mobile experiences that empower our customers to build better financial futures. We collaborate closely with Product, Design, and Backend Engineering to ensure every interaction on Android reflects quality, performance, and care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntt _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Crypto expansion team &lt;/strong&gt;is building Robinhood products for new regions, extending crypto and adjacent financial experiences to customers around the world. The team owns all critical parts of the app across onboarding, funding, account setup, trading product integrations, and platform capabilities required to operate in new jurisdictions. This team sits at the intersection of building an internationalization platform and region specific product execution, to help Robinhood be successful in new markets. Recent work in expansion effort has included Canada, Europe launches with multi-currency wallet capabilities, local funding rails, translations infrastructure, and new onboarding experiences for each region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntt _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Android Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; on the Crypto Expansions team, you’ll help launch Robinhood’s crypto and adjacent financial products in new regions by building critical Android experiences end to end. You’ll work across onboarding, local funding rails, account setup, multi-currency wallet capabilities, trading surfaces, and translations infrastructure, balancing region-specific execution with long-term platform thinking. You’ll play a key role in delivering reliable, intuitive mobile experiences that make Robinhood successful in global markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1491&quot; data-end=&quot;1596&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA OR New York, NY office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1598&quot; data-end=&quot;1824&quot;&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;1826&quot; data-end=&quot;1829&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1831&quot; data-end=&quot;1849&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1852&quot; data-end=&quot;1964&quot;&gt;Build intuitive, elegant, and stable mobile experiences using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and modern Android APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1967&quot; data-end=&quot;2089&quot;&gt;Lead the full lifecycle of product features — from ideation and technical design to implementation, testing, and release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2092&quot; data-end=&quot;2216&quot;&gt;Collaborate closely with Product Managers, Designers, Backend Engineers, and Data Scientists to create impactful solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2219&quot; data-end=&quot;2315&quot;&gt;Champion engineering best practices that ensure code quality, scalability, and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2318&quot; data-end=&quot;2394&quot;&gt;Mentor junior developers and help elevate team standards and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;2396&quot; data-end=&quot;2399&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2401&quot; data-end=&quot;2419&quot;&gt;What you bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2422&quot; data-end=&quot;2491&quot;&gt;6+ years of professional experience developing Android applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2494&quot; data-end=&quot;2602&quot;&gt;Proficiency with Kotlin and/or Java, and a strong grasp of Android SDK and architecture patterns like MVVM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2605&quot; data-end=&quot;2709&quot;&gt;Experience using Jetpack Compose, Coroutines &amp;amp; Flow or RxJava, and libraries such as Retrofit and Room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2712&quot; data-end=&quot;2790&quot;&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills with a product-focused mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2793&quot; data-end=&quot;2892&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to mentor peers, lead complex projects, and influence architecture decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2895&quot; data-end=&quot;2959&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;2961&quot; data-end=&quot;2964&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2966&quot; data-end=&quot;2983&quot;&gt;What we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2986&quot; data-end=&quot;3037&quot;&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3040&quot; data-end=&quot;3165&quot;&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3168&quot; data-end=&quot;3276&quot;&gt;Best-in-class benefits including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3279&quot; data-end=&quot;3376&quot;&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3379&quot; data-end=&quot;3469&quot;&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3472&quot; data-end=&quot;3554&quot;&gt;Generous time off including company holidays, PTO, sick time, and parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3557&quot; data-end=&quot;3648&quot;&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, stocked kitchens, and commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
