8109607:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We have significant work ahead, which creates an opportunity to do meaningful, high-impact work with colleagues and users around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s New Zealand business is growing, and we are building our enterprise new-business capability in the market. The Enterprise team focuses on winning and developing relationships with New Zealand’s largest and most strategic companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive, New Business, you will establish and grow a new enterprise territory. You will identify must-win accounts, build a high-conviction pipeline, develop executive relationships, and lead complex sales cycles that help prospective users use Stripe to modernise and grow their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory strategy for New Zealand’s largest prospective enterprise users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create new pipeline through thoughtful outbound prospecting, account research, partner engagement, executive networking, and targeted account plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full new-business sales cycle, from initial outreach and discovery through solution design, commercial negotiation, close, and transition to implementation and post-sales teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with senior business and technical stakeholders, including leaders across Finance, Product, Engineering, Operations, Digital, and Technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex, multi-threaded sales processes involving multiple business units, decision-makers, and internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulate Stripe’s business and technical value across the platform, connecting customer priorities to measurable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Solutions Architects, Product, Partnerships, Marketing, Legal, Deal Pricing, and post-sales teams to develop and close strategic opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial negotiations for complex and bespoke agreements while protecting long-term customer value and Stripe economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build account plans, mutual action plans, financial analyses, and executive-level presentations that advance opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish and refine Stripe’s enterprise sales motion in New Zealand by sharing market insight, improving messaging, and contributing to repeatable sales practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a high-performing enterprise seller who thrives in new-business environments. You know how to open doors at large organisations, earn credibility with senior stakeholders, and lead complex sales cycles from ambiguity to a clear commercial outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are commercially rigorous, technically curious, and persistent. You can balance strategic account planning with the day-to-day discipline needed to build pipeline and maintain momentum across long sales cycles. You are comfortable operating with autonomy and enjoy building a territory where there is substantial opportunity to define the playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Sales experience with at least 3+ in&amp;nbsp; enterprise new-business sales, ideally in complex B2B software, cloud, fintech, payments, or technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success opening and closing net-new enterprise customers, with a clear record of meeting or exceeding sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing a territory or greenfield account strategy, including defining target accounts, creating pipeline, and building executive relationships from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles involving technical, financial, operational, and executive buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience selling to senior leaders, including CFO, CIO, CTO, COO, Chief Product Officer, and other executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead sophisticated commercial negotiations, including bespoke agreements and cross-functional approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and executing account plans across complex organisations with multiple business units and decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgement, analytical capability, and ability to connect product capabilities to customer business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment with high ownership and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be based in Auckland, with travel across New Zealand as required and occasional international travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling at a leading enterprise software, cloud, or platform company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling payments, financial infrastructure, fintech, or other technically complex platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into large New Zealand or ANZ enterprise organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth technology company where territory strategy, messaging, and sales processes were still being developed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with technical pre-sales, product, partnerships, and implementation teams on enterprise opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8109753:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Privacy Engineering team’s mission is to protect the trust of our customers by embedding privacy into every layer of Robinhood’s technology and culture. We collaborate across Engineering, Product, Legal, and Compliance to make sure privacy, data governance, and security are integral to every initiative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Privacy Engineer, you’ll lead privacy reviews, guide the design of privacy-enhancing technologies, and help scale our privacy-by-design programs — while also championing the use of AI and agentic tooling to transform how the team runs privacy operations and processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our New York, NY office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct detailed privacy architecture reviews to identify potential risks, recommend controls, and ensure privacy-by-design is built into every technical layer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Product, Legal, and Compliance to implement privacy-by-design in systems, applications, and workflows from inception to launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and use AI agents and sub-agents to automate and scale privacy operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the selection and deployment of privacy-enhancing technologies (PETs), ensuring alignment with our technical architecture and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise stakeholders and adjust practices to maintain compliance in alignment with development in global privacy regulations, standards, and technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal efforts to share best practices and increase awareness of privacy principles across engineering and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Cybersecurity, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring 2+ years of experience in data privacy, security, or privacy engineering, including hands-on work with privacy architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re highly proficient with AI, with hands-on experience building and utilizing agents and sub-agents to solve real operational or technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed both technical and operational processes at the same time, and know how to prioritize when things move fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re familiar with regulatory frameworks like GLBA, GDPR and CCPA and understand how to apply them to technical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked with privacy-enhancing technologies and understand data anonymization and secure data lifecycle practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a clear communicator who builds strong cross-functional partnerships, including with legal teams, and can explain complex technical topics to both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$157,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$185,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$139,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$122,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$144,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8110122:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer on the RippleX Platform Engineering team, you’ll play a critical role in ensuring the reliability, scalability, and security of XRPL infrastructure. The Platform team operates at the intersection of software engineering, infrastructure, and operations—managing critical services, public test environments, and internal developer tooling. With strong foundations in DevOps and GitOps, the team is focused on delivering fully automated, highly available, and cost-efficient systems that enable developer velocity and protect the health of the XRPL ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll drive the design and development of platform components and infrastructure services that support distributed, high-throughput systems. You’ll help evolve core systems through automation, monitoring, and incident response, while influencing technical direction and mentoring other engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable and resilient infrastructure supporting production-grade XRPL services and public blockchain networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation for infrastructure lifecycle, CI/CD workflows, and deployment pipelines using tools like Terraform, Helm, and GitHub Actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop systems and services that support observability, secret management, disaster recovery, and regional failover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve platform reliability through proactive instrumentation, alerting, and incident response in collaboration with observability and security teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and maintain internal tooling, self-service workflows, and platform capabilities that support developer efficiency and service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new tools to improve infrastructure scalability and reduce manual overhead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field—or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional experience, including 2+ years operating cloud-native infrastructure at scale (AWS/GCP preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Go, Python, or Java, with a deep understanding of Linux systems, networking, and concurrency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with Kubernetes (EKS or similar), container runtimes (Docker/OCI), and service meshes (Istio, Linkerd, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building CI/CD pipelines and deploying infrastructure using GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in Infrastructure-as-Code (e.g., Terraform, Helm, Ansible) and related automation practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with distributed systems monitoring and observability using Prometheus, Grafana, or equivalent tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and collaboration skills—able to align technical execution across teams while mentoring and developing talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and problem-solving abilities, with a focus on driving outcomes in complex and evolving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;For positions that will be based in CA, the annual salary range for this position is below. Actual salaries may vary based on numerous factors including, among other things, an individual applicant’s experience and qualifications for the position. This range does not include equity or additional compensation, such as bonuses or commissions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA Annual Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ripple is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We do not discriminate against qualified employees or applicants because of race, color, religion, gender identity, sex, sexual identity, pregnancy, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, military status, or any other characteristic protected by local law or ordinance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please find our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/eu-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UK/EU Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/a&gt;and our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/ca-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for reference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8110261:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive covering strategic accounts, you’ll manage existing relationships and identify new opportunities to expand Stripe’s footprint within existing accounts. Specifically, we’re looking for someone who can execute on long-term sales strategies, engage with internal and external stakeholders, align on technical and business requirements with product teams, build value in competitive situations, lead commercial negotiations, and close deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work strategic Stripe customers to develop and execute long-term sales strategies to expand Stripe’s revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand business with high growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop outbound strategies to create and nurture opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large, complex renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders within your book of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for account mapping and coordinating effective meetings with the appropriate external stakeholders expanding the customer relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects to develop and refine our sales process and help shape the Stripe sales culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a highly technical product to enterprise customers, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and execute account plans spanning multiple business units across complex organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working well with a wide range of people, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8110416:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AMER Startups Sales team is responsible for Stripe&#39;s fastest-growing customer segment, the companies that will become the platforms, networks, and enterprises of the future. You will be tackling the &quot;founder&#39;s dilemma&quot; at scale: how do we maintain the intimacy of a 1:1 relationship with thousands of companies, while building highly intelligent systems that scale? Startups represent a disproportionate share of Stripe&#39;s long-term value, and this team ensures those relationships deepen over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;As Head of Startup Sales (Grower), you will lead the organization responsible for growing and expanding Stripe&#39;s relationships with thousands of startup accounts post-activation. This is an expansion engine for the highly strategic Startups segment. Your teams will drive multi-product adoption, identify and act on growth signals, and build coverage models calibrated for the unique economics of high-growth startups.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a second-line leader managing frontline managers across multiple specialized sub-teams, each with distinct operating rhythms and coverage ratios. You&#39;ll partner cross-functionally with product specialists, solutions architects, customer success, and marketing to build the motions that turn early-stage activations into deep, multi-product platform relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Head of Startups.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the long-term vision and operating model for Startup (Grower), building specialized sub-teams with distinct charters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive multi-product expansion across a large portfolio of accounts at varying stages of growth, from pre-PMF through rapid scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operationalize structured expansion cadences, ensuring every high-potential account has a product-attach strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design coverage models that balance high-touch investment on the highest-growth accounts with signal-driven, AI-augmented coverage at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product specialist teams (billing, treasury, platform products) to build co-sell motions that compound revenue across the Stripe platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the systems that detect breakout accounts accelerating within the portfolio, and ensure they receive the right coverage at the right moment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make hiring decisions, refine ideal candidate profiles by sub-team, and build a team development engine that grows AEs from early-career through senior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design comp and incentive structures that reward expansion and product depth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the forecasting and pipeline operating rhythm for a segment with unique leading and lagging indicators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally across Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Operations to shape Stripe&#39;s startup experience and influence roadmap priorities based on what you hear from customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a candidate with proven success scaling tech sales teams, strong analytical and relationship-building skills, and a genuine passion for the startup ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience leading high-growth sales organizations, with 3+ years as a second-line manager, specifically building specialized sub-teams with distinct operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success driving multi-product platform growth through value-based selling, structured expansion funnels, cross-sell motions, and customer lifecycle design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinker with quantitative skills to model portfolio economics, coverage ratios, and signal-driven investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire and develop high-performance AEs across various seniority levels while managing long-horizon economics and compounding returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering cross-functionally with product, specialist overlays, and customer success teams in a complex platform environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with startups as customers, understanding the nature of high-growth companies and require purpose-built coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a high-growth technology or infrastructure company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing comp plans for expansion-focused teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building or leveraging AI/automation to scale coverage beyond linear headcount growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership Style&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a &quot;player-coach&quot; who can zoom into the details of a specific startup’s strategy while simultaneously zooming out to shape our long-term operating rhythm. You ensure the customer remains the north star of everything that we do and that our growth motions genuinely deliver value at every stage of the startup lifecycle.You thrive in high-velocity environments and can lead through influence in a matrixed organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will embody Stripe’s core operating principles in your day-to-day leadership:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User first:&lt;/strong&gt; You will advocate for the startup founder’s experience, ensuring our growth motions and product expansions solve genuine business problems for our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay curious:&lt;/strong&gt; You will constantly seek to understand the evolving startup landscape, experimenting to improve how we serve our fastest-growing segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate egolessly:&lt;/strong&gt; You will work seamlessly across Stripe prioritizing the collective success of the Startups mission over individual or team-specific accolades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8110496:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team/ Role Paragraph:&lt;/strong&gt; The FCM Operations team supports Coinbase Financial Markets, Inc.’s US Futures, Options, and Prediction Markets businesses by managing critical operational workflows, including trade flow and position management, margin monitoring, internal and regulatory reporting, and business analytics. The team also enables new product launches, feature enhancements, and vendor management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a senior individual contributor who can operate at both strategic and execution depth, using technical and regulatory expertise to evolve the FCM operating model. This person will identify where workflows, controls, and tooling may break as the business scales, partner cross-functionally to design better solutions, and drive those solutions through implementation. This role is ideal for a hands-on, product-oriented operator who can translate business complexity into scalable processes, control frameworks, and operational tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously improve the FCM operating model across core workflows including trade flow management, position management, margin monitoring, internal reporting, regulatory reporting support, and business analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and build of scalable operational solutions across people, process, and tooling, with a focus on reducing manual effort, increasing control quality, and improving operational resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and track stability in the environment and across process reliability using data and operational insights.. Provide transparency on health, categorize and prioritize enhancements required and lead to delivery across a high-stakes regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Risk, Accounting, Compliance, Legal, and external partners to shape requirements, influence roadmap priorities, and ensure business needs are translated into practical, well-controlled solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategic initiatives across launch readiness, process redesign, automation, control architecture, vendor tooling, and remediation of operational pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define future-state workflows and ownership models for new products, features, and business expansions, ensuring that operational considerations are embedded early in design rather than addressed after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and elevate documentation, policies, procedures, governance standards, and decision frameworks for critical workflows and strategic changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of listed derivatives, futures operations, and broker-dealer or FCM workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in operations, product operations, business operations, or program leadership in regulated financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on technical knowledge of trade processing systems, books and records, and related infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large-scale transformation initiatives in the listed derivatives ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate autonomously at a senior individual contributor level with both strategic judgment and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record leading ambiguous, cross-functional initiatives and turning them into durable process or tooling improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Product and Engineering to build scalable operating solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, prioritization, communication, and systems-thinking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses generative AI responsibly, with strong human oversight to improve efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Base salary varies by location (see range below). Total compensation may also include equity and bonus eligibility, and benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k)).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual base salary range (excluding equity and bonus):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$201,365&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$236,900 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Application Limit: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Candidates may submit a maximum of 3 applications within a 6-month period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer: &lt;/strong&gt;Coinbase is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. Applicants with criminal histories will be considered consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Applicants: &lt;/strong&gt;View&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WHD/legacy/files/eppac.pdf&quot;&gt; Employee Rights&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt; Know Your Rights&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://static-assets.coinbase.com/e-verify.pdf&quot;&gt; E-Verify&lt;/a&gt; Notice of Participation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations: &lt;/strong&gt;If you are an individual with a disability who needs a reasonable accommodation, email us your request and contact info at accommodations[at]coinbase.com.&amp;nbsp;Need screen reading technology?&lt;a href=&quot;https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/screen-reader/kgejglhpjiefppelpmljglcjbhoiplfn&quot;&gt; Click here&lt;/a&gt; to download a free compatible screen reader and view the&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.chromevox.com/tutorial/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;tutorial&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy &amp;amp; Arbitration: &lt;/strong&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/legal/applicant_privacy_notice&quot;&gt; Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. US applicants: By submitting your application, you agree to&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/legal/application-arbitration-agreement&quot;&gt; Arbitration of Disputes&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8110814:
&lt;p&gt;Flow Traders is looking for an experienced Staff Enterprise Engineer in our Amsterdam office. The ideal candidate is proactive and driven, with a genuine appetite for modernizing and continuously improving our technology estate. This is a unique opportunity to join a leading proprietary trading firm with an entrepreneurial and innovative culture at the heart of its business. We value quick-witted, creative minds and challenge them to make full use of their capacities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior individual contributor within the Enterprise Systems domain, you will define the long-term technical architecture and engineering standards across the estate, including identity, endpoints, compute, virtualization, operating systems, storage, databases, and the platforms beneath our enterprise SaaS. Reporting to the Global Head of IT, you will act as the senior technical authority and a mentor to our engineers, driving automation, engineering best practices, and modernization. This is a hands-on, senior IC role rather than a people-management position: an opportunity to shape technical direction and build, not to manage a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the long-term architecture and engineering standards for Enterprise Systems, covering identity, endpoints, compute, storage, databases, and the foundations supporting enterprise SaaS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior technical authority, mentoring engineers and driving high-quality architecture and design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business and technology challenges into clear technical roadmaps and scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead modernization across identity, endpoint management, compute, and workplace technologies, and make on-premise versus cloud decisions on merit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive automation and self-service capabilities to improve efficiency, resilience, and user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rationalize and optimize the technology landscape, responsibly retiring legacy systems in favor of modern, cost-effective solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the underlying platforms that support enterprise applications, including SSO, provisioning, integrations, and data flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion engineering excellence through rigorous testing, validation, and lab-first deployment practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you need to succeed&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of senior enterprise infrastructure engineering experience at Staff, Principal, or Technical Lead level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in identity and access management, cloud platforms, virtualization, and enterprise infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success leading cloud migrations, legacy platform retirements, and large-scale modernization initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architectural judgment with a vendor-neutral approach to cloud and platform decisions, choosing the right target on merit rather than by default&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating enterprise SaaS platforms through SSO, automated provisioning, APIs, and secure connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with automation, Infrastructure as Code, and applying AI to improve operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence and drive cross-functional alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative technical leader who mentors engineers, raises engineering standards, and thrives as a hands-on individual contributor in a global, multi-region environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we offer&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flow Traders, we create the conditions for hard‑working, high‑performing people to do their best work. From a thorough onboarding and ongoing access to Flow Academy, to latest technology and a collaborative, non‑hierarchical culture, we give you the tools, ownership, and support to move fast and drive outcomes. We keep a close‑knit, small‑company feel while offering competitive salary, annual discretionary profit share, and comprehensive benefits,&amp;nbsp;so talent can grow here, and stay here.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;See our benefits below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flow Academy and opportunities to attend domain-related conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily catered lunch, great coffee, and a fully stocked kitchen and snack bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house Bar and Lounge with arcade, table tennis, billiards, and game consoles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company boat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house gym and sessions with our nutritionist or personal trainer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bi-weekly massages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company trip and a variety of events throughout the year, such as the New Years Event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global rotations across our offices worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

8111799:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe’s user base and global footprint grows dramatically, we have distinctly unique support problems resulting from both our type of scale and the type of businesses we partner with. The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. We strive to deliver frictionless experiences for all of our users, whether they are an Independent Business, Startup, SMB, or Enterprise and our mission is to provide all Stripe Users with the best support experience possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will manage a team of Associates&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; You will act in a player-coach capacity and are accountable for supporting associates in delivering against target set goals and mentoring in subject matter expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing management of the operational performance of your team to deliver KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage capacity and scheduling, dividing and assigning work between team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring your team has all the skills and resources needed to be successful in their role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting clear goals and expectations for individual and team performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement to refine team processes and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support recruitment and hiring initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor individuals for career progression via structured career development conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide continuous performance feedback and facilitate periodic formal performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive and own initiatives that make the team a warm and welcoming place to work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement process improvements that enhance team productivity, reduce manual effort, and improve user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience leading operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal and communications skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exemplary planning and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate effectively with multiple, cross-functional stakeholders to achieve results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience mentoring others and are able to constructively provide feedback to others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to motivate the team and keep them engaged in an otherwise structured process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be subject matter experts in the relevant line of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a team lead or people management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in customer service or internal/external user-facing operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses data to set priorities, track progress, and spot trends before they become problems. Comfortable building or maintaining dashboards and interpreting operational metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brings numbers into conversations naturally and grounding decisions in evidence and making tradeoffs visible, not just reporting what the data says&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8112037:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are experts in business data, building the canonical data foundation that powers decision-making across Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, Business Data Science, GTM, and Marketing. We engineer scalable and efficient data pipelines and provide curated data products that give Stripe&#39;s teams a consistent, accurate, and fresh view of the business—from the top to the bottom of the funnel. We work side by side with partner teams—AI, Data Science, and Business Systems—to deliver high-quality data assets that power growth motions, product performance tracking, and go-to-market metrics reporting. We invest in data quality, data engineering automation, and operational excellence to minimize issues and maintain the trust our customers place in the products we build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a person who could contribute to the team by solving high-impact, cutting-edge data problems. The ideal candidate will be someone that has built data pipelines for large scale volume, is deeply knowledgeable of key tools including Airflow/Spark/Kafka/Flink, is empathetic, excels at building strong relationships, and collaborates effectively with other Stripe teams to understand their use cases and unlock new capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead the technical outcomes for a team of ambitious, talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver cutting-edge data pipelines that scale to users&#39; needs, focusing on reliability and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong subject matter expertise and manage the SLAs of data pipelines and full stack web applications that support critical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and peers across the company to create/improve canonical datasets and data warehouses, use golden paths, and ensure Stripes and customers are using trustworthy data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI/LLM and Agents at scale to produce and analyze high-quality data on ambiguous problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the opportunity to drive the execution of key data initiatives for Stripe, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
