8112184:
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Flow Traders is strengthening leadership across its Research Engineering department and is hiring an Engineering Manager. Research Engineers conduct applied research jointly with quants to deliver our trading models and research platform. As the firm scales, the quality of engineering management has become one of the most important factors in how well our teams grow, retain talent, and deliver - and this role exists to raise that bar.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering Managers are accountable for the planning and people side of the organisation - project deliveries, growth, performance, culture and hiring - and partner with technical leads who own architecture, technical direction, and hands-on execution. The two work in close partnership; neither succeeds without the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be measured on the engineers you develop and the outcomes your team delivers. You will spend the large majority of your time leading people and managing delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Own the roadmap: manage priorities, planning, and sequencing of the work in line with company goals.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Develop your engineers: own career planning, promotions, coaching, and structured, continuous performance management.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Plan and build the team: lead hiring, headcount planning, and resource allocation in line with the team&#39;s roadmap and the firm&#39;s priorities.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cultivate a healthy team: actively manage culture, morale, and productivity, and address conflict early and constructively.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Lead with rhythm: hold regular one-on-ones, give clear and timely feedback, and invest in team building.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Translate technical and business requirements into clear delivery plans, identifying dependencies with other teams and risks up front.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Act as the liaison between Engineering, Trading, and Quant teams to design and roll out new products.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Drive delivery predictability: track progress against plan, manage risk and scope trade-offs, and report status clearly to stakeholders.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Continuously improve delivery processes and team velocity.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ensure alignment: keep your team&#39;s work connected to organisational goals and delivery timelines, collaborating closely with Tech Leads and Staff Engineers on research and technical direction.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;What you need to succeed:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Strong people-leadership skills: coaching, feedback, conflict resolution, and building an environment in which engineers thrive&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Strong project management skills: experience building roadmaps, sequencing work, managing dependencies and risk, and driving delivery predictability in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A technical or research background sufficient to earn the respect of the engineers you manage and to engage credibly in technical discussions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Demonstrated experience leading, growing, and managing the performance of applied researchers and software engineers.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A track record of delivering applied research through a team, balancing scope, quality, and timelines.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Sound judgment in hiring and developing talent.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Excellent communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, including experience managing cross-functional stakeholders (e.g. Trading, Quant).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Based in Amsterdam, or willing to relocate.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8112448:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud Strategy is responsible for building scaled fraud mitigation systems that prevent fraud and protect the financial ecosystem, while minimizing disruption to good users. The fraud team’s mission is to protect Stripe, our users, and the broader financial ecosystem from actors who abuse Stripe accounts for financial gain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Fraud Strategist, you will be responsible for building strategies to mitigate fraud (buyer fraud, seller fraud and account fraud) on new and existing Stripe products. You will enable safer money movement for our users and help Stripe manage fraud risks intelligently. The stakes are high, and you will be up against ever-evolving challenges. You will face some of the most complex and dynamic problems at the company, and the nature of your work will evolve rapidly to combat new and more sophisticated challenges to Stripe&#39;s integrity in the financial ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations and other Risk Strategy functions to ensure fraud controls are embedded in every Stripe product. Beyond protecting against fraud risk, you&#39;ll drive innovation in how Stripe approaches fraud management— staying ahead of emerging fraud trends and pushing the boundaries of what effective, scalable fraud risk management looks like at a global payments company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor portfolio to identify, mitigate and predict risky behavior that could result in losses for Stripe, our users, and the financial ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal partners like Product, Engineering, Data Science, Risk Partnerships, and Operations, to tailor fraud risk management techniques to various products and payment methods across the globe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually evaluate products for gaps and propose risk controls to enhance the product while enabling growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale risk processes to cover a large and complex landscape of fraud risks. Effectively design, outsource and automate manual/repetitive workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Stripe users to educate them and guide them on how to prevent potential fraud risks to their business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively and clearly communicate with other Stripes, Stripe&#39;s users, and Stripe&#39;s financial and regulatory partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;5+ years of relevant experience, preferably in Financial Services, Payments or FinTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Curiosity and passion for risk management - you dig into anomalies and solve root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Decisiveness and openness to learning, with comfort making high-impact calls daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Data-driven judgment - skilled at using quantitative analysis to drive and defend decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Empathy for early-stage businesses and the ability to balance enforcement with user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Strong analytical skills, including the ability to frame complex tradeoffs through data and visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Advanced SQL skills with hands-on experience in business environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Proven ability to collaborate and execute cross-functionally with Engineering, Product, Data Science, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to convey complex ideas clearly across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Holistic thinking and the ability to build scaled processes that bridge systemic gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Track record of deriving actionable insights from complex problem spaces and influencing product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Ownership mentality and the ability to lead without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Proficient with AI tools to accelerate productivity and process automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with quantitative tools such as Python, R, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, risk, or trust &amp;amp; safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with machine learning teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced and rapidly changing start-up environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8112938:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini is a global crypto and Web3 platform founded by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss in 2014, offering a wide range of simple, reliable, and secure crypto products and services to individuals and institutions in over 70 countries. Our mission is to unlock the next era of financial, creative, and personal freedom by providing trusted access to the decentralized future. We envision a world where crypto reshapes the global financial system, internet, and money to create greater choice, independence, and opportunity for all — bridging traditional finance with the emerging cryptoeconomy in a way that is more open, fair, and secure. As a publicly traded company, Gemini is poised to accelerate this vision with greater scale, reach, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Department: People&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;People Operations Associate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Gemini People Team, you&#39;ll help shape and scale our People Operations function as we continue to grow. As an Associate, People Operations, you&#39;ll own and support key People Operations processes across the employee lifecycle, from onboarding and orientation to offboarding, HR systems, and employee data management. You&#39;ll play an integral role in delivering a seamless employee experience by ensuring our people programs and operations are efficient, accurate, compliant, and people-centered.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll partner closely with teams across the business to execute core People initiatives, continuously improve processes, and identify opportunities to simplify and automate workflows. You&#39;ll regularly work with highly confidential information and be trusted to exercise sound judgment and discretion while maintaining exceptional attention to detail and data integrity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who is proactive, detail oriented, resourceful, highly organized, and thrives in a fast-paced, evolving environment. You&#39;ll be successful if you&#39;re comfortable managing multiple priorities, taking ownership of your work, collaborating across teams, and independently driving projects forward once priorities are established. This role is based in our New York office and requires weekly in-person attendance to support new hire onboarding and orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute core People Operations programs across the employee lifecycle, including onboarding, offboarding, employee engagement initiatives, performance management, and other People Team programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end onboarding experience, including weekly in-person onboarding, welcoming new hires on their first day, conducting identity and security verification, assigning required training, facilitating live orientation sessions, and serving as the primary point of contact for onboarding-related questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with People Business Partners and the broader People Team to deliver a seamless employee experience and support People programs throughout the employee lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute employee lifecycle transactions and maintain accurate employee records within Workday (transitioning to Dayforce), Lattice, and other People systems across functional areas including Benefits, Payroll, Performance Management, and People Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the background check process for employees, interns, and contractors, ensuring accuracy, confidentiality, and compliance with company policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the first point of contact for employee HR inquiries by managing the People Team Help Desk and People Solutions inbox, responding within established SLAs and appropriately triaging or escalating complex or sensitive matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process I-9 employment verifications and maintain confidential employee files, ensuring the highest standards of data integrity, accuracy, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer required annual compliance training and learning programs, ensuring timely completion and accurate reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve, standardize, and automate People Operations processes to increase efficiency and enhance the employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits by coordinating, validating, and delivering accurate HR documentation and evidence within required timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams including Talent Acquisition, IT, Security, Payroll, and other stakeholders to ensure seamless onboarding, offboarding, and employee lifecycle processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, maintain, and continuously improve Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), process documentation, and knowledge resources within Confluence and Google Drive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to People Team initiatives and cross-functional projects, managing deliverables within defined scope and timelines while adapting to evolving business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in Human Resources, People Operations, or a related HR function within a fast-paced, high-growth organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience administering Workday, Dayforce, or a comparable Human Resources Information System (HRIS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting employee lifecycle processes, including onboarding, offboarding, HRIS transactions, and employee data management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of U.S. employment laws and HR compliance requirements, including I-9 verification, employee record maintenance, and confidential data handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impeccable attention to detail with a proven commitment to data integrity, accuracy, and compliance across People processes and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with ticketing systems such as Jira or equivalent platforms to manage employee requests and operational workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Google Workspace (Gmail, Calendar, Docs, Drive, and Sheets), including strong analytical skills in Google Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain the highest level of discretion when handling sensitive and confidential employee information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to identify process improvement opportunities, simplify workflows, and leverage automation to improve operational efficiency and employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and operational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities, proactively follow up on deliverables, and consistently produce high-quality work in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with confidence facilitating live presentations and delivering an engaging onboarding experience for new hires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and critical thinking skills, with the ability to troubleshoot issues, evaluate options, and balance employee needs with broader business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build strong cross-functional partnerships with teams such as Talent Acquisition, Tech, Security, Payroll, Benefits, and other business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with the ability to work independently, navigate ambiguity, adapt quickly to changing priorities, and proactively remove roadblocks while maintaining a high level of service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in building a career in People Operations and growing alongside a scaling People Team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SHRM-CP or equivalent HR certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with People Operations tools such as Confluence, Checkr, Lattice, Slack, Jira, Zip, and DocuSign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI-powered tools to streamline workflows, improve documentation, and increase operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;It Pays to Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;The compensation &amp;amp; benefits package for this role includes:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive starting pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;A discretionary annual bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Long-term incentive in the form of a new hire equity grant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Comprehensive health plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;401K with company matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;: The base salary range for this role is between $82,500 - $110,000 in the State of New York. This range is not inclusive of our discretionary bonus or equity package. When determining a candidate’s compensation, we consider a number of factors including skillset, experience, job scope, and current market data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the United States, we offer a hybrid work approach at our hub offices, balancing the benefits of in-person collaboration with the flexibility of remote work. Expectations may vary by location and role, so candidates are encouraged to connect with their recruiter to learn more about the specific policy for the role. Employees who do not live near one of our hubs are part of our remote workforce. All employees, however, are required to onboard in-person at one of our office locations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Gemini, we strive to build diverse teams that reflect the people we want to empower through our products, and we are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status. Equal Opportunity is the Law, and Gemini is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. If you have a specific need that requires accommodation, please let a member of the People Team know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-MW1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

8112959:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a SMB Hunter Sales Manager at Stripe, you will play an instrumental role in fueling Stripe’s growth through new customer acquisition. In this role, you will build and lead a team of high-performing Account Executives, helping them to develop their skills and deliver on their ambitious targets, as well as roll your sleeves up to work directly with customers. We are looking for a proactive leader who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, managing high-performing teams and solving complicated problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have management and leadership experience scaling a technology sales team and possess first-class analytical, communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop and lead a team of Account Executives who focus on small and medium, high-growth, tech-forward businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior leadership to develop the long-term vision and strategy for the team, and manage day-to-day operations with a focus on performance against key sales and growth metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for increasing revenue and new client acquisition at high rates of growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate and enable development of team members to promote career growth and impact for Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively and cross-functionally across the organization to help shape Stripe’s products and solutions to meet customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a personal and direct role in building and maintaining enduring customer relationships, up to C-level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement programs to improve pipeline generation efforts and improve overall efficiency for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience, with 2+ years of people management experience preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading sales in an early stage, high-growth technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train and coach a high-performance sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships with strategic client and industry thought leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for start-ups and new technology businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and articulate technical concepts, and translate them into industry- or business-relevant terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience forecasting and managing a high growth commercial business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience running complex sales cycles, ideally with both commercial and enterprise size companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience leading a team in an office outside of the company headquarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the payments industry and/or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8112966:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Data Science team partners deeply with teams across Stripe to ensure that our users, our products, and our business have the models, data products, and insights needed to make decisions and grow responsibly. We&#39;re looking for data scientists with a passion for analyzing data, building machine learning and statistical models, and running experiments to drive impact. Our work is broad and varied, influencing how our products work (e.g., understanding user needs, preventing fraud, or optimizing charge flows), how our business works (forecasting key outcomes, managing liquidity, and quantifying risk exposure), how our go-to-market motions operate (designing growth experiments, optimizing marketing investments, refining sales processes, and estimating causal effects), and everything in between.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Data Science team at Stripe is the dedicated data science and analytics partner for Link - currently with a strong product market fit in offering one-click checkout to shoppers who shop across Stripe’s merchant network, trusted by more than 300M users. The Link team has an exciting roadmap to launch consumer-friendly features to make Link the best way to spend, while continuously generating conversion uplift to our merchants. We are hiring for two data scientists dedicated to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Local Payment Methods &lt;/span&gt;- We want to enable consumers across the globe to be able to pay using their preferred local payment method like UPI, PIX etc. This allows merchants to get conversion uplift from reduced friction as consumers get to pay with the payment method that is most accessible for them. In this role, you get to drive the enablement and support of more local payment methods, run analyses to surface friction points and improve the product, and be a pioneer in shaping consumer payment method preferences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Link Consumer Team&lt;/span&gt; - Beyond the one-click accelerated checkout product, the Link team has also shipped a lot of value-added features for our consumers. On the Link App you can review your subscriptions, add more than one payment methods so you can choose the right payment method that maximizes your rewards on checkout without having to manually fill it up anywhere, and&amp;nbsp; even an agentic AI-wallet that allows your preferred AI model to transact on your behalf without exposing your payment credentials.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with a specific part of the business, playing a crucial role in optimizing our systems and leveraging data to make strategic business decisions. As Data Scientists at Stripe, it&#39;s our mission to ensure that the company strategy, products, and user interactions make smart use of our rich data, using techniques like machine learning, statistical modeling, causal inference, optimization, experimentation, and all forms of analytics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD with 3+ years, MS or MA with 6+ years, or BS or BA with 8+ years of data science or quantitative modeling experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in Product Analytics, Experimentation and Causal Inference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, running, and analyzing complex experiments or leveraging causal inference designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with cross-functional teams to deliver results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate results clearly and a focus on driving impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated ability to manage and deliver on multiple projects with a high attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and experience in synthesizing complex analyses into actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AI tools to accelerate model development, analysis, and coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge and hands-on experience in several of the following areas: machine learning, statistics, optimization, product analytics, causal inference, and experimentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience deploying models in production and adjusting model thresholds to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder&#39;s mindset with a willingness to question assumptions and conventional wisdom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed tools such as Spark, Hadoop, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A PhD or MS in a quantitative field (e.g., Statistics, Engineering, Mathematics, Economics, Quantitative Finance, Sciences, Operations Research)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;

