8119967:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSA) are domain experts aligned to specific Stripe solutions and customer buying centers. We have in-depth knowledge of specific solution offerings and a deep understanding of customer challenges. We align with specialist product sellers on deals, advise the broader pre-sales team on complex opportunities, support pipeline development and revenue attainment, serve as an advisor on go-to-market sales plays, and provide critical insights to our product and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;You will collaborate closely with sales and pre-sales teams to drive pipeline and revenue targets, while also educating the product and engineering teams on market trends and strongly influencing the product roadmap. You will develop deep relationships with senior customer business leaders and grow Stripe&#39;s solution offerings with new and existing customers. As a subject matter expert, you will scale the broader organization by creating reusable assets and coaching others on complex, high-value opportunities.The team is looking for a payments optimization specialist with a proven track record of designing and deploying payment infrastructure for global enterprises. You will engage with customers as a thought leader in the advanced payments stack - helping them navigate multi-PSP environments, payment orchestration, adaptive pricing, and buy-now-pay-later integrations to maximize authorization rates, reduce costs, and improve conversion at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Act as a subject matter expert on Stripe&#39;s Optimized Checkout Suite, Adaptive Pricing, Managed Payments, Orchestration, and BNPL integrations to accelerate opportunities globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Demonstrate a deep understanding of global payment optimization - including local acquiring, intelligent routing, dynamic currency conversion, and authorization improvement strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Develop expertise in designing multi-PSP and payment orchestration architectures, including how Stripe integrates alongside or replaces incumbent processors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Advise customers on BNPL strategy, including product selection, regulatory considerations, and integration patterns across checkout and billing flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Define, share, and learn best practices and reusable assets with the broader GTM organization to enhance the quality and efficiency of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Create reference architectures that help customers design end-to-end payment infrastructure with Stripe at the core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Partner closely with the Payments product sales team on Stripe&#39;s most complex OCS and Orchestration opportunities, leading solution strategy and owning key customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Serve as a &quot;Voice of the Customer&quot; internally to drive product and feature request prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Identify and summarize trends in payment orchestration, cost optimization, and alternative payment methods, and provide actionable insights to product stakeholders and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Act as an escalation point to drive complex technical issues to resolution with Stripe&#39;s engineering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Stay current on competitive analysis and market differentiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Support marketing events including executive briefings, conferences, user groups, and trade shows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Approximately 25% travel is anticipated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;7+ years of experience in payments, fintech, or a closely related industry in a pre-sales, solutions architecture, or technical consulting role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong working knowledge of global payment methods including cards, wallets, bank-based methods, and BNPLs - including regional preferences and regulatory context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience designing payment optimization architectures for large enterprises, including multi-PSP environments and orchestration layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Knowledge of authorization rate improvement levers: local acquiring, network tokenization, 3DS, smart retries, and the technical and commercial tradeoffs between them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of software engineering and API integration patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Experience integrating Stripe or other RESTful payment APIs into web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Knowledge of ISO payment standards and card network rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Experience with payment cost modeling, interchange optimization, or processor benchmarking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Familiarity with marketplace and platform payment flows (Connect, multi-party transactions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Experience as a subject matter expert in a relevant industry, vertical, or product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8119994:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ripple is growing rapidly. We are looking for a focused Software Engineering Manager to lead the Product Ledger team. This team builds the double-entry ledger service powering accounting and financial state across Ripple Products. You&#39;ll partner closely with Accounting, Product, and Compliance to build a correctness-critical system that scales across new business lines while remaining audit-ready and Oracle-integrated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think strategically while balancing both short and long-term needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will build and lead hard-working engineering teams by motivating your team and leading by example to continuously innovate, improve and think differently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will deliver outstanding results for our customers and are a role model for other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a shared vision and build and maintain strong partnerships with Product Management, Ops, Security, Research, Customer Success, and Business development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for the entire software development process for your team’s work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver your roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading impactful engineering teams, having led teams of 8+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in Java (Spring) and comfort reviewing/contributing to backend service code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience building or operating a &lt;strong&gt;double-entry ledger or core accounting/financial system&lt;/strong&gt; — journals, debits/credits, chart of accounts, balance derivation, reversals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record with &lt;strong&gt;correctness-critical, high-throughput transactional systems&lt;/strong&gt;: idempotency design, concurrency control (optimistic locking / conditional writes), and balance-integrity guarantees under concurrent writes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with team members — revenue recognition, intercompany accounting, GL mapping, reconciliation, and ERP integration (e.g., Oracle)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of databases at scale and familiarity with NoSQL data modeling (e.g., DynamoDB) for future migration paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing &lt;strong&gt;event-driven systems&lt;/strong&gt; that translate business events into balanced, auditable postings, with simulation/dry-run tooling for onboarding new event types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a &lt;strong&gt;regulated, audit-sensitive environment&lt;/strong&gt; — immutable/append-only records, traceability requirements, safeguarding or similar compliance obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: familiarity with crypto custody and multi-network asset movement (wallets, blockchain networks, exchanges) given the ledger&#39;s (asset, network) balancing model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of defining and owning a technical roadmap across multiple product verticals. This includes onboarding additional service areas onto a shared platform rather than focusing on a single product surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bias toward action, sound judgment under ambiguity, and success recruiting and growing strong engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;For positions that will be based in NY, the annual salary range for this position is below. Actual salaries may vary based on numerous factors including, among other things, an individual applicant’s experience and qualifications for the position. This range does not include equity or additional compensation, such as bonuses or commissions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NY Annual Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$245,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ripple is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We do not discriminate against qualified employees or applicants because of race, color, religion, gender identity, sex, sexual identity, pregnancy, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, military status, or any other characteristic protected by local law or ordinance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please find our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/eu-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UK/EU Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/a&gt;and our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/ca-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for reference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8120028:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blockchain&lt;/strong&gt; is connecting the world to the future of finance. As the most trusted and fastest-growing global crypto company, it helps millions of people worldwide safely access cryptocurrency. Since its inception in 2011, Blockchain has earned the trust of over 90 million wallet holders and more than 40 million verified users, facilitating over $1 trillion in crypto transactions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As we prepare for our next phase of growth, including a potential transition from a private to a public company, we are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Stock Plan Administrator&lt;/strong&gt; to manage our global equity programs. This is a critical role responsible for ensuring the accuracy, compliance, and scalability of our stock administration function during a pivotal time for the company. You will be a key member of the Legal and Finance teams, supporting our employees and stakeholders through this exciting evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the day-to-day administration of the company’s global equity plan (stock options, RSUs, etc.) currently on the Carta platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process all equity-related transactions, including new grants, exercises, cancellations, and vesting events, ensuring accuracy and timeliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the preparation and execution of all equity administration aspects related to the company’s transition to a public entity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement public company processes, including trading window administration, pre-clearance procedures, and support for 10b5-1 trading plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for employees, executives, and other stakeholders for all questions related to equity awards and company policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Legal, HR, and Finance teams to ensure seamless data flow for payroll, tax withholding, accounting (ASC 718), and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and reconcile equity data for internal and external reporting, including support for public filings (e.g., S-1, 10-K, Proxy Statements) and Section 16 reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our transfer agent, outside counsel, and other vendors to build and maintain a robust public company stock administration infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver educational materials and communications to help employees understand the value of their equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with all applicable securities laws and regulations, both domestically and internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL NEED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 5-8 years of direct experience in stock plan administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crucial:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing equity plans through a company’s transition from private to public (IPO, SPAC, or direct listing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise with equity administration platforms, particularly Carta.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of public company equity administration, including SEC regulations, Section 16 filings, Rule 144, and 10b5-1 plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the accounting (ASC 718) and tax implications of equity compensation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work cross-functionally with Legal, HR, and Finance in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, organizational skills, and ability to manage sensitive data with the highest degree of integrity and confidentiality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a demonstrated ability to explain complex concepts to employees at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets for reporting and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Equity Professional (CEP) designation is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time salary based on experience and meaningful equity in an industry-leading company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid model (remote &amp;amp; on-site setup is mandatory)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited vacation policy; work hard and take time when you need it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apple equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to be a key player and build your career at a rapidly expanding, global technology company in an emerging field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work culture&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Blockchain is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender expression, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status or any other characteristic protected by law. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, and apprenticeship. Blockchain makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;You may contact our Data Protection Officer by email at dpo@blockchain.com. Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation) as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, if you are located outside of the United States, your personal data will be transferred to the United States once you submit it through this site. Because the European Union Commission has determined that United States data privacy laws do not ensure an adequate level of protection for personal data collected from EU data subjects, the transfer will be subject to appropriate additional safeguards under the standard contractual clauses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment.&amp;nbsp; Under the GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with an EU supervisory authority.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8120101:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood is seeking a Senior Software Engineer to join the Enterprise Build team: the small, high-leverage team that turns the company&#39;s best AI-built prototypes into true enterprise-grade services. Robinhood has gone all-in on an AI-accelerated workforce: every week, Hoodies across Finance, HR, Legal, Compliance, and beyond use sanctioned AI tools to build working prototypes of the tools they wish they had. The best of those ideas deserve to become real software. That is this team&#39;s entire job, and yours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is built on the premise that AI multiplies what a senior engineer can own: agents do the first pass of assessment, porting, and scaffolding; you review, harden, and decide. The work is a distinctive loop.&amp;nbsp; A prototype earns real usage in our experimental sandbox and arrives through a single front door. You assess it, decide what survives, often the idea and the workflow, rarely the code, and rebuild it as an enterprise-grade, production-spec service that meets our full engineering standards: SSO, audit logging, secrets management, CI/CD, infrastructure as code, and security review, baked in from the first commit. While you build, you work directly with business partners, the forward-deployed pattern, pointed inward. Robinhood operates in a heavily regulated industry. Building fast here means building safely, and this team exists to help make sure those aren&#39;t in tension.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess vibe-coded prototypes from across the company and make the technical call: harden, rebuild, or redirect, then own the outcome end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and ship services on Robinhood&#39;s enterprise platforms, meeting the company&#39;s full standards for secure, reliable enterprise software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-natively: drive agents through first-pass assessment, porting, and test scaffolding, and ship MCP servers, sub-agents, and agent skills as production artifacts where the solution calls for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with sponsoring business units (Finance, HR, Legal, Compliance) during each build, translating real workflows into software people actually adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean operational handoffs as part of your definition of done: runbooks, evals, and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the paved patterns with the Enterprise Platforms team: when you solve the same problem twice, make it a platform capability the third time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar on AI-era engineering quality, including rigorous, teaching-quality review of AI-generated code, your own and others&#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience building and running production backend or full-stack systems, with a track record of independently delivering high-ambiguity projects end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on cloud depth, GCP preferred, including containerized services, CI/CD pipelines, and infrastructure as code, with a strong focus on a serverless stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated AI-native development: daily fluency with agentic coding tools, experience building LLM-powered applications or agentic workflows, and the judgment to review, harden, and productionize AI-generated code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product sense and scoping discipline: you can find the 20% of a prototype worth keeping, say no to the rest, and finish, this team&#39;s leverage depends on engagements that end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication with non-engineers: you&#39;re comfortable embedded with finance, legal, or HR partners, translating in both directions without losing precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in highly regulated industries, particularly finance or fintech, is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
