8120460:
&lt;p&gt;Flow Traders is looking for a Software Engineer (Trading Automation) to join our Technology department in our New York office. As a member of Trading Automation team, you will develop applications that support our core business by improving data frameworks, automating workflows, and creating opportunities for greater efficiency and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be responsible for developing applications, services, mentoring team members and managing stakeholders. Your actions will directly contribute to the performance of the company. You will also get the opportunity to interact and work closely with the global Trading Automation team and different departments to gain a well-rounded knowledge of start-to-end trading landscape, how they function and integrate within our ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop workflow automation processes aligned with business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, create, and maintain data pipelines and data-intensive applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write automated test cases, ensuring that they cover major edge cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thoroughly document your work, including technical/design specifications and operational guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy software applications to production using continuous integration and continuous deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as first line of defense with regards to operational support of the solutions delivered by the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with both local and global stakeholders and team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you need to succeed&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional working experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or related fields required; advanced degree preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of Git, SQL, Python, and Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with any of Airflow, Ansible, Kafka, Docker, Kubernetes, and AWS/Azure/GCP is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using LLMs to develop software and integrate solutions with existing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with a strong sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on, entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flow Traders, we acknowledge the importance of open and transparent communication whether it be with our employees, our stakeholders, or our local and global communities.&amp;nbsp;When it comes to salary, Flow Traders uses reliable market research to create base ranges. Where candidates will fall within the range depends on a few different factors including but not limited to level of experience, location, and specific skill set.&amp;nbsp;We also consider ourselves one global team, and to demonstrate that, all employees are eligible to share in the company’s success through an annual discretionary variable remuneration allocated based on company, group and individual performance and contribution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Per NYC salary transparency law, the total compensation for this role includes a base range of $185,000 to $240,000 plus annual discretionary variable remuneration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;#LI-MM1&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8120494:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk Engineering builds the systems that protect Stripe from fraud, credit losses, and regulatory risk across user onboarding, compliance, financial crimes, and identity verification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial Crimes Engineering builds the systems and controls that let Stripe safely onboard businesses in emerging and regulated industries while keeping Stripe in compliance with sanctions law, anti-money-laundering rules, and financial partner requirements. We keep known bad actors off Stripe, find new through ongoing detection, and build AI-augmented tooling that helps expert reviewers resolve cases quickly and accurately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at scale, screening every user, enforcing jurisdictional restrictions across money movement in real time, and automating signal acquisition and synthesis into investigation workflows. We&#39;re now re-architecting our screening platform to make it safe and easy for new Stripe products to launch with the right financial crimes controls, to express richer policy as code, and to serve as a multi-tenant Risk Platform offering across Stripe&#39;s products and subsidiaries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer on Financial Crimes Engineering, you&#39;ll own technical direction across our screening, detection, and review systems. You&#39;ll design infrastructure that balances screening latency with accuracy, build the systems that surface emerging risk and collect information to resolve it, and ensure investigators have the tooling they need. You&#39;ll work across distributed systems and policy logic, partnering with ML, Legal, and Compliance to translate regulation into working software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define technical strategy &amp;amp; vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish the multi-year architecture for Stripe’s real-time entity matching infrastructure, policy enforcement engines, and reviewer tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect high-scale systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and optimize distributed screening engines and detection pipelines handling entity- and transaction-level requests at scale with strict SLA and uptime guarantees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build investigations infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Design the systems that surface suspicious activity, collect additional information from users, route cases to reviewers, and augment human judgment with AI to drive faster, more accurate case resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive cross-functional technical alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical voice with Legal, Compliance, ML, and Product leaders to translate evolving global regulatory requirements into technical ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable Risk as a Service:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the architectural evolution toward a multi-tenant screening platform - laying the technical foundation for both internal product launches and external developer-facing APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Set standards for system design, API consistency, and operational rigor across backend and ML-adjacent systems; mentor senior engineers and lead high-stakes design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure operational excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Own system reliability, observability, and latency, ensuring production systems adapt quickly to sudden changes in global sanctions lists or traffic spikes, and participate in an on-call rotation for these systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, including 5+ years in a strategic technical leadership role on core infrastructure, distributed systems, or platform engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing, building, and operating high-throughput, low-latency APIs and distributed backend systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of defining technical roadmaps and driving alignment across multiple engineering teams and cross-functional domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on technical depth - comfortable jumping from high-level system architecture down to code-level performance tuning and production debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of articulating technical decisions to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain experience in financial crimes, sanctions screening, AML (Anti-Money Laundering), entity resolution, or high-stakes trust &amp;amp; safety platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with applying LLMs or ML to operational workflows (e.g., case triage, entity resolution, review automation), or experience with fuzzy string matching and NLP for entity matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building investigator/analyst tooling, case management systems, or human-in-the-loop review workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform products or APIs consumed by both internal engineering teams and external developers (e.g., API backward compatibility, client libraries).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience leading 0-1 platform builds or major architectural modernizations from concept to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech stack experience across multi-language environments (e.g., Primarily Ruby and Java) and modern data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity and making high-judgment engineering calls in a fast-moving regulatory environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8120501:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s People Systems Team sits at the intersection of technology and human experience. We are internal consultants who turn ambiguity into scale. Part of the People Solutions org, we partner with Corporate Technology, Finance, Payroll, the wider People team including Total Rewards &amp;amp; Benefits teams to build a world-class employee experience. We are a &quot;strategy-first, quality- execution-always&quot; team that values technical rigor, nimble problem-solving, and a deep empathy for the Stripes we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Workday Analyst, Payroll, you&#39;ll be a technical anchor for our Workday ecosystem and a driver of what&#39;s next for it. This role goes beyond keeping the lights on: you&#39;ll bring new Workday feature knowledge into the team, help automate manual payroll processes, and shape how we use emerging Workday capabilities (including AI-driven and agent-based tools) to modernize our payroll operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the technical health of our Workday Payroll environments for Workday in-house payrolls, balancing critical keep-the-lights-on (KLTO) operations with high-impact strategic projects. You&#39;ll also act as a bridge to our broader tech stack, supporting HRIS tools built on top of Workday and partnering with Payroll and other internal and external stakeholders for smooth data flow and a unified user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll partnership and delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Payroll:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary technical partner for the Payroll team, translating business needs into scalable Workday solutions and setting clear expectations on delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver payroll changes: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead technical configuration for Workday Payroll changes end to end, from requirements through implementation, testing, and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support new country onboarding: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead implementation to onboard new payroll countries as Stripe expands, covering configuration, testing, and knowledge transfer so the team can support new geographies independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation and automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring new capability into the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay current on new Workday Payroll features and functionality, and assess and pilot them for Stripe&#39;s environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate and modernize: &lt;/strong&gt;Identify manual, repetitive payroll processes and redesign them using Workday automation, integrations, or agent-based tools, reducing manual effort and error rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive strategic roadmapping: &lt;/strong&gt;Work alongside People Solutions to lead product-led strategic projects from discovery to deployment, so our Workday footprint evolves ahead of Stripe&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence best practices: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to influence stakeholders on workday and HRIS best practices to apply, to deliver solutions and projects that are scalable and supportable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HCM operations support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve open tickets:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide operations support on the Workday HCM &amp;amp; Payroll side to resolve and close Stripe&#39;s open Workday tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Handle integration-specific tasks: &lt;/strong&gt;This includes issue resolution, data access requests, report writing, and managing integration errors and warnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as Tier 3 expert: &lt;/strong&gt;Act as the escalation point for complex HCM, Payroll, and security issues that other tiers can&#39;t resolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day to Day Project work: &lt;/strong&gt;Project work may include developing Workday configurations, creating Workday dashboards, and producing custom Workday reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance and collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Payroll, Compliance, Legal, and Internal Audit to manage payroll compliance controls (SOX ITGCs, segregation of duties, ACA reporting, multi-state tax nexus, FLSA rules, provincial obligations, and leave laws), annual access certifications, EEO-1/VETS-4212 filings, and T4/ROE year-end processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share knowledge: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to a supportive team culture by sharing knowledge and helping peers, and use good judgment to escalate risks and roadblocks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in HRIS/People Systems, with at least 3+ years of deep configuration experience in the Workday HCM, Reporting, Time and Absence and Payroll modules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working with highly confidential information&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;and supporting critical business operations and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to set clear expectations with senior stakeholders and the confidence to escalate issues when necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead cross-functional projects, navigating ambiguity and high-pressure timelines with a sense of urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of payroll processing, payroll calculations, costing, retro payroll, reconciliations, payroll auditing, and payroll security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday certifications in Payroll for US and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of EIBs, Studio, or Core Connectors to support data flow between Workday and third-party vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Workday automation tools, AI-driven features, or agent-based capabilities (for example, Workday Illuminate or Extend), and an interest in applying them to payroll operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience supporting Workday Payroll implementations in new countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a &quot;low-ego, high-talent&quot; person who likes bringing order to complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8120523:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Plant Project Manger&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Plant PMO&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports To:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; PMO Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA Status:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Exempt, Full-Time, Benefited&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range: &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;$88k - $95K - DOE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Southern CA preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role of the Plant Project Manager is to ensure that outside plant projects run efficiently, timely and within budget. This position is responsible for managing all aspects of multiple outside plant construction projects from the design concept through project delivery while promoting Sonic&#39;s core values of outstanding customer service, quality, security and integrity. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type/Expected Hours of Work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Plant Project Manager is a full-time (40 hours per week), exempt position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Travel is expected for this position. A valid California Driver’s License and Clean DMV is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervisory Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Plant Project Manager directly supervises, monitors, and schedules Contractors and in-house Construction Crews and provides regular feedback to the PMO Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent Communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer/public interactions and relations/problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating long- and short-term plans, including setting targets for milestones and adhering to deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delegating tasks on the project to employees best positioned to complete them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making effective decisions when presented with multiple options for how to progress with the project&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as a point of contact for teams when multiple units are assigned to the same project to ensure team actions remain in synergy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicating with executives or department managers to keep the project aligned with their goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing quality control on the project throughout development to maintain the standards expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Materials takeoff/orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scheduling projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing project budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adjusting schedules and targets on the project as needs or financing for the project change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with other Project Managers and team to manage resources across multiple projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply for and maintain permits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cost control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong MS Project, GIS, and Accounting Software/ERP software skills required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To perform the job successfully, an individual should demonstrate the following competencies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibility -&lt;/strong&gt; Acts independently in the field within reason; knows when to consult for assistance; acts with integrity in all business-related decisions; takes responsibility for vehicles, tools and credit cards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving &lt;/strong&gt;- Identifies and resolves problems in a timely manner; Gathers and analyzes information skillfully; Develops alternative solutions; Works well in group problem solving situations; Uses reason even when dealing with emotional&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills &lt;/strong&gt;- Assesses own strengths and weaknesses; Pursues training and development opportunities; Strives to continuously build knowledge and skills; Shares expertise with Previous experience with Microsoft Project strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Service &lt;/strong&gt;- Manages difficult or emotional customer situations; Responds promptly to customer needs; Solicits customer feedback to improve service; Responds to requests for service and assistance; Meets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interpersonal Skills &lt;/strong&gt;- Focuses on solving conflict, not blaming; Maintains confidentiality; Listens to others without interrupting; Keeps emotions under control; Remains open to others’ ideas and tries new&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oral Communication &lt;/strong&gt;- Speaks clearly and persuasively in positive or negative situations; listens and gets clarification; Responds well to questions; Demonstrates group presentation skills; Participates in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Written Communication &lt;/strong&gt;- Writes clearly and informatively; Edits work for spelling and grammar; Varies writing style to meet needs; Presents numerical data effectively; Able to read and interpret written&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethics &lt;/strong&gt;- Treats people with respect; Keeps commitments; inspires the trust of others; Works with integrity and ethically; Upholds organizational&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driving is expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Plant Project Managers may be exposed to varying climates and elements, determined by Mother Nature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While performing the duties of this job, the employee is constantly required to sit and stand; talk or hear; reach with hands and arms; key/type.&amp;nbsp; The employee is required to walk; use hands to finger, handle, or feel objects, tools or controls; climb stairs; balance; stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl. The employee must lift and/or move up to 80 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by the job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. The employee is required to drive a vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sonic is an equal opportunity employer. Sonic is committed to providing a work environment free of harassment, discrimination, retaliation and disrespectful or other unprofessional conduct based on sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding or related medical conditions), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), color, gender (including gender identity and gender expression), national origin (including language use restrictions and possession of a driver&#39;s license issued under Vehicle Code section 12801.9), ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, registered domestic partner status, age, sexual orientation, military and veteran status or any other basis protected by federal, state or local law or ordinance or regulation. It also prohibits discrimination, harassment, disrespectful or unprofessional conduct based on the perception that anyone has any of those characteristics, or is associated with a person who has or is perceived as having any of those characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8120681:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Crimes Team at Robinhood works across multiple verticals to protect our customers and ensure strict compliance with all relevant Anti-Money Laundering (AML) and Sanctions regulations. As our team of passionate professionals continues to evolve the program, we are intensely focused on leveraging innovative thinking, advanced analytics, and cutting-edge technology to build a best-in-class Financial Crimes Program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Specialist, Model Validation &amp;amp; Analytics, you will play a key role in this mission by executing the validation, testing, tuning, and optimization of various transaction monitoring and filtering programs across Financial Crimes. You will partner closely with the AML Surveillance Team, engineering partners, and cross-functional verticals to ensure our financial crimes models and systems are accurately implemented, rigorously evaluated, and effectively calibrated to meet the diverse regulatory requirements of our domestic and international lines of business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Denver, CO, New York, NY, or Westlake, TX office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model Validation &amp;amp; Review Execution: Perform independent, rigorous quantitative and qualitative analyses of rule-based and machine learning financial crimes surveillance models, filtering systems, and detection logic targeting model design, algorithm soundness, data integrity, and change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Review &amp;amp; Remediation: Act as a technical bridge within a fast-paced fintech environment by leveraging a solid foundation in data engineering, data modeling, and infrastructure. Collaborate seamlessly with software engineers, data engineers, and data scientists to decipher complex logic, evaluate model implementations, test data pipelines, and support the remediation of model issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimization &amp;amp; Model Tuning: Execute effective tuning methodologies and statistical analyses to continuously calibrate and enhance surveillance models. Work on strategic initiatives focused on maximizing risk detection capabilities while systematically reducing false positive volumes to ensure an efficient and effective alert review process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logic &amp;amp; Data Integrity Assurance: Conduct comprehensive data validation and logic testing initiatives to establish a strong foundation of data quality. Ensure the completeness, accuracy, and end-to-end reliability of critical data pipelines and inputs feeding our compliance models, mitigating systemic risks and safeguarding the integrity of our transaction monitoring ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subject Matter Expertise: Serve as a knowledgeable subject matter resource in AML and Model Risk, providing practical domain insights and supporting cross-functional partners in understanding model logic, performance, and risk trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Build strong working partnerships across engineering, product, and compliance teams to ensure technical solutions are conceptually sound, effective, and aligned with our risk tolerance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change &amp;amp; Issue Management: Uphold change and issue management policies for covered systems, models, and solutions, ensuring end-to-end traceability and maintaining defensible documentation for internal audit and external regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Strategy &amp;amp; Tech-Forward Adoption: Bring hands-on capabilities and experience leveraging AI tools, Large Language Models (LLMs), and automation techniques to enhance daily productivity, elevate deliverable quality, and optimize team workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Reporting: Author thorough, concise, and defensible validation reports, change and issues management documentation, and executive summaries that clearly explain model theory, testing logic, performance findings, and actionable recommendations for key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor&#39;s Degree or equivalent in a quantitative, technical, or financial field (e.g., Computer Science, Data Analytics, Statistics, or Finance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 5+ years of experience across AML, Financial Crimes, or risk management within the financial services or fintech industry, with a focus on model validation, quantitative analysis, or surveillance system management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain Expertise: 3+ years of direct experience in the verification, validation, testing, or tuning of AML rule-based systems and/or machine learning models, along with a working knowledge of core Model Risk Management (MRM) principles and governance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Analytical Skills: Proficiency in SQL and experience using quantitative tools or programming languages (e.g., Python, R) to query large datasets, perform statistical analyses, and evaluate model performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability &amp;amp; Communication: Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to explain complex technical and quantitative concepts to non-technical partners, coupled with an ability to manage multiple competing priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$141,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$106,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8121218:
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Flow Traders is seeking a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Market Data Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to own the strategy, governance, and value realization of our external market data portfolio. You will ensure the right data reaches the right users under the right terms, helping to maximize utility, minimize waste, and empower our Trading, Research, and Technology teams with fit-for-purpose datasets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Your work will bridge commercial, technical, and operational domains to deliver market data that is compliant, cost-effective, and actionable. As the steward of our external market data, you will shape how Flow Traders discovers, acquires, and applies information at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the subject-matter expert on market data usage across the firm, mapping datasets to use cases, workflows, and systems, covering real-time, delayed, and historical data for pricing, analytics, execution, and research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive budgeting and forecasting accuracy: model usage, seat inventory, and consumption trends; translate business demand into spend forecasts; track variance and ROI; and advise on cost optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern entitlements and compliance: ensure data consumption aligns with licensing requirements, exchange/provider policies, display vs. non-display rules, redistribution terms, derived data policies, and audit requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize the utility of external data: benchmark vendors, evaluate quality and coverage, run pilots and proof-of-value studies, and partner with engineers to integrate data into production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational coverage by fulfilling reporting obligations and managing entitlement administration. Actively contribute to knowledge and process management best practices related to market data administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Legal and Compliance on contract interpretation and policy adherence; with Data Engineering on integration patterns and monitoring; and with Trading and Research on evolving data needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Core Skills and Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with data usage in a trading organization, including exchange data, consolidated feeds, alternative data, reference data and corporate actions, ESG data, OTC pricing, and historical and derived datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with market data licensing, entitlements, and compliance, including display vs. non-display usage, redistribution, derived data, device counts, end-user policies, and audit workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in market data vendor management and negotiations with exchanges and major providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and financial skills in budgeting, forecasting, and consumption modeling, with experience working with usage telemetry and cost allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with data engineering, MDM, and market data platforms (e.g., feed handlers, tick stores, API gateways, and entitlement systems), with the ability to translate business needs into technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to influence across Trading, Research, Technology, Finance, Legal, and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured, process-oriented mindset with a focus on continuous improvement and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

8121419:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and unlock new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. There is an enormous amount of work ahead, and an opportunity to do some of the most meaningful work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Funded Startups team partners with the most promising venture-backed startups across EMEA. We combine deep knowledge of Stripe’s products with strong relationships across the startup ecosystem to help founders build, monetize, and scale their businesses globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work brings the next generation of high-potential businesses to Stripe and helps them create sustainable growth—directly advancing Stripe’s mission to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive on the Funded Startups team, you will build partnerships with some of Italy’s most innovative and fast-growing venture-backed startups. You will help founders and operators understand how Stripe’s financial infrastructure can support their growth ambitions, unlock new revenue streams, and create an advantage in their markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a high-velocity sales motion from prospecting through close, while developing a strong understanding of each user’s business, technical environment, and priorities. You will identify opportunities for users to adopt more of Stripe’s product suite, create and execute campaigns that build new pipeline, and partner cross-functionally to set users up for long-term success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and qualify high-potential venture-backed startups through inbound leads and proactive outbound prospecting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, from first engagement to closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute territory and account plans that drive new business, product adoption, and sustained user value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of users’ business models, technical environments, and pain points; recommend the Stripe solutions that best meet their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create pipeline through research, networking, targeted outreach, cold calling, and territory campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in the Italian startup ecosystem and help expand our local presence through founder, investor, and community engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and work with a network of international and local Parters&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Investment Partnerships team on venture-capital portfolio analysis and founder-focused events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with in-country go-to-market teams and our Dublin headquarters on shared initiatives and regional events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Solutions Architects, SDRs, Marketing, Product, Risk, Operations, and other partners to deliver a seamless user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring user feedback and complex needs to internal teams to help improve Stripe’s products and go-to-market approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a thoughtful, high-quality experience in every interaction, regardless of deal size.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a strategic, commercially minded seller who enjoys building trusted relationships and operating with pace. You can manage high-velocity deal cycles while navigating technical conversations and coordinating a diverse set of internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are curious about ambitious businesses and the problems they are solving. You combine strong sales judgement with a solution-oriented mindset, adapt quickly in ambiguous environments, and take ownership of moving work forward. You are motivated by helping founders build and scale, and by developing your own craft along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not meet every preferred qualification. The minimum requirements are the baseline for consideration; preferred qualifications are a bonus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a closing sales role; comparable experience in a product-focused commercial role will also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in Italian and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with venture-backed startups in Italy, with an established network across founders, investors, accelerators, and the broader Italian startup ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of consistently achieving or exceeding ambitious sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a full sales cycle in a complex or technical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical ecosystems and build credibility with technical and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgement and the ability to manage multiple priorities across complex sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building territory plans that identify the highest-impact activities and opportunities in a market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-functional projects and coordinating input from a range of internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building skills with internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and motivation to succeed in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;Experience in payments or financial technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a sales or customer-facing role at a high-growth technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with venture-backed startups in Italy, with an established network across founders, investors, accelerators, and the broader Italian startup ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in business models, monetization, and the challenges of scaling a company internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

