8124304:
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic infrastructure for the internet. Millions of businesses use Stripe to accept payments, manage revenue, and grow globally. Stripe Tax helps businesses calculate, collect, and manage indirect taxes as they sell across products, markets, and business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Staff Product Manager to help shape the future of Stripe Tax. In this role, you will lead high-impact product strategy and execution across a broad portfolio, making it easier for businesses to understand, calculate, collect, and manage tax as they grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager on Stripe Tax, you will identify the most important opportunities to improve our tax products and turn them into focused strategies, durable platforms, and exceptional user experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Engineering, Design, Tax, Partnerships, Go-to-Market, and other product teams to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set strategy and lead product initiatives that help more businesses successfully adopt and use Stripe Tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the speed, accuracy, reliability, and usability of Stripe Tax calculations and related workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand support for the geographies, tax requirements, industries, products, and business models that matter most to Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build capabilities for complex tax needs, such as registrations, exemptions, address and fulfillment logic, tax customization, and other business-specific requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable products and platform capabilities that work across Stripe’s ecosystem, including integrations, connector apps, marketplaces, and Connect platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Stripe to create coherent end-to-end experiences spanning calculation, collection, reporting, and tax management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer insight, market context, data, and technical understanding to prioritize investments and make clear tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders and cross-functional partners around a shared product direction, measurable outcomes, and an execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help make Stripe Tax a product businesses can rely on as they scale. Merchants should be able to confidently answer “yes” to questions such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can I use Stripe Tax for my business and the locations where I sell?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does Stripe Tax support the taxes and business models that apply to me?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can it calculate tax accurately for my registrations, exemptions, customers, products, and fulfillment model?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is it fast, reliable, and easy for my team to operate?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does it work with the other Stripe products, platforms, and integrations my business depends on?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a product leader who is comfortable operating in ambiguous, high-stakes spaces where customer needs, regulatory complexity, technical constraints, and commercial opportunity intersect. You can translate a broad mission into a focused strategy, build alignment across teams, and deliver meaningful products over multiple horizons.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You likely have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant product management experience, including ownership of complex, platform-oriented, or technically deep products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting strategy and delivering multi-team initiatives with measurable business and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in prioritizing across customer needs, market opportunities, operational complexity, and engineering investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering and design partners to build reliable, scalable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate clearly with executive stakeholders and to align diverse partners around a shared direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about global commerce, financial infrastructure, tax, compliance, payments, marketplaces, or developer platforms. Direct domain experience is helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first mindset and the ability to turn complex requirements into simple, effective product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tax is a fundamental challenge for businesses that sell across borders, channels, and business models. Stripe Tax has the opportunity to remove that complexity, helping businesses launch faster, expand with confidence, and operate globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage role at the intersection of global commerce, financial infrastructure, and product platform strategy. You will shape how Stripe Tax evolves to serve the next generation of internet businesses.&lt;/p&gt;

8124588:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Due to increased demand, we’re looking to hire a Cloud Infrastructure / Platform Engineer to join our team supporting our internal developer platform built on AWS. This is a hands-on role for someone with a few years of relevant experience who wants to grow in platform engineering, cloud operations, observability, and developer experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a good fit for someone who wants to grow beyond day-to-day platform support and into a broader platform engineering career.&amp;nbsp;You’ll&amp;nbsp;have exposure to both infrastructure and developer workflows, with a chance to make a real impact on cloud cost, platform reliability, and developer productivity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll&amp;nbsp;partner closely with Infrastructure, Security, IT, and Spire’s software development teams to improve how our platform runs, how our developers ship software, and how efficiently we spend it on AWS.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&amp;nbsp;you’ll&amp;nbsp;do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead analysis of AWS&amp;nbsp;spend across both platform-owned infrastructure and developer team workloads&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify&amp;nbsp;cost optimization opportunities and help implement changes that reduce spend without sacrificing reliability or developer experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support migration of existing workloads onto our newest internal developer platform&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate, troubleshoot, and resolve platform issues raised by internal customers, primarily software developers and IT/Security engineers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform regular maintenance, upgrades, and improvements across platform services and tooling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;code libraries, templates, and integrations that make it easier for application teams to instrument and&amp;nbsp;observe&amp;nbsp;their systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with platform observability and delivery tooling across:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS EKS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS networking (VPC, subnets, TGW, load balancers, routing) and security (Security Groups, NACLs)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub and GitHub Actions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ArgoCD&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog&amp;nbsp;Artifactory and X-Ray&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grafana Enterprise, Alloy, Mimir, Tempo&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OpenSearch&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Karpenter&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calico&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gatekeeper&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OpenCost&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&amp;nbsp;we’re&amp;nbsp;looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3+ years of experience in cloud infrastructure, platform engineering, SRE, DevOps, or a similar role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with AWS and Kubernetes, especially EKS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with&amp;nbsp;GitOps&amp;nbsp;workflows and CI/CD pipelines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable troubleshooting distributed systems and production issues&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of observability tooling and concepts such as metrics, logs, traces, and alerting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write code or libraries in one or more general-purpose languages to support developer workflows&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication&amp;nbsp;skills and a customer-focused mindset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable collaborating&amp;nbsp;frequently&amp;nbsp;with a variety of infrastructure, IT,&amp;nbsp;security&amp;nbsp;and application teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cost optimization in AWS or Kubernetes environments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with&amp;nbsp;ArgoCD&amp;nbsp;or similar&amp;nbsp;GitOps&amp;nbsp;tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Grafana ecosystem tooling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with policy and admission control tools like Gatekeeper&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes networking or traffic policy tools like Calico&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting internal developer platforms or platform product teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with&amp;nbsp;Open-Telemetry&amp;nbsp;or application instrumentation patterns&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification as an AWS Certified Solutions Architect or Certified&amp;nbsp;CloudOps&amp;nbsp;Engineer is an asset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spire operates a hybrid work model, and this position will require you to work a minimum of three business days per week in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun CommentHighlightClicked SCXW152905918 BCX0&quot;&gt;Access to US export-controlled software and/or technology may be required for this role. If needed, Spire will arrange the necessary licenses—this is not something candidates need to have before applying. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;sub&gt;#LI-MK1&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The anticipated base salary range for this position is listed below. Final base salary for this role will be based on the location, skills, experience and qualifications. In addition to base compensation, this role may be eligible for annual equity awards and our employee benefits program, including vacation, sick, and personal time off; optional medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage; a 401(K) plan; health and wellness reimbursement program; and participation in Spire’s Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$171,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Global Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛰️ Name Your Satellite Program (NYSP)&lt;br&gt;🚀 Launch Attendance&lt;br&gt;🌴 Generous Time Off Policy&lt;br&gt;🎓 Education Assistance Program&lt;br&gt;🥰 Employee Assistance Program (EAP)&lt;br&gt;📈 Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;br&gt;👣 Family Leave&lt;br&gt;💪 Fitness Reimbursement&lt;br&gt;🧡 Employee Referral Program&lt;br&gt;🍉 Healthy snacks &amp;amp; beverages in every office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Spire&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;improve life on Earth with data from space.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spire Global is a space-to-cloud analytics company that owns and operates the largest multi-purpose constellation of satellites. Its proprietary data and algorithms provide the most advanced maritime, aviation, and weather tracking in the world. In addition to its constellation, Spire’s data infrastructure includes a global ground station network and 24/7 operations that provide real-time global coverage of every point on Earth.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spire is Global and our success draws upon the diverse viewpoints, skills and experiences of our employees. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, gender identity or veteran status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;To help &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;maintain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt; a safe and secure workplace for Spire employees, all candidates who receive a conditional offer will &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;be required&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;to complete a background check&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;. This &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW208825983 BCX0&quot;&gt;may include criminal history and employment verification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please take a moment to review &lt;a href=&quot;https://spire.com/global-data-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;Spire&#39;s Global Data Privacy Notice for Employees, Contractors, Candidates and Visitors&lt;/a&gt;, as well as&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spire.com/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;Spire&#39;s Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kindly be advised that communication regarding your application may come from @spire.com, @recruiting.spire.com, or from Candidate.fyi (our scheduling tool).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8125473:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Counsel, Money Movement Legal (Asia-Pacific)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Legal team at Stripe manages the legal and regulatory aspects of designing, building, and launching products and services. The team works on technical, commercial, and regulatory matters and advises product, engineering, and partnerships teams on issues across financial services, business, and technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports the Money Movement and Storage business across Asia-Pacific. The business includes stored-value and e-money, foreign exchange, cross-border transfer, stablecoin and digital asset, and other financial products. The team helps ensure these products comply with applicable laws and regulations while supporting responsible product development and commercialization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Product Counsel, you&#39;ll advise teams on the legal and regulatory considerations for money movement products across Asia-Pacific. You&#39;ll partner with product, engineering, partnerships, compliance, risk, marketing, and Legal teams to navigate emerging requirements and bring products to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the Product Legal team deliver products that comply with laws and contractual commitments to users globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise product teams on the intersection of technological innovation, e-commerce user experiences, and financial services compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, engineering, partnerships, compliance, risk, and marketing teams on product development and commercialization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise teams on new and emerging legal and regulatory developments, identify potential effects on business activities, and apply existing laws to new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with colleagues across the global Legal team to support regulatory structures, customer agreements, and strategic financial partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and build scalable processes for legal review and product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date on money movement laws and regulations, and serve as a strategic advisor to senior managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a qualified lawyer in a law firm, in-house legal team, or government agency, with expertise in payment services laws and regulations, such as the Payment Services Act of Singapore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualification to practice law, preferably in a jurisdiction in Asia-Pacific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising technology teams and translating complex legal requirements into clear, actionable advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate with teammates, share knowledge, understand complex business models and product use cases, and exercise sound judgment with imperfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, project management, and prioritization skills in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on the development of stablecoin and digital asset products, particularly across multiple regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting legal, regulatory, or commercial matters for money movement or financial services products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8125586:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corporate Security helps keep Stripe secure and Stripes safe by building practical, risk-based programs that enable the company to operate and grow. We are looking for an experienced Regional Security Manager to join our team. As the Regional Security Manager Americas at Stripe, you will be responsible for developing our core physical-security deliverables to office locations in the Americas (North America and parts of Latin America), and help evolve our program to support Stripe around the globe. You will work cross functionally within the Corporate Security team, and alongside other business teams at the company to keep Stripe secure and Stripes safe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Regional Security Manager Americas, reporting to the Head of Global Security Operations, you will lead and continuously improve physical security operations across North America and relevant parts of Latin America. This is an individual-contributor role: you will manage regional contractors and vendor relationships, but will not directly manage employees at this time. You will translate regional risk into scalable programs, build trusted partnerships with internal teams and service providers, and help evolve Stripe’s global security operating model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role. The successful candidate will spend 50% of their time in one of our AMER office locations in San Francisco, New York, Seattle, or Chicago. We are not entertaining remote candidates at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional physical-security operations for the Americas, including security governance, escalations, incident response, service delivery, and performance reporting; contribute to global programs as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams such as Workplace, People, IT, Events, business leaders, and external providers to deliver a security program that scales with business needs while preserving a high-quality employee and visitor experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or coordinate risk, threat, vulnerability, and site-security assessments; document material risks; prioritize mitigations; and track delivery to closure. Conduct annual site-security assessments and risk reviews for company sites and relevant vendor sites to evaluate and improve controls in line with regional risk and established standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and test clear policies, standard operating procedures, and playbooks covering office security, escalation, incident documentation, event support, and crisis response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage regional security contractors, service providers, and guard-force partners through defined scopes, service-level expectations, key performance indicators, quarterly business reviews, and corrective-action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Business Continuity, Crisis Management, and Environmental Health &amp;amp; Safety to ensure regional emergency and crisis-response plans are current, practicable, and exercised regularly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Security Systems team as a regional decision maker to define and support physical-security technology design for new offices, relocations, expansions, and significant workplace changes. Ensure appropriate CCTV, alarm, and access-control capabilities are in place, functional, and aligned to regional risk and escalation needs across the region’s offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional operational planning and budgeting: forecast spend, identify cost and service improvements, and manage approved programs responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver security-awareness and education initiatives that help employees make safer decisions and strengthen Stripe’s security culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional security projects that reduce risk, improve resilience, and produce measurable operational outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced physical-security leader who pairs sound judgment with a practical, service-oriented approach. You can move comfortably between strategic program design and hands-on operational problem solving. You communicate clearly with executives, frontline partners, and vendors; make progress amid ambiguity; and build durable relationships across diverse geographic and business contexts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressively responsible physical-security, corporate-security, or closely related risk-management experience supporting a multinational organization, including responsibility for operations in the Americas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, operating, and measuring risk-based physical-security programs across multiple sites or jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting risk, threat, vulnerability, or site-security assessments and translating findings into prioritized, practical mitigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing security vendors or guard-force/service-provider relationships through scopes of work, performance measures, service reviews, and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or materially contributing to incident, emergency, or crisis-response planning and exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program and project-management skills, with the ability to prioritize multiple concurrent initiatives and communicate tradeoffs, risks, and progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, discretion, and a demonstrated commitment to employee safety, privacy, and an inclusive workplace experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel within the Americas and internationally up to 25%, including occasionally on short notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a technology, financial-services, or other fast-growing, globally distributed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting office construction, relocations, expansions, or physical-security system design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with access-control, video-surveillance, alarm, or other enterprise physical-security technologies and the governance that accompanies them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing security operations at large scale public events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant degree, CPP/PSP, or comparable professional certification; equivalent practical experience is also valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established professional relationships across the security industry, public-sector partners, or relevant regional networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in Spanish&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8125729:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Manager, for DACH Startups, you’ll play an instrumental role in fueling Stripe’s growth in the market through new customer acquisition and existing customers growth. You&#39;ll lead and coach high-performing account executives, helping them deliver on ambitious targets, as well as roll up your sleeves to work directly with users and prospects. We are looking for an individual who is keen to work alongside a high-performing team of individuals to navigate complex organizations, find new opportunities to make payments a competitive advantage for their businesses, and evolve our joint go-to-market in new ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop and lead a team of sales professionals, with a particular focus on the startup segment across DACH, CEE and Emerging markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the long-term vision and strategy for the team/markets and manage day-to-day operations, with a focus on performance against key sales metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for increasing revenue and new client acquisition at high rates of growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving deal strategy and execution including strong pipeline development, opportunity/renewal management, and forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills through all facets of the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a personal and direct role in building and maintaining enduring customer relationships, up to C-level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate and enable personal and career development of team members, both to promote career growth and to increase impact for Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating closely with key stakeholders across Sales, Product/Connect, Sales Ops, S&amp;amp;O, Marketing, GTM Partnerships, and others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in industry events to help support positive market awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with and knowledge of the EMEA Startups ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience consistently forecasting and managing a high growth business for multiple quarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in settings with a high level of autonomy to create strategy, direction, and structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train, and coach a high-performance sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build executive relationships with customers and ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and articulate technical concepts, and translate them into industry or business relevant terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8125789:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Middle Office Trading team’s mission is to deliver an excellent end-customer experience while minimizing firm risk and enabling the seamless operation of cutting-edge brokerage products. We support Robinhood’s dynamic trading offerings by handling core middle office functions, processing transactions, and tackling critical operational risk tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Trading Specialist on the Middle Office Trading team, you’ll help scale and refine our Trading Operations desk! You’ll support daily risk management activities, resolve customer-impacting escalations, push cross asset operational automation with teams across Robinhood to ensure the smooth functioning of our trading business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Lake Mary, FL, Denver, CO, or Chicago, IL office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications for this role will be accepted through August 30th, 2026. Please connect with your recruiter for more information about this role’s application window.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily trading operational tasks such as expiration processing and account-level risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently identify process inefficiencies, design improvements, and implement scalable solutions — leveraging AI tools, SQL, and automation to eliminate manual work and scale the desk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a point of contact for teammates on complex cases, and escalate appropriately when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Compliance, and Customer Experience teams to prioritize features, test the functionality of our trading products, and drive process improvements that span team boundaries — from operational workflows to regulatory response processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support desks across Middle Office Trading with out-of-hours responsibilities, including flexing across multiple time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and refine AI-assisted workflows for core operational tasks — risk reviews, reconciliations, data analysis, and regulatory inquiries — and push adoption of these tools across the desk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active FINRA Series 7 and Series 63 licenses (or the equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active FINRA Series 4 license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Robinhood’s Options Onboarding process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and customer service skills, with a drive to improve the client experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in complex financial topics like options, equities and margin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work outside regular hours and adapt to the evolving needs of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working autonomously, multitasking, and prioritizing in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, Python, and/or AI tooling (LLM assistants, agentic workflows) to automate and scale processes is a plus, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Tier benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the Robinhood Employee Fund that gives eligible US employees the opportunity to invest in a private employee fund that provides exposure to Robinhood Ventures funds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet - a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$94,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$110,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$82,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$97,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$73,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$86,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8125912:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a highly skilled and passionate software engineer looking for an exciting new challenge? Join Ripple and help redefine the way we send and receive payments globally! As a Senior Software Engineer, you will have the chance to develop enterprise-level payment applications that enable FinTech and banks to settle cross-border payments instantly, securely, and efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a technical guide, you will collaborate with a team of engineers to prototype and implement new solutions for sophisticated software problems, providing invaluable insights and mentorship to the team. You will work closely with multi-functional teams, including product, legal, and business development, to ensure that your design decisions are aligned with the strategic goals of the organization. Join us on this exciting journey and help craft the future of payments and the Internet of Value!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of distributed systems architectures, trade offs, and challenges as they relate to payment transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building highly scalable and performant enterprise software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent proven understanding of Java and its ecosystem (i.e. threading, concurrency ... etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eagerness to work openly and collaboratively with a diverse team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive demeanor and a passion for sharing knowledge - the go-to person on the team for small and large questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to encourage engineering standard processes in a team and the larger department&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years experience&lt;/strong&gt; in Software Engineering, with a deep focus on backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep, hands-on backend engineering experience&lt;/strong&gt; building and operating modern, cloud-native, and highly-available distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven track record designing and delivering complex features&lt;/strong&gt; within large-scale systems in complex, regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in &lt;strong&gt;API design and integration&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., REST and/or gRPC), with a focus on defining clear, reusable service contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms (AWS preferred) and container orchestration (Kubernetes, ECS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to tactically &lt;strong&gt;navigate and reduce technical debt&lt;/strong&gt; while driving significant business value and managing feature-level migration efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong technical ownership skills:&lt;/strong&gt; demonstrated ability to own the technical delivery for complex features and influence local, cross-team decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred (But Not Required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with our current stack: Java + Spring Boot. We welcome candidates from other robust backend stacks (Go, Kotlin, C#, Python, Rust, etc.) who can quickly learn JVM technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;event-driven architecture&lt;/strong&gt; (Kafka, SNS/SQS, etc.), essential for building a decoupled and resilient platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Other common names for this role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;For positions that will be based in CA, the annual salary range for this position is below. Actual salaries may vary based on numerous factors including, among other things, an individual applicant’s experience and qualifications for the position. This range does not include equity or additional compensation, such as bonuses or commissions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA Annual Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ripple is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We do not discriminate against qualified employees or applicants because of race, color, religion, gender identity, sex, sexual identity, pregnancy, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, military status, or any other characteristic protected by local law or ordinance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please find our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/eu-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UK/EU Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/a&gt;and our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/ca-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for reference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8126047:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with teams across the organization to understand pain points in their infrastructure usage to find common ideas and work to create solutions which span multiple domains;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and produce high quality written proposals, communications and documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute on technical programs that require deep systems and engineering level knowledge;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers, Tech Leads, Engineers and other Technical Program Managers to define, scope and drive large programs to conclusion;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key part in shaping the technical design, predicting technical roadblocks by collaborating with engineers, and identifying trade-offs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and iterate on program management techniques, frameworks, and KPIs to achieve goals with well defined success criteria;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate the execution muscle of engineering teams around you;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train them to be better at delivery where needed;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help influence peers / stakeholders and build consensus while dealing with ambiguity;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data and acquired knowledge to drive strategic decisions at an engineering leadership level;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create widely circulated plans, driving consistency, clarity and building alignment across teams;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize and execute critical cross functional programs spanning multiple engineering organizations for Infrastructure (Developer Infrastructure, Core Infrastructure, Service Infrastructure);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape technical design, predicting technical roadblocks by collaborating with engineers, and identify trade-offs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive programs that span across Stripe in the core infrastructure of Stripe’s payment systems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for the successful definition, cross-functional strategy, planning and execution of large-scale technical programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex problems and enable products and infrastructure at scale;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver exceptional results through building and implementing solutions that scale while protecting our users and serving the business; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate deep technical expertise in software infrastructure (e.g. AWS Cloud Infrastructure, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud, Oracle Cloud, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Engineering, Computer Science, Management Information Systems, or a related field, plus 5 years of progressive, postbaccalaureate experience in Software engineering, systems engineering or technical program management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years experience in Core infrastructure including database, cloud compute, networking and services;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years experience in Program management during all phases of software development from kick-off to launch;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 years experience in Service Oriented Architecture (SOA);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years experience in software architecture and systems design;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years experience in technical program management in software infrastructure;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years experience in cloud infrastructure in compute, networking, databases, or service frameworks; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 year experience in SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $173,400 - $260,200&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;100% Telecommuting Permitted.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Up to 10% Domestic and International travel required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. &lt;strong&gt;CA41.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
