88761734:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenFX is on a mission to &lt;strong&gt;move money as freely as data, unrestricted by time zones, banking hours, or legacy systems.&lt;/strong&gt; We are building the infrastructure that will power the next generation of cross-border payment systems for institutions. The team&#39;s execution has been exceptional, and we&#39;re scaling at a remarkable pace. Our stellar early team brings experience at companies such as J.P. Morgan, Goldman Sachs, FalconX, PayPal, Affirm, Polygon, Kraken, Nium &amp;amp; others. We&#39;re backed by Accel, Lightspeed, NfX, and other top-tier investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an &lt;strong&gt;BDM Manager, North America&lt;/strong&gt; to join our dynamic go-to-market team. You&#39;ll own the full sales cycle for institutional customers across North America — from prospecting through close, helping banks, fintechs, and other institutions move money faster and more efficiently across borders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Business Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a pipeline of institutional prospects across North America, from initial outreach through qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize target accounts — banks, fintechs, and other institutions with cross-border payment needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Cycle Sales Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own deals end-to-end: discovery, solution design, negotiation, and close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently meet or exceed quarterly and annual revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate pipeline and forecast data in the CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client &amp;amp; Stakeholder Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with senior stakeholders (Treasury, Finance, Payments, and Operations leaders) at prospective and existing clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic advisor, understanding each client&#39;s cross-border payment needs and tailoring OpenFX&#39;s value proposition accordingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Legal &amp;amp; Compliance, and Marketing to navigate technical integrations and structure deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leadership to refine sales strategy, messaging, and positioning as the go-to-market motion matures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Strategy &amp;amp; Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to trends in cross-border payments and institutional finance to inform territory and account strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share client feedback with Product to help shape the roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of full-cycle, quota-carrying sales experience in fintech or payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of meeting or exceeding revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from prospecting to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, negotiation, and executive presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with ambiguity in a fast-moving, early-stage environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with CRM tools (e.g., Hubspot) for pipeline and forecast management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What helps you stand out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into banks, fintechs, or other financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in cross-border payments, FX, treasury, or related infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at an early-stage or high-growth startup, helping build sales process and playbooks from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing network of relevant buyer personas within target institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and benefits package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in a rapidly growing company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work in a fast-paced startup at the forefront of fintech innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to make a significant impact on global financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative work culture with emphasis on personal and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;

