&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with senior stakeholders (Treasury, Finance, Payments, and Operations leaders) at prospective and existing clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic advisor, understanding each client&#39;s cross-border payment needs and tailoring OpenFX&#39;s value proposition accordingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Legal &amp;amp; Compliance, and Marketing to navigate technical integrations and structure deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leadership to refine sales strategy, messaging, and positioning as the go-to-market motion matures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Strategy &amp;amp; Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to trends in cross-border payments and institutional finance to inform territory and account strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share client feedback with Product to help shape the roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of full-cycle, quota-carrying sales experience in fintech or payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of meeting or exceeding revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from prospecting to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, negotiation, and executive presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with ambiguity in a fast-moving, early-stage environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with CRM tools (e.g., Hubspot) for pipeline and forecast management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What helps you stand out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into banks, fintechs, or other financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in cross-border payments, FX, treasury, or related infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at an early-stage or high-growth startup, helping build sales process and playbooks from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing network of relevant buyer personas within target institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and benefits package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in a rapidly growing company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work in a fast-paced startup at the forefront of fintech innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to make a significant impact on global financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative work culture with emphasis on personal and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;

88777001:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Luno is the crypto investment app you can rely on, enabling you to buy, store and explore crypto securely. We’re committed to putting the power of cryptocurrency in everyone&#39;s hands sensibly and responsibly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2013, we’ve helped millions of people around the world invest safely in crypto. We do this by cutting through the hype and supporting customers at every step of the way. All products and cryptocurrencies on our platform must first meet stringent legal, risk and technical security standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Transparency is key for us. Luno stores all crypto on a 1:1 basis and we have rigorous processes in place so you can be confident your investment is secure. We’re available in more than 40 countries around the world and we work closely with respective regulators in all of these markets to be fully compliant, as we believe this is the best way to help everyone, everywhere, invest safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role in a nutshell:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a front-line trading seat on Luno&#39;s OTC desk in South Africa, reporting to the Head of Trading. You&#39;ll price, execute and risk-manage large trades for customers who already trade with us in size — institutions, corporates and professional traders — in one of the world&#39;s most active crypto-fiat markets. Sitting within our Treasury team, you&#39;ll work with the rest of the OTC desk, in-country teams and relationship managers to turn that flow into a consistently profitable book.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s a mid-level role built to grow. We intend to lead every market we operate in, and we&#39;re building the desk&#39;s future leadership from within: you&#39;ll start by running South African flow, take on new markets and strategies as we expand, and step toward senior desk leadership as the trading business scales. If your ambition is to one day run a desk, this is where you build the track record and client franchise to get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission will be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;- Own the client book&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the voice of the desk for institutional customers and VIP traders: price and quote large OTC trades, source counter-trades, and execute with speed and discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build durable relationships with those clients alongside our country teams and relationship managers — the goal is repeat flow, not one-off tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the desk&#39;s working capital, ensuring anticipated trades are pre-funded or backed by adequate credit facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own trade disputes end-to-end, and work with Trade Operations to settle every trade cleanly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;- Run execution and risk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute across the book — OTC trades, counter-trades, and market counter-trades when matched flow falls through — always within approved trading strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hedge Luno&#39;s market risk on its working capital and revenue streams, and execute revenue liquidation trades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the desk&#39;s P&amp;amp;L against targets and risk limits — you&#39;ll know your numbers cold and be able to defend every line of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;- Shape trading strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the development of trading strategies across crypto and FX — OTC, hedging and revenue liquidation today; derivatives, arbitrage and warehousing as the desk matures — with risk management and profitability at the core.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;- Read the market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce in-depth analysis of digital asset markets: trends, opportunities and risks, plus the news, regulatory shifts and flows that move prices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver the daily market read to the Treasury team, and push your insights into decisions made across Luno.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;- Report with rigour&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of trades, P&amp;amp;L, risk and performance metrics — an auditable book is a credible book.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce regular stakeholder reporting on trading activity, performance and market insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;- Build the desk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spec improvements to Luno&#39;s trading and risk systems and shape our push into automation — helping us evolve from manual execution to a scaled, systematic operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pressure-test our risk frameworks and models, and make the case for changes as market dynamics shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A little about you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of trading experience within a brokerage or sell-side OTC trading desk in crypto (preferred), FX, equities or derivatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s in Finance, Economics, Mathematics, Business Administration, Accounting or related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derivatives arbitrage knowledge or experience would be a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An advanced degree or professional qualification (CFA, CAIA, MBA) in a related field is beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A successful broking / OTC trading track record across more than one market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambition to grow with the desk — you see this role as a step toward broader market ownership and, in time, trading leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt to a fast-paced and dynamic trading environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with regulatory standards and a commitment to ethical trading practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and accuracy in trade execution and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, a strong team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Friendly, transparent, articulate and driven to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Luno:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote but reachable work policy gives you the freedom to choose between working from home or the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus the option to buy and sell up to 5 days leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve body and mind, with excellent private medical insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Learnably and our additional learning platforms for your personal and professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 months primary care-giver leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paw-ternity leave for your furry friend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Inspiration Day in addition to your annual leave which increases based on your length of service!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, friendly work community, with regular social events and virtual cooking, dancing, drawing and house planting classes hosted by our Lunauts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch and snacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0 fees up to a certain amount with Luno from the day you start.*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Offer only available on Luno Instant Buy, not Luno Exchange.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

88784807:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re making Africa the first cashless continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2017, over half the population in Sub-Saharan Africa had no bank account. That&#39;s for good reason—the fees are too high, the closest branch can be miles away, and nobody takes cards. Without access to financial institutions, people are forced to keep their savings under the mattress. Small business owners rely on lenders who charge extortionate rates. Parents spend hours waiting in line to pay school fees in cash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re solving this by building financial services that just work: no account fees, instantly available, and accepted everywhere. In places where electricity, water and roads don&#39;t always work, you can still send money with Wave. In 2017, we launched a mobile app in Senegal for cash deposit, withdrawal, and peer-to-peer and business payments. Now, we have millions of users across 9 countries and are growing fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to make Africa the first cashless continent and that&#39;s where you come in...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;How you&#39;ll help us achieve it&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a CTO who wants to own engineering end to end: the systems, the people, and the standards for a company whose work changes lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep us moving fast as we get bigger: We deliberately favour fewer processes, simple designs, and deeply understood tools, because that&#39;s what lets a small team operate a system this important. Your job is to protect that as the headcount grows and ensure more ownership per engineer, and a clear view of where complexity is worth the tradeoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own reliability: Wave is the financial system for tens of millions of people. You&#39;ll set the standards for uptime, incident response, and how carefully we change things that move money and you&#39;ll be accountable when we fall short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the leadership layer: You&#39;ll inherit 5 direct reports and an engineering organization of ~132 people including security, data and infrastructure. You will be responsible for hiring, developing, and where necessary replacing engineering managers and directors. You&#39;ll be personally involved in senior hiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set our vision on AI: Set our vision on AI. We’re already seeing AI accelerate product velocity, but we think we’re in the early days of what we can do with AI in our apps and to move faster across the org. We want you to make Wave a truly AI forward organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support expansion. Wave already has over 25M users with accelerating growth. This scale and each new market brings new challenges and constraints. You’ll help us plan the right architecture and organizational structure to help us grow smoothly and consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent engineering to the company. Wave is very transparent, whether that’s defaulting to public conversations in slack, frequent Ask Wave Anything sessions, or defaulting to writing public docs to explain major decisions. You&#39;ll communicate openly and clearly about what engineering is doing and why, to an audience that includes engineers, non-engineers, our leadership team, and our when needed regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Drew Durbin, CEO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Around ~132 engineers across 5 teams (Payment, User-facing products, Internal, non-product teams and platform) plus 5 leaders. Engineering teams are co-led by Product Managers and an engineering manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Python 3 with mypy on the backend, GraphQL API layer, Postgres and Redis, Kotlin/Jetpack on Android (our main client), Swift/SwiftUI on iOS, TypeScript and React on the web. Infrastructure on GCP, managed with Kubernetes and Terraform. Most backend work happens in a large Python monolith, deployed across multi-country architecture. Current in-flight work includes agentic developer tooling, a large scale migration of our databases, and some refactoring of our monolith.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This is a fully remote role. Candidates must be based in one of our talent hub countries (Spain, UK, East Coast of USA, Canada, Kenya, Ghana) or in one of our operating markets in Africa including Senegal, Côte d&#39;Ivoire, or Burkina Faso etc. Expect to travel to our markets a minimum of twice per year to stay close to local realities, products, teams and of course our users. Wave covers all costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;Our salaries are competitive and are calculated using a transparent formula. For this role, depending on your level and location, we offer a salary of up to $356,500 USD, plus a generous equity package:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wave provides a yearly $1,200 stipend to support coworking meetups with teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Major benefits:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized health insurance for you and your dependents and retirement contributions (both vary from country to country).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 months of fully paid parental leave and subsidized fertility assistance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation, with most folks taking between 21-30 days exclusive of statutory holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$10,000 annual charitable donation matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process: &lt;/strong&gt;The process runs up to 5 conversations, including 2 technical discussions. We want this to be a 2-way assessment: as much a chance for you to evaluate us as for us to get to know you. Along the way you&#39;ll meet our CEO, Head of People, Head of Product, both Engineering Directors, and a senior leader from one of our markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve managed an engineering organization of at ~100 people, including managers who manage others. You can describe how your own job changed as the org grew.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a software engineering background and are good at it. You can still read code and follow a technical argument to the end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve been accountable for a system where failure was expensive: money, safety, or regulated data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve hired senior engineering leaders, and you&#39;ve moved someone out of a role that wasn&#39;t working. You can talk about both honestly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write well. Clear, short, and persuasive, for readers who aren&#39;t engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a clear and positive point of view on AI in engineering: something you&#39;ve tried, changed, or abandoned, not a plan to look into it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You believe in what we&#39;re building and can say why without being prompted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-preserver-spaces=&quot;true&quot;&gt;You might be a good fit if you&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Would rather run a great team than be the smartest engineer in the room, and don&#39;t feel a loss in that trade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable being the person who says the unwelcome thing in a meeting, and can do it without making it personal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change your mind in public when the evidence changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prefer the simplest system that works to the most interesting one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care about what our users actually experience: how long a transfer takes on a bad network, what happens to a shop owner when a deposit fails and bring that up unprompted when discussing infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility for outcomes rather than processes, including when the outcome is bad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are drawn to a company that publishes its numbers internally every month, expects direct feedback in both directions, and would rather be embarrassingly honest than comfortable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We have a rapidly growing in-country team in Senegal, Côte d&#39;Ivoire, Mali, Burkina Faso, The Gambia, Uganda, Niger, Sierra Leone, and Cameroon plus remote team members spread across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We&#39;re deeply passionate about our mission of bringing radically affordable financial services to the people who need them most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We foster autonomy for our employees. You&#39;ll own your projects at every stage, from understanding the problem to monitoring your solution in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We raised the largest Series A in Africa in 2021. Our world-class investors, include Founders Fund, Sequoia Heritage, Stripe, Ribbit Capital, Y Combinator, and Partech Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We are on&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.ycombinator.com/topcompanies/revenue&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.ycombinator.com/topcompanies/revenue&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Y Combinator&#39;s top companies by revenue&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How to apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fill out the form below, and upload a resume in English and a&amp;nbsp;cover letter describing your interest in Wave and the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We review applications frequently and recommend that you apply to the role that most closely aligns with your skills, experience and career goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wave is an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

88822045:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like PayPal Ventures, Paradigm, and Galaxy Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh is looking for an exceptional leader to build and scale our Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) organization — a new function at the company, starting with you. We have a strong preference for someone who resides in the New York City area or San Francisco.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to our CTO, you&#39;ll lead a team of senior engineers who embed directly with a small, capped set of our most strategic partners — exchanges, neobanks, and prediction markets that drive the lion&#39;s share of our volume. These partners aren&#39;t buying a static product off the shelf. They&#39;re buying working crypto rails inside their product, against their brokers, their compliance posture, and their release schedule. The gap between a demo that works and a production integration that survives contact with a partner&#39;s environment is where deals stall, and where generic support queues and quarterly roadmap cycles fail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our thesis is simple: FDE sits inside Engineering, not in a services org. An FDE ships code that lands in the account and when it generalizes in our core platform. Engagements are time-boxed with a clear &quot;ship something working end-to-end&quot; milestone — not open-ended residencies. And the function stays deliberately small. The moment it needs a manager of managers, it has stopped being FDE and become consulting with an engineering badge. Holding that line is a core part of the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires equal parts technical judgment, commercial acumen, and organizational leadership. You need to be technical enough to earn immediate credibility with a partner&#39;s top engineers, scope an integration live on a call, and call out a bad architectural decision — but your leverage comes from the team you build and the alignment you drive, not from the code you personally write.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and scale the FDE organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the operating model: engagement shape, deployment cadence, scoping standards, and hiring bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire at least 2-3 senior and staff-level generalists this year placed close to the partner engineering team and timezone they support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be open to running the first engagement(s) yourself to prove the playbook, then scale it through the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own delivery at our most strategic accounts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the person a partner&#39;s VP of Engineering or CTO calls — run integration reviews, hold commitments, and turn stalled technical conversations into signed plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assign named owners, not a rotating pool: one engineer or small pod per account, with a mapped executive sponsor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the qualification bar. FDE is justified when integration is the bottleneck, the account can absorb a dedicated engineer, speed decides the deal, or the pattern generalizes to the next ten partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the boundary with Customer Success, who own the relationship, and Support, who own break-fix. CS flags what an account needs; you decide whether it&#39;s an FDE build, a platform ask, or neither&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure partner growth, volume, and time-to-production — not tickets closed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape product and platform strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn the sharpest signal in the company — what partners need in production — into scoped, prioritized platform input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce the productization ratchet: what&#39;s built either generalizes into our shared platform inside a defined window, or we stop re-investing in it. Guard against both failure modes — a silent per-customer fork, and a core roadmap hijacked by one-off asks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reference architectures, QA, and monitoring that catch failure modes inside the integration rather than in a support queue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership and team building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in technical roles, with 4+ years leading forward-deployed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a 0→1 organization or a new service line inside an existing company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of attracting, developing, and retaining senior engineers in a competitive market, including personally closing candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical credibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You came up as a strong backend or integrations engineer and can still read a codebase, whiteboard a system, debug a design, and review architecture alongside your team. You are not expected to be in the codebase day to day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience with broker, exchange, or payments integration patterns and crypto rails. Our partners&#39; engineers will spot someone learning the domain on the job in the first meeting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of embedding with customer engineering teams to deliver complex technical work in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial and strategic acumen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence — effective and composed in front of partner executives and our own leadership team, including when an integration is on fire&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-facing instincts: you like being in front of partners, can read a room, and can separate the stated ask from the real constraint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to push back. You&#39;ve declined bad requests from partners and internal stakeholders alike, and driven alignment across engineering, revenue, and product without escalating every disagreement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining engagement models, scoping, and pricing for technical delivery work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $282,000 - $355,000, plus equity, in New York or San Francisco. The compensation range provided may span multiple career levels and will be narrowed during the interview process based on factors including a candidate&#39;s experience, skills, qualifications, and geographic location. For candidates outside of New York or San Francisco, compensation will be adjusted to reflect the applicable market and location-based pay band. The base salary range listed excludes commission (if applicable), equity, and benefits. The pay range represents the minimum and maximum target for new-hire compensation. Actual compensation may vary and may be higher or lower depending on individual circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, you&#39;re not stepping into a typical role—you&#39;re joining a rocket ship in mid-liftoff. You&#39;ll tackle complex, meaningful problems that actually move an industry forward, working alongside a sharp, motivated team that moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and expects everyone to operate with ownership. This is the kind of place where you&#39;ll see your work ship fast, make real impact, and be able to point to something and say, &quot;I built that.&quot; You&#39;ll grow fast, level up your skills, and get a front-row seat to how a high-growth company scales from the inside, with competitive comp, solid benefits, and room to stretch your craft all coming standard. If you&#39;re energized by building, learning, and shaping something big—this is where you&#39;ll want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, New York, and Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; hubs are expected to work from the office at least 40% of the time (approximately two days per week). This expectation may vary slightly depending on role, team, and business needs. Certain roles that require closer cross-functional collaboration or operational support may have additional in-office requirements, which will be discussed during the interview process. Our hybrid approach is designed to balance meaningful in-person collaboration, team building, and real-time decision-making with the flexibility to work remotely. We believe this structure supports strong execution while preserving autonomy and focus time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Care For Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel valued and supported. That starts with competitive salary and equity that grows as you and the company grow, plus comprehensive health coverage for you and your family. We offer unlimited PTO—and we mean it. Take the time you need to recharge and show up at your best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re invested in your growth with a dedicated budget for courses, conferences, and certifications. Work from wherever you&#39;re most productive with our remote-friendly approach, and count on having the top-tier tools and equipment you need to do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh Pay is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, genetic information, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, lawful alien status, national origin, age, marital status, and non-job related physical or mental disability, or protected veteran status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

88930091:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re making Africa the first cashless continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2017, over half the population in Sub-Saharan Africa had no bank account. That&#39;s for good reason—the fees are too high, the closest branch can be miles away, and nobody takes cards. Without access to financial institutions, people are forced to keep their savings under the mattress. Small business owners rely on lenders who charge extortionate rates. Parents spend hours waiting in line to pay school fees in cash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re solving this by building financial services that just work: no account fees, instantly available, and accepted everywhere. In places where electricity, water and roads don&#39;t always work, you can still send money with Wave. In 2017, we launched a mobile app in Senegal for cash deposit, withdrawal, and peer-to-peer and business payments. Now, we have millions of users across 9 countries and are growing fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to make Africa the first cashless continent and that&#39;s where you come in...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you&#39;ll help us achieve it&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to help reshape the future of payments in Mali? We&#39;re looking for an exceptional sales professional who is energized by ambitious goals, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and is excited to help businesses embrace a cashless future. You&#39;ll lead the adoption of Wave&#39;s payment and business solutions among key corporate clients, accelerating our growth across Mali.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Key Account Lead, you will be part of the sales team responsible for prospecting and acquiring new high-revenue business customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Development (Prospecting):&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively identify and target high-potential companies and organizations (large corporations, structured SMEs, NGOs, government institutions) that can use Wave Business services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a robust sales pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sales Cycle Management:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct sales presentations and product demonstrations for decision-makers (CFOs, CEOs, HR Directors).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand client needs in-depth to propose customized solutions (e.g., salary payments, supplier payment collection, invoice collection).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate contract terms and ensure closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on key sales performance indicators (KPIs) using our CRM tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide structured field feedback to the Product and Marketing teams to improve our Business offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct competitive intelligence on the Business offerings of other players (banks, telcos).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: You&#39;ll work from our office in Bamako and may travel to upcountry locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work authorization in Mali is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a permanent position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our salaries are competitive and calculated using a transparent formula.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer generous health insurance for yourself and your dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We support working parents by offering 26 weeks of parental leave for mothers and 4 weeks for fathers, in addition to subsidized childcare when they return to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Airtime reimbursement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free food and a beautiful office space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience in a similar position (ideally in an international company, a bank, a mobile money company, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in sales, project management, finance, international relations, business management, or a comparable field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good command of:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French: Fluent (spoken and written) - Primary working language.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English: Professional proficiency required to communicate with regional teams and management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have complete mastery of the B2B sales cycle, from prospecting to negotiating complex contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an existing and relevant professional network in Abidjan (particularly with CFOs, HR Directors, and CEOs of large companies).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent communication, active listening skills, and persuasive ability. You know how to adapt your discourse for high-level stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are &quot;mission-driven,&quot; have an appetite for challenge, and a demonstrated culture of performance (a track record of exceeding targets).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to work proactively and organized in a very dynamic and fast-paced start-up environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We have a rapidly growing in-country team in Senegal, Côte d&#39;Ivoire, Mali, Burkina Faso, The Gambia, Uganda, Niger, Sierra Leone, and Cameroon plus remote team members spread across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We&#39;re deeply passionate about our mission of bringing radically affordable financial services to the people who need them most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We foster autonomy for our employees. You&#39;ll own your projects at every stage, from understanding the problem to monitoring your solution in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We raised the largest Series A in Africa in 2021. Our world-class investors, include Founders Fund, Sequoia Heritage, Stripe, Ribbit Capital, Y Combinator, and Partech Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We are on&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.ycombinator.com/topcompanies/revenue&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.ycombinator.com/topcompanies/revenue&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Y Combinator&#39;s top companies by revenue&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How to apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fill out the form below, and upload a resume in English and a&amp;nbsp;cover letter describing your interest in Wave and the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We review applications frequently and recommend that you apply to the role that most closely aligns with your skills, experience and career goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wave is an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

88998814:
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;OpenFX is on a mission to move money as freely as data, unrestricted by time zones, banking hours, or legacy systems. We are building the infrastructure that will power the next generation of cross-border payment systems for institutions. The team&#39;s execution has been exceptional, and we&#39;re scaling at a remarkable pace. Our stellar early team comes with experience in companies like J.P. Morgan, Goldman Sachs, FalconX, PayPal, Affirm, Polygon, Kraken, Nium &amp;amp; others. We&#39;re backed by Accel, Lightspeed, NfX and other top-tier investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;OpenFX processes billions of dollars in transaction volume every month across global corridors. The Growth pod owns everything a client touches before and while they become a paying, trading customer: the public API they integrate against, the onboarding and verification journey that gets them approved, the activation surface that gets them to their first trade, and the marketing site that brings them in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Client onboarding runs today on third-party tooling and is being brought in-house, which means rebuilding KYB and KYC as our own product rather than a vendor workflow. And onboarding policy is still effectively global, when the business needs requirements that vary by jurisdiction and customer segment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Every point of friction across those surfaces is a client who does not activate, or who activates slowly and expensively. The work is also unusually dependency-heavy: nearly every onboarding item depends on Compliance and Legal, the API programme depends on Platform, Payments, Banking, and Client Trading, and the website work depends on Brand Design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;We need an Engineering Manager who can hold four surfaces at once, ship inside a stage-gated product process without letting it become theatre, and keep a correctness bar on flows that touch identity, compliance, and the money path.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;If we do not solve this well, activation stays gated on manual work and vendor tooling, and growth stays bottlenecked on ad hoc engineering requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Run the Growth pod of roughly 6 to 10 engineers and QA across frontend, backend, and integrations. You own the roadmap, the delivery, and the standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Own the API as a product. Land the V3 overhaul, our largest and most cross-dependent programme, while V2 stays supported. Ship client-facing API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Bring onboarding in-house. Move the client onboarding experience off third-party tools onto OpenFX, and build the rules engine that replaces global policy with dynamic KYB and KYC requirements by jurisdiction and customer segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Extend onboarding to new segments — self-serve signup through to first trade with no sales touch, enterprise (large entities, directors, UBO, bespoke verification), channel partners and platform-of-platforms, multi-product onboarding across banking and payments, and eventually agent-based customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Own the activation surface: digital signatures, in-product activation checklists, recovery and lifecycle client comms, and a self-serve notification centre.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Own the marketing site as a growth surface, partnering with Brand Design and the visual explainers that both generate market intelligence and give sales what they need to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Run the product development process credibly. Take work from discovery through solution, design, and RFC validation into delivery and beta, own or assign RFCs, and hold the design-ready and delivery-ready gates so nothing enters a sprint half-shaped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Manage a dependency-saturated roadmap. Compliance, Legal, Platform, Payments, Banking, Currencies, TPV, Client Trading, Brand Design, and GTM all sit on your critical path. Sequencing around them is a core part of the job, not an interruption to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Own the interface with GTM and Product: one intake for growth and sales requests, joint prioritisation with the Growth PM, and an expedite lane whose cost in displaced work is explicit rather than silently absorbed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Stay hands-on. You review designs, and you still write and ship code, debug production, and set the implementation bar by example, including the standard for AI-assisted development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Hold the bar where correctness is not optional: identity and KYC deduplication, idempotency on quote and trade paths, permission and compliance boundaries, money precision and rounding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Hire and grow the team: close open roles, grow your team, run 30-60-90 ramps, set explicit performance expectations, and act on them early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;EM-level scope: 2 or more years managing a full team of 5 or more, with a Tech Lead or senior IC reporting in, on top of a strong individual contributor track record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Still writes code. You can design an API, model a schema, and produce idiomatic, runnable, tested code. Design fluency without hands-on ability is not enough at this level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Experience owning a public or partner-facing API as a product, including versioning and running an old and a new major version side by side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Shipped client-facing product end to end, including the unglamorous parts: migrations, deprecations, and error states.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Has delivered against Compliance and Legal as hard dependencies, not as a review step at the end. Onboarding at OpenFX is a compliance surface first and a product surface second.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Comfortable running a stage-gated product process — discovery, solution and design validation, RFC, delivery — without letting it slow the team down or become box-ticking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Can take a one-line placeholder and turn it into shaped, sized, sequenced work. A large share of the forward roadmap is deliberately undefined.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Demonstrated hiring and performance management, including at least one underperformance case you saw through to an outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Has worked directly with Product and a commercial or GTM function, and can say no with a reason that holds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;High agency: operates with low oversight on ambiguous problems, in a demanding environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Can articulate and enforce a correctness bar under commercial time pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What helps you stand out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Fintech, payments, or another regulated domain where onboarding is a compliance surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;KYB and KYC in production, and replacing a vendor onboarding or verification workflow with an in-house build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Jurisdiction-aware or segment-aware policy engines, where requirements are configuration rather than code branches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Developer experience work: API documentation, SDKs, sandbox environments, webhook delivery, or developer funnels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Activation and lifecycle engineering: in-product onboarding checklists, transactional and lifecycle comms, notification preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Marketing site or growth-experiment engineering in partnership with Brand Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Growth instrumentation and analytics tooling, and comfort reading a funnel yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Onboarding for enterprise entities (directors, UBO) or for channel partners and platform-of-platforms models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Share of TPV through the API, with a target of 60%. The V3 overhaul, webhook reliability, and API observability are the levers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Activated customers, with a target of 200+. Onboarding, digital signatures, and the activation surface are the levers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Annualised TPV, contributing to an annualised $250B dollar goal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Zero lights-out compliance and financial crime findings on the flows you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Predictable delivery: commitments land on the dates given, and when they slip you flag it early with a revised plan rather than late with an explanation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Dependencies land: work with Compliance, Legal, Platform, and Brand Design closes on schedule because you drove it, not because it happened to unblock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Discovery converts: ambiguous placeholder initiatives become shaped, sized, RFC-validated work rather than sitting at low confidence for a quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Quality on the identity and money path: onboarding and API defects are caught by tests and monitoring, not by clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Team strength: fully staffed and ramped, your Tech Lead is growing, strong performers stay, and weak performance is addressed rather than tolerated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Talent magnetism: you bring strong engineers with you and raise the bar of every loop you sit on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;Why This Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
