88998818:
&lt;h2&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenFX is on a mission to move money as freely as data, unrestricted by time zones, banking hours, or legacy systems. We are building the infrastructure that will power the next generation of cross-border payment systems for institutions. The team&#39;s execution has been exceptional, and we&#39;re scaling at a remarkable pace. Our stellar early team comes with experience in companies like J.P. Morgan, Goldman Sachs, FalconX, Paypal, Affirm, Polygon, Kraken, Nium &amp;amp; others. We&#39;re backed by Accel, Lightspeed, NfX and other top-tier investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior Backend Engineer for our Hedging team — the team that owns the risk OpenFX carries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hedging owns inventory and exposure management, risk management, hedging positions across venues through smart routing strategies, market making, Cost, PnL and net revenue calculation. Every trade a client places creates exposure, and this team decides what we hold, what we hedge, where we hedge it, and what it costs us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own significant parts of the Risk Management Engine and Smart Hedging end-to-end — design, build, ship, and operate. This is a hands-on senior IC role with high ownership and accountability - the routing and exposure logic you write today shows up in tomorrow&#39;s net revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re specifically looking for someone with a trading background — you&#39;ve built systems where a position had to be accurate and a hedge had to fire in time, and where a bug meant real money. Think a crypto exchange, brokerage, or trading platform (CoinDCX, Groww, CoinSwitch Kuber, or similar).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate services across the risk path — inventory and exposure tracking, hedge decisioning, venue routing, and WAC / PnL / net revenue calculation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end-to-end: scoping, technical design, delivery, rollout, and the operational health of what you ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive work to closure with Product, Design, and Operations. You are accountable for adoption, not just delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a product engineer — scope a problem statement, understand its product impact, and take the hard prioritisation calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build for correctness and timeliness on a live risk path. Understand and weigh trade offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with external venues and liquidity providers, and build smart routing strategies that hold up when a venue degrades or goes away.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument what you build — logging, metrics, and alerting that make exposure, positions and hedge behaviour predictable in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for failure: retries, idempotency, reconciliation, and safe recovery when a venue or downstream dependency misbehaves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar through code review and design feedback, and mentor L1/L2 engineers on the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a healthy engineering-excellence and tech-debt backlog — surface the right items, work with the EM on a resolution plan, and drive them to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call, respond to incidents with urgency, and turn post-mortems into durable fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with the Trading team, treasury and finance to connect what you build to exposure, risk and net revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6 years of experience building and operating production backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A trading background&lt;/strong&gt; — you&#39;ve worked at a trading company, exchange, or brokerage and have built systems on a live trade, order or risk path (e.g. CoinDCX, Groww, CoinSwitch Kuber, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in system design, data modelling, and API design, with practical experience in distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid command of object-oriented programming principles and low-level design patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid production engineering instincts — observability, debugging complex systems, performance tuning, and incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with money and numbers where being approximately right is not good enough — positions, cost basis and PnL have to reconcile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with &lt;strong&gt;abstract, ambiguous problems&lt;/strong&gt; — you can turn a vague mandate into scoped, sequenced deliverables without waiting for someone to specify it for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on and high agency.&lt;/strong&gt; You find the important problem and go solve it rather than waiting to be assigned it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Heavy AI user.&lt;/strong&gt; You use AI coding tools with real technique and get materially more done because of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-driven&lt;/strong&gt;, and a clear written communicator — we are async-heavy and globally distributed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What helps you stand out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hedging, exposure or risk management systems specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-venue execution, smart order routing, or market making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PnL, cost-basis or position-keeping logic, and reconciliation against external venues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with FX, multi-currency systems, or cross-border payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with market data, order books, or market microstructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The services you own on the risk path are reliable, well-tested, and observable — exposure is accurate, hedges fire as intended, and issues are caught before they cost us money.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You ship complex features end-to-end from technical design to execution, delivery and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The team moves faster because of your code reviews, documentation, and technical judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;L1/L2 engineers around you grow measurably faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You become a go-to engineer for the risk path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You raise the bar for the Hedging team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and benefits package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in a rapidly growing company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work in a fast-paced startup at the forefront of fintech innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to make a significant impact on global financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative work culture with emphasis on personal and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

