&lt;p&gt;You will own the client-facing surface of that experience. This is where an institutional client sees a live quote, understands the price and fees, commits to a trade, and tracks it through to settlement. You will own architecture for these flows — state management, data fetching, error handling, and performance — and be trusted with the correctness of what the client sees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also work across the stack. You&#39;ll build and extend the APIs your surfaces depend on, model the data behind them, and ship the backend piece of a feature rather than waiting on someone else to unblock you. You don&#39;t need deep backend systems experience for this role, but you do need to be genuinely comfortable there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re specifically looking for someone with a trading background. Think a crypto exchange, brokerage, or trading platform (CoinDCX, Groww, CoinSwitch Kuber, or similar).&lt;/p&gt;
