&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture of critical client trade flows — quote and pricing surfaces, trade initiation, and status and settlement tracking — across GUI, API and conversational AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design frontend state and data-fetching patterns, exception handling and retries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive frontend performance and reliability — rendering efficiency under frequent updates, load times, and stability on the flows that carry volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and extend the APIs and data models your surfaces depend on, and ship features end-to-end rather than stopping at the boundary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument the client experience — Error rates, flow completion, and latency — problems are visible before clients report them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Design and Product to shape flows, and with backend engineers to shape API contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive work to closure with Product, Design and Operations. You are accountable for adoption, not just delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a product engineer — scope a problem statement, understand its product impact, and take the hard prioritisation calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar through code review and design feedback, and mentor L1/L2 engineers on the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a healthy engineering-excellence and tech-debt backlog — surface the right items, work with the EM on a resolution plan, and drive them to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call, respond to incidents with urgency, and turn post-mortems into durable fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of experience building production web applications, with the majority of that depth on the frontend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A trading background&lt;/strong&gt; — you&#39;ve worked at a trading company, exchange, or brokerage and have built client-facing systems on a live trade or order path (e.g. CoinDCX, Groww, CoinSwitch Kuber, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript and React&lt;/strong&gt;, and strong command of &lt;strong&gt;Redux&lt;/strong&gt; or equivalent state management on non-trivial applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with &lt;strong&gt;server-side rendering&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;code splitting&lt;/strong&gt;, and a clear sense of when each is worth the cost.&lt;/li&gt;
