89508035:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenFX is on a mission to &lt;strong&gt;move money as freely as data, unrestricted by time zones, banking hours, or legacy systems.&lt;/strong&gt; We are building the infrastructure that will power the next generation of cross-border payment systems for institutions. The team&#39;s execution has been exceptional, and we&#39;re scaling at a remarkable pace. Our stellar early team comes with experience in companies like J.P. Morgan, Goldman Sachs, FalconX, Paypal, Affirm, Polygon, Kraken, Nium &amp;amp; others. We’re backed by Accel, Lightspeed, NfX and other top-tier investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Americas&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Legal Counsel&lt;/strong&gt; to serve as a strategic partner and legal advisor across our business, with a particular focus on financial products and partnerships. This role combines the intellectual challenge of navigating cutting-edge financial technology with the opportunity to shape legal strategy in the early stages at a high-growth company. You&#39;ll work on some of the most complex and interesting problems at the intersection of cross-border payments, cryptocurrency, foreign exchange and technology—providing pragmatic, business-oriented counsel that enables rapid growth while managing risk effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a team player who is energized by a high-growth environment and translating complex legal requirements and legal ambiguity into clear, actionable strategies. You move quickly with sound judgment, and excel as a trusted senior advisor to product, engineering, compliance, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Legal&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise product and engineering teams on the legal and regulatory aspects of product design, development, and launch, with a particular focus on payment and banking products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex regulatory requirements into clear guidance that helps teams build compliant products while growing rapidly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Licensing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with business teams and compliance to develop and execute licensing and market entry strategies across multiple jurisdictions, contributing to and overseeing license applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide practical, forward-thinking regulatory guidance on the complex and evolving regulatory landscape for payments, money transmission, cryptocurrency, foreign exchange, and cross-border transactions across global markets, leveraging local counsel efficiently and effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential regulatory risks and develop creative, pragmatic solutions to mitigate them while achieving business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate &amp;amp; General Legal Matters&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide comprehensive legal support across the full range of corporate legal matters impacting the company, including corporate governance and board matters, employment and HR issues, privacy, intellectual property, fundraising and strategic transactions, and other general corporate legal needs as the business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, assess, and develop mitigation strategies for legal and business risks across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic business partner to leadership, product, engineering, and growth teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external counsel and consultants efficiently to support the business with cost-effective, high-quality legal services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable legal processes and frameworks that support OpenFX&#39;s rapid growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to building a collaborative, high-performing legal function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of legal experience, including significant fintech or financial services background; 15+ years of experience for senior Counsel level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of financial services and payments regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to provide practical, business-oriented legal advice that appropriately balances risk with commercial objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working collaboratively with product, engineering, compliance, and business teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills combining creativity with meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who thrives in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and takes ownership of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills and ability to manage multiple priorities and execute quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD from an accredited law school and bar membership in good standing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What helps you stand out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English and Spanish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience with cryptocurrency and/or Banking as a Service products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup or high-growth company experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience with international regulatory regimes and cross-border transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a humble team player who excels at collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think strategically about legal issues and anticipate challenges before they arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable making sound decisions with imperfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You approach legal work with curiosity and intellectual courage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by solving novel problems at the intersection of law, technology, and finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see legal as an enabler of business growth, not just a risk mitigator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and benefits package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in a rapidly growing company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work in a fast-paced startup at the forefront of fintech innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to make a significant impact on global financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative work culture with emphasis on personal and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

89511713:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like PayPal Ventures, Paradigm, and Galaxy Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh is seeking our first Head of Card Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Crypto solved receiving value. It has not solved spending it. Hundreds of millions of people hold crypto they cannot use to buy fuel or groceries. Every previous fix asked the merchant to change... new software, new assets, new risk... and merchants declined. The result is a vicious cycle: because crypto is not spendable, consumers do not hold much of it. Because consumers do not hold much of it, merchants do not accept it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are breaking the cycle from the other side. A user pays with crypto. The merchant receives an ordinary card payment. Nothing changes at the point of sale, so everything changes for the consumer: crypto becomes spendable at over a hundred million merchants in more than two hundred countries overnight... including the markets where people are already paid in stablecoins and have nowhere to spend them. It stops being an asset you hold and becomes money you use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own this program end-to-end: the consumer experience, the bank partnership, the network relationship, and the compliance framework that makes it real. Card programs are not won with code. They are won by earning the confidence of banks and networks, which is why so few companies can build this. If you have spent your career learning how card programs really work, this is the seat where that knowledge changes what money can do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the card program end to end&lt;/strong&gt;. You are the single accountable owner of this product ... its launch, its growth, its economics. If it touches the program, it&#39;s yours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Earn the confidence of banks and networks&lt;/strong&gt;. You will sit across from bank officers, network compliance teams, and regulators ... in every market the program touches ... and get to yes on KYC, fraud, refunds, and every edge case of how money moves. You write the specificity a bank signs. This is hands-on work, not delegated work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make paying with crypto feel effortless&lt;/strong&gt;. Provisioning a card into a wallet, confirming on device, recovering from a failed or disputed transaction. You decide what the user believes is happening and make every screen and state consistent with that belief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win distribution through wallet partners.&lt;/strong&gt; This product only matters if wallets carry it. You pitch it, shape each integration, and make partners successful ... their volume is the scoreboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decide what cards become at Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;. Today it is one program. New programs, networks, geographies, and commercialization are yours to figure out ... and to argue for at the exec table with evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: You have owned a regulated financial product that shipped through a bank partner or regulator ... a card program, a lending product, a banking or money movement product. Card program experience is a strong plus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Fluency&lt;/strong&gt;: You have earned a compliance sign-off from a bank partner, network, or regulator ... KYC, AML, transaction monitoring, fraud, disputes. You can describe a decision a bank pushed back on and how you got to yes.&amp;nbsp; Experience across multiple markets or regulatory regimes is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumer Product Judgment&lt;/strong&gt;: You have owned a consumer payments or fintech product and its outcome ... volume, activation, retention, or P&amp;amp;L. You can walk through a flow you shipped and the reasoning behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile Payments&lt;/strong&gt;: You have shipped device-level payment experiences ... secure element or secure enclave integration, push provisioning, token requestor work with the networks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Leverage&lt;/strong&gt;: You use AI daily to draft program documentation, model economics, and automate the operational work of running a program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crypto&lt;/strong&gt;: Ideally, you have built products that integrate into crypto wallets like MetaMask, Trust Wallet, or Phantom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $229,000 - $300,000, plus equity, in San Francisco or New York. We have a strong preference for candidates based in San Francisco. The compensation range provided may span multiple career levels and will be narrowed during the interview process based on factors including a candidate&#39;s experience, skills, qualifications, and geographic location. For candidates outside of San Francisco or New York, compensation will be adjusted to reflect the applicable market and location-based pay band. The base salary range listed excludes equity, and benefits. The pay range represents the minimum and maximum target for new-hire compensation. Actual compensation may vary and may be higher or lower depending on individual circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, you&#39;re not stepping into a typical role—you&#39;re joining a rocket ship in mid-liftoff. You&#39;ll tackle complex, meaningful problems that actually move an industry forward, working alongside a sharp, motivated team that moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and expects everyone to operate with ownership. This is the kind of place where you&#39;ll see your work ship fast, make real impact, and be able to point to something and say, &quot;I built that.&quot; You&#39;ll grow fast, level up your skills, and get a front-row seat to how a high-growth company scales from the inside, with competitive comp, solid benefits, and room to stretch your craft all coming standard. If you&#39;re energized by building, learning, and shaping something big—this is where you&#39;ll want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, New York, and Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; hubs are expected to work from the office at least 40% of the time (approximately two days per week). This expectation may vary slightly depending on role, team, and business needs. Certain roles that require closer cross-functional collaboration or operational support may have additional in-office requirements, which will be discussed during the interview process. Our hybrid approach is designed to balance meaningful in-person collaboration, team building, and real-time decision-making with the flexibility to work remotely. We believe this structure supports strong execution while preserving autonomy and focus time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Care For Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel valued and supported. That starts with competitive salary and equity that grows as you and the company grow, plus comprehensive health coverage for you and your family. We offer unlimited PTO—and we mean it. Take the time you need to recharge and show up at your best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re invested in your growth with a dedicated budget for courses, conferences, and certifications. Work from wherever you&#39;re most productive with our remote-friendly approach, and count on having the top-tier tools and equipment you need to do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh Pay is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, genetic information, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, lawful alien status, national origin, age, marital status, and non-job related physical or mental disability, or protected veteran status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

89511714:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like PayPal Ventures, Paradigm, and Galaxy Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh is seeking an exceptional Head of Design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A great crypto payments product is deceptively simple: pick an asset, pay, done. But we serve everyone from prediction markets to crypto exchanges to neobanks, and the user&#39;s mental model shifts with the merchant ... sometimes they&#39;re thinking in dollars, sometimes in ETH. Underneath, crypto is deeply fragmented ... hundreds of wallets, dozens of exchanges and networks ... so the product must quietly swap, bridge, and pay fees just to work. Every seam the user sees is a moment of hesitation, and in payments, hesitation is death. Your job is to design one system that absorbs all of this and disappears. Then go further ... rewards, just-in-time lending, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To succeed in this role, the thinking comes first. Before any pixels, someone has to decide what the user believes is happening ... and make every screen, state, and word consistent with that belief. You must be world class at that, and world class at the craft itself. This is a hands-on role. You will also build and lead the team. Crypto and payments experience is nice to have; exceptional design is mandatory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the end-to-end Mesh experience. &lt;/strong&gt;The consumer app, and every merchant surface ... from first impression to failure states, error recovery, and support handoffs. If a person sees it, it&#39;s yours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own design&#39;s hardest problems, hands-on.&lt;/strong&gt; Which mental model each merchant type gets, what we standardize versus customize, when a flow ships versus needs another pass ... and the flows where those decisions live: deposits, swaps, bridging, fiat on-ramps, failure recovery. You are the tiebreaker on experience questions, and roughly half your time is in the work itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the team.&lt;/strong&gt; Manage, coach, and grow the designers on the team today, and hire as we scale. You set the bar for design talent at Mesh ... and you build the team that can hold it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reinvent design for the AI era.&lt;/strong&gt; AI is changing what a designer produces, how fast, and what&#39;s worth doing by hand. Decide how design works at Mesh ... the tools, the workflows, the ratio of prototypes to specs ... and evolve the function ahead of the curve, not behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent design at the exec table.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring evidence-backed positions to roadmap and customer decisions with the CEO, CTO, and SVP Product. Design is in the room where direction gets set ... you are that presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 8+ years in product design, including 3+ years leading designers while staying hands-on. You have shipped consumer products at scale and can show the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Stakes&lt;/strong&gt;: A track record of designing for complex systems where users really care when it doesn&#39;t work ... money movement, health, infrastructure, etc. Your portfolio holds up under failure, not just on the happy path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First-Principles Thinking&lt;/strong&gt;: You originate the frame, you don&#39;t just execute it. You can point to products where the conceptual model was yours ... and explain the alternatives you rejected and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Influence&lt;/strong&gt;: You have changed the direction of a roadmap with a design argument, with executives and engineering leaders in the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Leverage&lt;/strong&gt;: You use AI aggressively in your own practice and are rethinking what design work is still worth doing by hand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain&lt;/strong&gt;: Payments or fintech experience is a plus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $229,000 - $300,000, plus equity, in San Francisco or New York. We have a strong preference for candidates based in San Francisco. The compensation range provided may span multiple career levels and will be narrowed during the interview process based on factors including a candidate&#39;s experience, skills, qualifications, and geographic location. For candidates outside of San Francisco or New York, compensation will be adjusted to reflect the applicable market and location-based pay band. The base salary range listed excludes equity, and benefits. The pay range represents the minimum and maximum target for new-hire compensation. Actual compensation may vary and may be higher or lower depending on individual circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, you&#39;re not stepping into a typical role—you&#39;re joining a rocket ship in mid-liftoff. You&#39;ll tackle complex, meaningful problems that actually move an industry forward, working alongside a sharp, motivated team that moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and expects everyone to operate with ownership. This is the kind of place where you&#39;ll see your work ship fast, make real impact, and be able to point to something and say, &quot;I built that.&quot; You&#39;ll grow fast, level up your skills, and get a front-row seat to how a high-growth company scales from the inside, with competitive comp, solid benefits, and room to stretch your craft all coming standard. If you&#39;re energized by building, learning, and shaping something big—this is where you&#39;ll want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, New York, and Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; hubs are expected to work from the office at least 40% of the time (approximately two days per week). This expectation may vary slightly depending on role, team, and business needs. Certain roles that require closer cross-functional collaboration or operational support may have additional in-office requirements, which will be discussed during the interview process. Our hybrid approach is designed to balance meaningful in-person collaboration, team building, and real-time decision-making with the flexibility to work remotely. We believe this structure supports strong execution while preserving autonomy and focus time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Care For Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel valued and supported. That starts with competitive salary and equity that grows as you and the company grow, plus comprehensive health coverage for you and your family. We offer unlimited PTO—and we mean it. Take the time you need to recharge and show up at your best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re invested in your growth with a dedicated budget for courses, conferences, and certifications. Work from wherever you&#39;re most productive with our remote-friendly approach, and count on having the top-tier tools and equipment you need to do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh Pay is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, genetic information, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, lawful alien status, national origin, age, marital status, and non-job related physical or mental disability, or protected veteran status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

89520276:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Work from anywhere, impact everywhere&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity is at the heart of who we are at Xapo Bank. &lt;br&gt;We’re a fully distributed team of over 160 Xapiens that work remotely from 50+ countries around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our beginning: A world that enjoys economic freedom and wealth protection,no matter where you live or who is running your country.&lt;br&gt;To achieve that, we search the world for the best people for the job. &lt;br&gt;We work hard, think globally, and inspire each other to learn and grow. &lt;br&gt;We are committed to changing the way things are done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;Although we are headquartered in Gibraltar, this is a full time, 100% remote position&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;Work from anywhere!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Position overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Treasury AVP at Xapo Bank, you will be a key member of our Treasury team, responsible for driving the Bank&#39;s Bitcoin first strategy along with focus on traditional finance, in particular across fixed income investment strategies that balance yield enhancement with prudent risk taking. Working closely with the Head of Treasury, you will bring a trading mindset to Treasury, structuring products across both traditional fixed income and Bitcoin, while leveraging strong Bitcoin and FX experience to support the Bank&#39;s investment and hedging activities. &lt;br&gt;If you are a commercially minded finance professional who thrives on designing creative, risk-aware solutions at the intersection of traditional finance and Bitcoin, we invite you to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed Income Investments: Manage and grow the Treasury&#39;s fixed income investment portfolio, including sourcing, evaluating, and executing investments to optimise returns within approved risk limits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Reward Balance: Assess and balance risk and reward across Treasury&#39;s investment and structuring activities, ensuring decisions are made within the Group&#39;s Risk Appetite and Financial Limits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Structuring: Structure investment and yield products for Treasury, working with internal stakeholders and counterparties to bring new structured solutions to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bitcoin Structured Products: Design and structure products referencing Bitcoin, including yield, hedging, and investment structures that align with the Bank&#39;s Bitcoin-first strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OTC Bitcoin &amp;amp; FX Execution: Execute and manage OTC Bitcoin trades and FX flows, maintaining strong counterparty relationships and ensuring best execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trading Support: Apply trading discipline and market experience to Treasury&#39;s day-to-day investment, hedging, and execution activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Management: Identify and mitigate investment-related risks, including credit, market, currency, and interest rate risk, in line with the Group&#39;s Risk Appetite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treasury Reporting: Contribute to Treasury Management Information, including investment performance, P&amp;amp;L, and risk reporting for senior committees such as the ALCO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Skills needed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CFA or CIMA or similar qualification preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in Fixed Income Investments, including sourcing, evaluating, and managing a fixed income portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience structuring products for Treasury, ideally including Bitcoin-referenced structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong OTC Bitcoin and FX trading/flow experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a Trading role, with a strong understanding of market execution and price discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of risk-reward trade-offs, with the ability to balance yield enhancement against the Group&#39;s Risk Appetite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative, commercially minded approach to designing new investment and yield-enhancing solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have Crypto experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial Expertise: Strong understanding of financial principles, investment management, and treasury operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical Skills: Excellent quantitative and analytical abilities to interpret financial data and make data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Management: Knowledge of investment and market-related risks and experience in developing risk mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Strong verbal and written communication skills to report and present financial information effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to Detail: A high level of attention to detail and accuracy in financial calculations and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Other requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dedicated workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reliable internet connection with the fastest speed possible in your area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with Our Values and the Xapo Values-Driven Leadership principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Why work for Xapo?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Impact Globally, Work Remotely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the Future&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improve lives through cutting-edge technology, work 100% remotely from anywhere in the world.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Great work-life balance&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;Build amazing things with a balance of autonomy and collaborative teamwork. Set your own work schedule and make use of a flexible PTO plan when you need to recharge.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expect Excellence&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt;Collaborate, learn, and grow with a high-performance team. Learn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 500;&quot;&gt; how you learn best - from books to conferences, you’ll get a yearly budget for your individual learning and development goals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Xapo, we prioritize consumer protection and adhere to regulatory requirements by ensuring that all Xapiens are accountable for upholding principles of fair treatment, transparency, and ethical conduct in their interactions with customers and stakeholders.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

89520599:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re making Africa the first cashless continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2017, over half the population in Sub-Saharan Africa had no bank account. That&#39;s for good reason—the fees are too high, the closest branch can be miles away, and nobody takes cards. Without access to financial institutions, people are forced to keep their savings under the mattress. Small business owners rely on lenders who charge extortionate rates. Parents spend hours waiting in line to pay school fees in cash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re solving this by building financial services that just work: no account fees, instantly available, and accepted everywhere. In places where electricity, water and roads don&#39;t always work, you can still send money with Wave. In 2017, we launched a mobile app in Senegal for cash deposit, withdrawal, and peer-to-peer and business payments. Now, we have millions of users across 9 countries and are growing fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to make Africa the first cashless continent and that&#39;s where you come in...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you&#39;ll help us achieve it&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you have a proven track record of defining and implementing marketing strategies that drive business growth? Are you a strategic thinker with a data-driven mindset and a passion for developing and executing marketing campaigns? If so, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Marketing Manager to oversee Above-the-Line (ATL) and Below-the-Line (BTL) activities, coordinate our marketing strategies and campaigns, and ensure they align with our overall business objectives and goals. You will play a key role in driving user growth and engagement through effective ATL and BTL marketing tactics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement ATL and BTL marketing strategies that align with Wave&#39;s growth objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, execute, and oversee all ATL activities (TV, radio, and print), and all BTL activities (events, promotions, and on-ground activations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams and stakeholders across the company to deliver impactful marketing campaigns that drive user acquisition and brand awareness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with external agencies and partners to ensure the successful execution of marketing activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze the performance of marketing campaigns, using data to make informed decisions and optimize strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular reports on the effectiveness of ATL and BTL activities, including insights and recommendations for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, build, and mentor a high-performing team to execute on key initiatives and achieve business goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The position is based in Niamey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must have work authorization in Niger.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a permanent position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our salaries are competitive and calculated using a transparent formula. We run performance reviews twice a year and award bonuses to strong performers who have been with the company for more than 6 months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer generous health insurance for yourself and your dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We support working parents - we offer parental leave policies (26 weeks for mothers and 4 weeks for fathers) and subsidized childcare when you return to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We help you live your fullest life now! We subsidize gym memberships and fitness classes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Airtime reimbursement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free food and a beautiful office space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or master&#39;s degree in business, marketing, communications, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of relevant work experience in marketing.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An all-rounded KPI-driven marketer having managed ATL and BTL campaigns and brand building events with proven commercial results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management skills, able to orchestrate different workstreams within sizeable complex campaigns under tight deadlines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical skills and ability to distill insights and make data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and interpersonal skills with a proven ability to work effectively across the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external agencies on both online and offline campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills accompanied by an engaging personality that can inspire, mentor, and develop a young team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in French, English, and one of the local languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are detail-oriented and highly organized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working in a marketing agency, telecom, payment service provider, FMCG, or financial institution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a curious and creative mind.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about marketing trends, consumer behavior, and brands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are able to work independently and as part of a team, with a proactive and results-oriented mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are adaptable and able to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We have a rapidly growing in-country team in Senegal, Côte d&#39;Ivoire, Mali, Burkina Faso, The Gambia, Uganda, Niger, Sierra Leone, and Cameroon plus remote team members spread across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We&#39;re deeply passionate about our mission of bringing radically affordable financial services to the people who need them most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We foster autonomy for our employees. You&#39;ll own your projects at every stage, from understanding the problem to monitoring your solution in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We raised the largest Series A in Africa in 2021. Our world-class investors, include Founders Fund, Sequoia Heritage, Stripe, Ribbit Capital, Y Combinator, and Partech Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We are on&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.ycombinator.com/topcompanies/revenue&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.ycombinator.com/topcompanies/revenue&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Y Combinator&#39;s top companies by revenue&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How to apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fill out the form below, and upload a resume in English and a&amp;nbsp;cover letter describing your interest in Wave and the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We review applications frequently and recommend that you apply to the role that most closely aligns with your skills, experience and career goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wave is an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

89520600:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re making Africa the first cashless continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2017, over half the population in Sub-Saharan Africa had no bank account. That&#39;s for good reason—the fees are too high, the closest branch can be miles away, and nobody takes cards. Without access to financial institutions, people are forced to keep their savings under the mattress. Small business owners rely on lenders who charge extortionate rates. Parents spend hours waiting in line to pay school fees in cash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re solving this by building financial services that just work: no account fees, instantly available, and accepted everywhere. In places where electricity, water and roads don&#39;t always work, you can still send money with Wave. In 2017, we launched a mobile app in Senegal for cash deposit, withdrawal, and peer-to-peer and business payments. Now, we have millions of users across 9 countries and are growing fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to make Africa the first cashless continent and that&#39;s where you come in...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you&#39;ll help us achieve it&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;As Wave continues to grow in Côte d’Ivoire, we’re looking for a Senior Marketing Manager who can turn a deep understanding of the market into meaningful action. You’ll be at the intersection of insight and influence: understanding what consumers, competitors, and the market are telling us, while building the partnerships and sponsorships that strengthen Wave’s presence and relevance in Côte d’Ivoire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Marketing, Côte d’Ivoire, this is an individual contributor role with ownership of two complementary pillars: Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Consumer Insights and Sponsoring &amp;amp; Brand Partnerships. You’ll bring analytical rigour, strategic thinking, and strong execution to both, using insights to guide where we invest and partnerships to make Wave matter in the moments that count.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Consumer Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the market intelligence agenda for Côte d&#39;Ivoire: design and manage local research initiatives — consumer surveys, usage and attitude studies, competitor tracking, and category analyses — working with external research agencies and vendors to produce insights that are actionable, not just informative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesise data from multiple sources (internal dashboards, market data, field findings, qualitative research) into clear, structured recommendations that help the team make sharper decisions about where and how Wave invests its marketing effort in CI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the team&#39;s go-to person on consumer behaviour and business dynamics in Côte d&#39;Ivoire: track trends, flag market shifts, and proactively surface insights that could shape our positioning, messaging, or activation choices — before someone asks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a working knowledge of our marketing performance data: comfortable navigating BI tools and dashboards, able to extract and analyse data independently, and translate numbers into narratives that inform strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief and manage research suppliers rigorously: write clear research briefs, evaluate methodologies, challenge findings where needed, and ensure the quality of outputs meets Wave&#39;s standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sponsoring &amp;amp; Brand Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute Wave&#39;s sponsoring strategy for Côte d&#39;Ivoire: identify the right properties (sports, culture, community, trade events), assess strategic fit against market intelligence, and lead negotiations and contract management end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximise the impact of every sponsorship: ensure each property delivers both above-the-line (ATL) visibility — broadcast, outdoor, media mentions — and meaningful below-the-line (BTL) activation on the ground, so Wave&#39;s presence is seen, felt, and remembered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a portfolio of brand partnerships aligned with Wave&#39;s positioning in CI, tracking performance and ROI with the same rigour applied to the intelligence pillar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hand-in-hand with global brand, growth, and in-country commercial teams to ensure sponsorships and partnerships are integrated into Wave&#39;s broader presence in the market — without duplicating remits.&lt;/li&gt;
