&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a product manager who wants to launch more real products in one year than most PMs ship in a career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What BitGo Labs is&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most corporate innovation labs are where ideas go to be studied. Decks get made. Pilots get piloted. Nothing ever meets a customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We built Labs to be the opposite of that. We push out real, live, revenue-generating products, and every one has to clear the same two-part bar:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A value proposition or economics only possible because of crypto.&lt;/strong&gt; If a normal company could build it on normal rails, it fails the test. We only build things where owning the infrastructure is the unfair advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Only buildable this fast because of AI.&lt;/strong&gt; Three months from blank page to live product. Not a prototype, not a beta behind a waitlist. Live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first product is already out in the world, built and launched inside ninety days. More are coming. Some will become businesses. Some will be shut down on schedule, without ceremony, because the numbers said so. Both outcomes are the system working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll sit at the center of the machine, working directly with BitGo&#39;s CEO and the Head of Labs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideas can come from anywhere, including you. Most will come from those two. Either way, an idea is just a thesis until someone turns it into a product real people use, and that someone is you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A cycle looks like this:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a thesis and find the product inside it. The first user, the wedge, the smallest version worth putting in the world. Push back hard if the thesis is wrong. You&#39;ll be doing this with the CEO in the room, so be the kind of person who gets sharper in that room, not quieter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship it in ninety days. Write the spec, run the build, make the tradeoffs, cut scope when the calendar says so. Pull BitGo&#39;s custody, stablecoin, and settlement rails into a consumer surface. Buy instead of build where it&#39;s faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the bar before launch. Real numbers, committed in advance, that decide the product&#39;s fate. No moving the goalposts after the fact.&lt;/li&gt;
