4702038006:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The world of digital assets is accelerating in speed, magnitude, and complexity, opening the door to new ways for leveraging the blockchain. Fireblocks’ platform and network provide the simplest and most secure way for companies to work with digital assets and it trusted by some of the largest financial institutions, banks, globally-recognized brands, and Web3 companies in the world, including BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Revolut, and thousands more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to Fireblocks, the industry-leading digital asset infrastructure technology company responsible for 15% of all crypto transactions!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s the bit about us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Fireblocks is an enterprise-grade platform delivering a secure infrastructure for moving, storing, and issuing digital assets &amp;amp; cryptocurrencies. At Fireblocks, we enable businesses to securely build, run and scale digital asset operations through the Fireblocks Network and MPC-based Wallet Infrastructure. Our next-generation multi-layer technology protects Digital assets from cyber-attacks, internal collusion, and human error. Fireblocks is the only platform that provides insurance for digital assets in storage, transfer, and E&amp;amp;O.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;As of January 2026, we serve over 2400 institutional customers, have secured the transfer of over $10 trillion in digital assets, and are the world&#39;s highest-valued digital asset infrastructure company, with over $1 billion raised.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our mission is simple: Enable every business to easily and securely support digital assets &amp;amp; cryptocurrencies. Come join us as we Secure. Simplify. Scale&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s the bit about the opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Fireblocks is seeking a highly motivated, and flexible legal professional to work collaboratively with the in-house legal team and our sales organisation. You will work closely with your legal colleagues to efficiently drive complex contract negotiations to closure. This will include project-managing the legal elements of significant revenue-generating opportunities, engaging relevant functional stakeholders and assisting with drafting the relevant contract documents. In this role, you will also help the legal team with its AI initiatives, template management, contract management tools, and the delivery of advice on various legal risks related to Fireblocks&#39; general operations and its range of offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;This role is based in London and reports directly to the Senior Legal Counsel, EMEA. The ideal candidate should be a self-starter and an efficient multi-tasker with an adaptable approach to problem-solving. You will work with business partners in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, driving meaningful impact. You should be comfortable working in a technical, software development environment alongside product, engineering, finance, sales and marketing professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focused on some of our largest commercial transactions supporting our SaaS services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking the lead in coordinating negotiations on a wide variety of contracts, including strategic license agreements and services agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with cross-functional teams to drive opportunities to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and refining processes to drive efficiencies between the legal and cross-functional teams throughout the deal cycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating templates and advising on implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving efficiencies through the effective use of AI tools..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning new technologies, products and practice areas without much precedence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Strong foundational knowledge of commercial contracting and legal concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Experience working at a technology company, preferably with a SaaS or software offering and/or at a top-tier law firm within a technology practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Background in financial services, fintech, blockchain, cybersecurity, or crypto industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified practising lawyer is not required for this role, though candidates ranging from trainee paralegals up to newly qualified lawyers will be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Experience as a team player who enjoys partnering with cross-functional teams to solve issues and work collaboratively to generate consensus across diverse points of view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Experience negotiating complex technology transactions on a global basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Fastidious attention to detail in both oral and written communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;A university degree is required or a GDL or JD, plus paralegal certification (CILEX, NALP, or ILSPA), is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;We&#39;d love for you to have financial services, fintech, blockchain, cybersecurity, or crypto industry experience, but we have a comprehensive onboarding and training program for all new employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

4701983006:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The world of digital assets is accelerating in speed, magnitude, and complexity, opening the door to new ways for leveraging the blockchain. Fireblocks’ platform and network provide the simplest and most secure way for companies to work with digital assets and it trusted by some of the largest financial institutions, banks, globally-recognized brands, and Web3 companies in the world, including BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Revolut, and thousands more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Fireblocks is the infrastructure powering the next era of digital finance -- banks, fintechs, and enterprises building on blockchain rails run on our platform. As we scale our revenue engine, we&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Talent Acquisition Partner&lt;/strong&gt; to own hiring for our GTM organization and help shape how we find, evaluate, and close the talent driving that growth.&amp;nbsp;This is a high-visibility, consultative seat. You&#39;ll run full-cycle recruiting end to end, but just as importantly, you&#39;ll be a trusted advisor to GTM leaders -- bringing market intelligence, and a sharp read on the competitive talent landscape to every conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting for GTM roles, from intake through offer and close, ensuring a thoughtful and high-quality candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve recruiting bottlenecks, proactively addressing challenges before they impact hiring velocity or quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Act as a talent advisor to Sales and Marketing leadership: real-time market mapping, competitive intel, and comp trends that keep our offers winning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Build a warm bench of top GTM talent ahead of need, so priority roles and territories never sit open waiting on a pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Push our recruiting process forward -- test new sourcing channels, tighten our funnel, and find scalable ways to improve speed and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Partner closely with Business Partners, People Ops, and hiring managers to keep the hiring process seamless and compliant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Spot bottlenecks before they cost you velocity or quality, and fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;4+ years of full-cycle recruiting in a fast-paced, high-growth environment; SaaS, fintech, or crypto strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;1+ years recruiting for GTM functions (Sales, Marketing, Sales Engineering)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;A track record of earning trust with senior stakeholders and influencing through data and judgment, not just process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Proven ability to source and close passive candidates in competitive markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Comfort using recruiting metrics to spot trends and sharpen strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Adaptability- priorities shift fast here, and you shift with them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Fluency with Greenhouse, LinkedIn Recruiter, and Claude/ AI Tools to move faster across sourcing, screening, and candidate communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;A genuine commitment to building diverse pipelines and inclusive hiring practices at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;In the NYC office 3x/week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For employees hired to work from New York, or from our NYC HQ, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to New York City and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs. It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is $110,000 - $150,000. The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a competitive equity grant, and generous benefits. While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

6134694004:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Galaxy Digital Inc. (Nasdaq: GLXY) is a global leader in digital assets and data center infrastructure, growing the economy that runs on code. Galaxy delivers the onchain infrastructure that connects institutions to digital assets, including trading, advisory, asset management, staking, self-custody, and tokenization. Galaxy also develops and operates data center infrastructure to power AI and HPC workloads. Anchored by its Helios campus in Texas, Galaxy is building a multi-gigawatt pipeline of more than 5.7 GW of potential capacity, positioning it among the largest and fastest-growing data center developers in North America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Company is headquartered in New York City, with offices across North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional information about Galaxy&#39;s businesses and products is available on &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.galaxy.com/&quot;&gt;www.galaxy.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Value:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a diverse team of free thinkers, and fast movers united to help investors and creators energize the global economy. We are looking for individuals&amp;nbsp;who&amp;nbsp;thrive in a culture of builders and overachievers&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;embrace high performance, transparent feedback, and a mission-first approach. Our culture shapes our way of working and gets us where we want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Seek Excellence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be Selective To Be Effective.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be Highly Aligned, Loosely Coupled.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Disagree Transparently.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Encourage Independent Decision-Making.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build Dream Teams.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Galaxy Digital is seeking a Site Development Associate to support data center development activities in and around Waco, Texas. This role is responsible for advancing sites through entitlement and permitting, building and maintaining relationships with municipal and county officials, negotiating with landowners, and coordinating with utilities — all in support of the company&#39;s data center development pipeline. This is a hands-on, field-facing role for someone who has been through at least one real estate development from land acquisition to entitlement and is excited to apply that experience to the data center industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support site entitlement efforts, including zoning, platting, land use approvals, and other local governmental approvals required to advance data center sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the company&#39;s primary point of contact with municipalities, counties, city councils, county commissioners, and other public officials on assigned projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain working relationships with mayors, city managers, county judges, and municipal/county staff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and deliver presentations to city councils, commissioners&#39; courts, planning and zoning boards, and other public bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, and help acquire permits required for site development, including building permits and entrance/access permits, and coordinate with public works and TxDOT/county road authorities as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with utility providers (power, water, wastewater, gas, telecom/fiber) to confirm capacity, service availability, and extension requirements for prospective sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support land acquisition efforts, including sourcing prospective sites, negotiating with landowners, and structuring purchase and option agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply working knowledge of Texas oil, gas, and mineral rights to identify and help resolve mineral, surface, and lease issues affecting site control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and help manage the basics of real estate contracts, title work, and the closing process, coordinating with legal counsel, title companies, and surveyors as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the basics of handling claims that may arise during due diligence, construction, or site development (e.g., title, boundary, or contractor-related claims), and know when and how to escalate them internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regularly and clearly with internal stakeholders — leadership, legal, engineering, and construction teams — on project status, risks, and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop working knowledge of data center development requirements (power, fiber, water, site criteria) and apply that knowledge to site selection and entitlement strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel within the Lubbock region and broader Texas market as needed to support site visits, public meetings, and landowner negotiations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in real estate development, with direct involvement in at least one completed development project from acquisition through entitlement (commercial or residential); OR equivalent experience as a landman.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience entitling property and working directly with municipalities, city councils, county commissioners, or other public officials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable and experienced presenting to public bodies, boards, and internal leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of Texas oil, gas, and mineral rights and how they can affect a real estate transaction or site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of real estate purchase contracts, title, and the closing process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating with landowners and/or sellers in a land acquisition context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to represent the company professionally to external officials and internal stakeholders alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and genuine interest in learning the fundamentals of data center development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license and ability to travel locally and regionally as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial real estate development experience strongly preferred over residential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience acquiring or coordinating utility, building, or entrance permits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with officials or staff in Waco and surrounding municipalities/counties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the basics of handling title, boundary, or construction-related claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in energy, land, or infrastructure-related real estate (landman, oil &amp;amp; gas land experience, utility right-of-way, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in Waco, Texas, with regular local travel and periodic travel elsewhere in Texas to support site visits, public meetings, and landowner negotiations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer (Remote):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary and discretionary bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Time Off (i.e. unlimited paid vacation days)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company paid Holidays (14)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company paid sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid health and protective benefits for employees, partners, and other dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3% 401(k) company contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free virtual coaching and counseling sessions through Ginger&lt;/li&gt;
